arrison.    Electronic Data: Our electronic data is stored in the following locations: Pre 2013 - On Ffynnon, SAC monitoring data is stored under the Monitoring folder for each SAC, e.g. Protected Sites - North Region - North West - Afon Gwyrfai a Llyn Cwellyn SAC ( SH55.11.100 ) – Monitoring Within each monitoring folder there will be a folder for each monitoring cycle of each feature, e.g. for the Gwyrfai there are folders for “Luronium natans 99 to 06”, “Luronium natans 07 to 12”, “Lutra lutra 99 to 06”, “Lutra Lutra 07 to 12”, etc.  There will also be a folder called “SAC Monitoring reports” which should contain the final SAC monitoring reports for each feature.  Post 2013 where projects were started once the DMS had been set up. This folder system is recreated on DMS for monitoring undertaken in the last 18 months or so.  It is all stored under the Land Management part of DMS: https://cyfoethnaturiolcymru.sharepoint.com/teams/landman/SitePages/Home.aspx\tInternal Custodians: North Region: Tom Harrison, Environmental Assessment Officer, NE EAAT. South Region: Karen Wilkinson, Environmental Assessment Officer, SE EAAT South Region: Dan Guest, Senior Environmental Assessment Officer, SW EAAT South Region: Alex Harding, Team Leader, SW EAAT Used to be: David Allen, Environmental Monitoring Manager, CCW  Metadata Contact: Data Services Team, NRW\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)\t\t1999-01-01\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-07-08T08:46:54.000Z\tnobody nobody\t-\tPublic record\n17782\tNRW_DS110510\t2024-05-28T12:31:29.138Z\t978\tUnassessed\tEditable\tCondition Monitoring of Sites of Special Scientific Interest (SSSIs) in Wales\t\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313130353130\tHigh level data are held centrally by CCW Environmental Change Group.  Supporting data are held in Regional CCW offices or by Science Groups.  Published reports are available from CCWs libraries.\tInternal Custodian: Dylan Lloyd, Specialist Advisor - Monitoring Strategy \u0026amp; Planning, Monitoring Strategy \u0026amp; Planning Team  (Formerly: David Allen, Team Leader, Monitoring, Strategy and Planning, Monitoring \u0026amp; Surveillance Team, NRW)\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)\t\t2015-12-31\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-04-17T10:01:45.000Z\tnobody nobody\t-\tPublic record\n17790\tNRW_DS110511\t2024-05-28T12:31:29.357Z\t4\tUnassessed\tEditable\tMonitoring and Surveillance of Sites of Special Scientific Interest (SSSIs) in Wales\t\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313130353131\t\tInternal Custodian: Dylan Lloyd, Specialist Advisor - Monitoring Strategy \u0026amp; Planning, Monitoring Strategy \u0026amp; Planning Team\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)\t\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T10:45:10.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPrivate record\n17785\tNRW_DS110512\t2024-05-28T12:31:29.231Z\t509\tUnassessed\tEditable\tMonitoring and Surveillance of National Nature Reserves (NNRs) in Wales\t\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313130353132\tIndividual NRW NNR warden offices. Data is fed into Countryside Monitoring System (CMS)  which is held on an external server accessed through a network connection. Contact Tom Hellewell about this.   The reserve staff and wardens hold a lot of the data - and also use a lot of the SAC and SSSI monitoring data to inform their site management plans.  September 2021 update - We still ask the NNR managers to update the data in CMSi. This was last done in November 2019. In the past we’ve tried to get it updated every 2 or 3 years – but looking to extend this to every 5 or 6 years as things really weren’t changing much. CMSi is good for at least another 2 years. There are plans to migrate the data to another system and the provisional plan was to do some development work on AMX to allow for this. However, this didn’t make the cut for this years IT development and no guarantee it will for next year either. Also not sure how this is affected by the AMX monitoring module – which I understand has been put on hold.\tInternal Custodian: Thomas Hellawell, Lead Specialist Adv