e 3 2013 – 2018.\t\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313136383230\tOriginal data is stored in KiECO / WISKI with the exception of the shad data Analysis (when completed)  for each bullhead SAC river is held in a separate spreadsheet on DMS.  Wye: SAMP-753-344\tData Custodian(s): Emma Keenan, Environmental Monitoring Officer Fisheries  Metadata Point of Contact:  Heather Garrett, Freshwater Monitoring Coordinator\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)\t\t2016-12-31\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-03-07T15:12:33.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n18359\tNRW_DS116821\t2024-05-28T12:47:20.613Z\t3\tUnassessed\tEditable\tMarine and Coastal Recreation Audit 2009\t\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313136383231\tX:\\Recreation and Access\\MCRA H:\\Science\\Knowledge Management\\MFSG Data archive\\Media1501to1600\\Media1552 Archived as project 475, media 1552.\tData: Kirsty Lindenbaum, Marine Resource Management Advisor or  Mary Lewis, Marine Strategic Plan Energy and Advice Team Leader Metadata point of contact: Monica Jones.  Original data i.e.  Natural Facilities database - contact is Sue Williams, Coastal Access Database is within Jont Bullbeck\u0027s team, Richard Deering is relevant contact, although database no longer exists other than what is available as GIS layers       The datasets have not gone through the Open Data Process and therefore should possible not be classed as open data as yet.  However it is unlikely  that there are any restriction.  The Coastal Access database does not appear to have used an OS admin boundary dataset as the background as it is too generalised for high water.\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)\t\t2017-10-12\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-03-07T16:50:59.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPrivate record\n18361\tNRW_DS116826\t2024-05-28T12:47:20.699Z\t1631\tValid\tEditable\tHistoric LIDAR Archive\tArchif catalog teils LiDAR CNC\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313136383236\tx:\\Basemapping\\LiDAR\\Historic LiDAR\tBen Anscombe / Louise Harris (Spatial services team)