ed\tEditable\tWorking with Natural Processes (WWNP) in Wales: Natural Processes Woodlands\t\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231353536\tX:\\Flood Risk\\Working with Natural Processes\\Natural Processes woodland.lyr\tVictoria Greest, Advisor, Flood Risk Strategy\t\t\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T10:38:35.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPrivate record\n18487\tNRW_DS121564\t2024-05-28T12:50:13.658Z\t293\tUnassessed\tEditable\tFlood mitigation woodland opportunities for Dyfi, Rhonndda and Tawe Area Trails\t\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231353634\tX:\\Resource Management\\Flood Mitigation Woodland Opportunities\\Dyfi Catchment.lyr  X:\\Resource Management\\Flood Mitigation Woodland Opportunities\\Rhondda Catchment.lyr  X:\\Resource Management\\Flood Mitigation Woodland Opportunities\\Tawe Catchment.lyr\tInternal Custodian: Patrick Green (patrick.green@cyfoethnaturiolcymru.gov.uk)  Metadata point of contact: GIS and Spatial Data Team  This dataset was done under contract and the external contractor was Forest Research: Huw Thomas huw.thomas1@forestry.gsi.gov.uk       Information from Huw Thomas from Forest Research the contractors of this dataset:  I’ve made some enquires and the only dataset which may present a problem would be the NSRI soils data and any dataset we created using the NSRI soil data so anything which selected areas on HOST class for example. In this case, Maps 16 to18. FR and FC are permitted to make use of any soil and soil derived data to meet the objectives of our agency so we can make the data visible via online map browsers and supply printed images but we cannot share the data unless the recipients have the same licence with the NSRI as we do (which the Environment Agency has). If NRW has the same licence agreements as the EA that will be fine also. 3rd parties can not have the spatial data unless they have a licence with NSRI or pay NSRI for the use of your data. However they can view the data.\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)\t\t2014-06-01\tpublication\tnu