-\tPublic record\n17387\tNRW_DS24327\t2024-05-28T12:21:23.200Z\t790\tUnassessed\tEditable\tWelsh Sand Dune Data\tSet data twyni tywod Cymru\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-3234333237\tThe site reports are available from NRW\u0027s library.   Biological Data held in Recorder 6 Sand Dune Survey Wales CCW0007600000001  Spreadsheets were stored on the personal drive of NRW\u0027s Coastal Ecologist (Peter Rhind, retired). There is a data set here:- Z:\\Archive\\Legacy\\CCW_H_DRIVE\\Science\\TSG\\USERS\\RhindP\\Dune Spreadsheets.  According to Julie Creer this appears to be  \u0027Peter Rhind\u0027s own interrogation of the Phase 2 sand dune survey data (both the UK and Wales), which I suspect he got from the paper versions of survey. Looking at a few of the spreadsheets it looks like he separated out the different sand dune NVC communities and then tabulated which sites had those NVC communities and then added in the quadrat data tables for each site of that NVC type. S, in short, this is his analysis of that data and not the original dataset per se. These are most useful to me, but I’m not sure useful to anyone else?\u0027\tInternal Custodian: Julie Creer, Lead Specialist Advisor – Coastal Habitats, Marine \u0026amp; Coastal Ecosystems Team Metadata Contact: Data Services Team, NRW\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)\t\t1995-12-31\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2026-03-03T12:00:53.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\tMEDIN\tPublic record\n17381\tNRW_DS24328\t2024-05-28T12:21:23.086Z\t1365\tValid\tEditable\tPembrokeshire Marine Species Atlas (PMSA)\tAtlas o Rywogaethau Morol Sir Benfro (PMSA)\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-3234333238\tData is archived under project no. 109 and 156, and media no. 382 and 394. Species Data is held in Marine Recorder.  This data is now available on the NBN Atlas  Some of the paper MNCR forms are held in off-site storage (Box CCW/MNCR/1, Box CCW/MNCR/2, Box CCW/MNCR/3)\tMonica Jones, Data Services Team Leader, EPP, NRW\tVarious including volunteer recorders-Natural Resou