            "type": "TABLE",
            "data": "Database ID\tNRW File identifier\tcreatedate\tpopularity\tValidation Status\tEdit Status\tTitle\tUse Constraints TEXT\tResource Identifier\tNRW Internal Location\tNRW Internal Custodian\tAbstractEN\tOwner organisation\tdate\tdatetype\tWMS\turl\tDate Last Edited\tLast Editor Name\tGroups Available in (GEMINI / MEDIN)\tRecord in Public view\n17067\tEXT_DS100183\t2024-05-28T12:10:10.480Z\t12\tUnassessed\tEditable\tWelsh Government: Land Parcel Identification System (LPIS) Crop Codes (3rd Party Data)\t© Crown Copyright: Welsh Government 2006 This dataset is owned by the Welsh Government, and licensed to NRW for internal use only. NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313030313833\tLegacy CCW Archive M:\\GIS_Data\\live\\Land_management\\agrienvironment\\WAG_DEPC\\lpis\\crop_codes_all.TAB\tGIS and Spatial Data Team\tThis is a spatial dataset containing the crop code to cross reference against field boundaries for the Land Parcel Identification System (LPIS).  It is an external third party dataset owned by the Welsh Government and licensed to Natural Resources Wales (NRW) for internal use only.\tWelsh Government\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-03-07T15:59:13.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPrivate record\n17069\tEXT_DS100191\t2024-05-28T12:10:10.646Z\t2622\tUnassessed\tEditable\tWelsh Government: Land Parcel Identification System (LPIS) Farm and Field Boundaries (3rd Party Data)\t© Crown Copyright: Welsh Government 2006 This dataset is owned by the Welsh Government, and licensed to NRW for internal use only. If a NRW Contractor requires any of the LPIS layers please contact the Data Services team who will contact Welsh Government to request permission. NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly. Attribution Statement: © Crown copyright: Welsh Government\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313030313931\tx:\\Resource Management\\Welsh Government\\LPIS Farm and field boundary join unredacted.lyr  x:\\Resource Management\\Welsh Government\\LPIS Farm Boundaries.lyr  x:\\Resource Management\\Welsh Government\\LPIS Field Boundaries Redacted.lyr  x:\\Resource Management\\Welsh Government\\LPIS Field Boundaries Unredacted.lyr  Legacy CCW Archive M:\\gis_data\\live\\land_management\\agrienvironment\\wag_depc\\lpis\\lpis_farm_bdy.tab\tGIS Service Desk\tThis is a spatial dataset containing the extent and location of farm boundaries for the Land Parcel Identification System (LPIS). It is an external third party dataset owned by the Welsh Government and licensed to Natural Resources Wales (NRW) for internal use only.   This dataset includes Land Parcel Identification System (LPIS) Field and Agricultural/Crop Information. The dataset has been supplied by the Welsh Government and contains Whole Farm and Field Boundaries, Customer Details with the appropriate Reference Number (CRN) and Crop Information for each Field Boundaries.\tWelsh Government\t2026-01-20\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2026-01-26T10:04:06.000Z\tMonica Jones\t-\tPublic record\n17066\tEXT_DS100682\t2024-05-28T12:10:10.173Z\t415\tUnassessed\tEditable\tEnvironment Agency (EA): Local Environment Agency Plans (LEAPs) boundaries (3rd Party Data)\t© Environment Agency Wales 2003. NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313030363832\tLegacy CCW Archive M:\\gis_data\\live\\physical\\hydrology\\environment_agency\\agency_infrastructure\\leaps_250k.tab\tGIS Service Desk\tThis is a GIS dataset containing spatial objects such as points, lines, and polygons.  It is an external third party dataset owned by the Environment Agency Wales and licensed to former Countryside Council for Wales (CCW) for internal use only.  The dataset has been supplied by the Environment Agency Wales and contains Local Environment Agency Plans. LEAP\u0027s are areas for which the Agency draws up specific action plans. For further information please contact your local Environment Agency Office.\tEnvironment Agency Wales (EA Wales)\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-03-21T10:38:23.000Z\tnobody nobody\t-\tPublic record\n17072\tEXT_DS100758\t2024-05-28T12:10:10.871Z\t1101\tUnassessed\tEditable\tWelsh Government: Less Favoured Areas (LFA) (3rd Party Data)\t© Crown Copyright: Welsh Government NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly. Attribution Statement: © Crown Copyright: Welsh Government.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313030373538\tx:\\Resource Management\\Welsh Government\\Less Favoured Areas.lyr\tGIS Service Desk\tThis is a GIS dataset owned by the Welsh Government and licensed to Natural Resources Wales (NRW) for internal use only.  In recognition of the different physical and socio-economic characteristics across the regions, the European Union introduced the Less Favoured Area (LFA) designation to support farming where production conditions are difficult. The criteria for LFA designation were first established in European legislation in 1975 (Directive 75/268 EEC and accompanying measures).\tWelsh Government\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-07-08T08:21:14.000Z\tnobody nobody\t-\tPublic record\n17065\tEXT_DS100762\t2024-05-28T12:10:10.029Z\t1128\tUnassessed\tEditable\tNational Trust: Ownership (3rd Party Data)\t© National Trust 2004 NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313030373632\tX:\\Ownership\\National Trust\\National Trust Ownership.lyr   Legacy CCW Archive M:\\gis_data\\live\\land_management\\external_agency\\national_trust\\nt_ownership_wales.tab\tGIS Service Desk\tThis is a spatial dataset that has been supplied by the National Trust and contains digital boundaries of the National Trust land ownership within Wales. Natural Resources Wales has access to this is data through an agreed National Trust Licence Agreement which states we can use this data for internal business use only.\tNational Trust\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T12:00:17.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17062\tEXT_DS100787\t2024-05-28T12:10:09.882Z\t764\tUnassessed\tEditable\tRSPB: Lapwings (3rd Party Data)\t© RSPB 2006                                                                    NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313030373837\tx:\\Biological\\Species sourced by NRW\\Terrestrial\\Birds\\Lapwings.lyr    Legacy CCW Archive M:\\gis_data\\live\\biological\\species\\all_wales\\rspb\\lapwings.TAB\tGIS and Spatial Data Team\tThis is a GIS dataset containing spatial objects such as points, lines, and polygons.  It is an external third party dataset owned by the Royal Society for the Protection of Birds and licensed to NRW for internal use only. The dataset has been supplied by the RSPB and contains Lapwing sites for Wales-showing status of birds sited. Supplied and updated by Tony Pickup ( RSPB ).\tRoyal Society for the Protection of Birds (RSPB)\t2015-11-18\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-03-07T17:31:44.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17064\tEXT_DS100789\t2024-05-28T12:10:09.814Z\t1482\tUnassessed\tEditable\tCadw: Scheduled Ancient Monument (SAM) (3rd Party Data)\t© Cadw Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and Cadw\u0027s copyright. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose. Attribution Statement: Designated Historic Asset GIS Data, The Welsh Historic Environment Service (Cadw), 2018, licensed under the Open Government Licence http://www.nationalarchives.gov.uk/doc/open-government-licence/version/3/\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313030373839\tX:\\Designations\\CADW\\Scheduled Ancient Monuments.lyr\tGIS Service Desk  External Contact: Records Officer at CADW\tNatural Resources of Wales (NRW) are supplied a number of historic and cultural datasets under a licence from Cadw. Cadw is the Welsh Government\u0027s historic environment service working for an accessible and well-protected historic environment for Wales. They were set up with the aim of conserving Wales\u0027s heritage, helping people understand and care about their history and helping to sustain the distinctive character of Wales.  This is a spatial dataset containing basic information concerning Scheduled Ancient Monuments (SAM) that lie within the boundaries of Wales. The data has been provided as a guide to the SAMs. Areas have been interpreted from paper maps taken from original legal documents and therefore remain indicative only. Archaeological sites of national importance are given legal protection by being placed on a \u0027Schedule\u0027 of monuments. Under the Ancient Monuments and Archaeological Areas Act 1979, the Welsh Ministers are required to compile and maintain this schedule.\tCadw. Welsh Historic Monuments\t2019-05-17\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-03-07T16:47:23.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17061\tEXT_DS100802\t2024-05-28T12:10:09.723Z\t791\tUnassessed\tEditable\tOS Open Data: Watsonian Vice County Boundaries (3rd Party Data)\t© OS NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly. Attribution Statement: Contains OS data © Crown copyright and database right (2018).\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313030383032\tX:\\Basemapping\\Admin Boundaries\\Watsonian Vice County Boundaries.lyr   Legacy CCW Archive M:\\gis_data\\live\\political\\boundaries\\vice_counties\\watsonian_vcb_polygon.tab\tGIS Service Desk\tThis is a spatial dataset containing the boundaries of the  Watsonian Vice Counties across Wales. This is a 3rd Party dataset supplied to Natural Resources Wales (NRW) under an OS Open Data Licence.\tOrdnance Survey (OS)\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-03-07T15:52:26.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17060\tEXT_DS100803\t2024-05-28T12:10:09.626Z\t2\tUnassessed\tEditable\tWelsh Government: Local Authorities in Wales - Village Greens (3rd Party Data)\t© Crown Copyright: Welsh Government NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly. Attribution Statement: © Crown copyright: Welsh Government. Ordnance Survey 100021874\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313030383033\tX:\\Designations\\Local Authorities\\Village Greens area.lyr  X:\\Designations\\Local Authorities\\Village Greens line.lyr    Legacy CCW Archive M:\\gis_data\\live\\access\\commons\\village_greens\\vilage_greens.TAB\tGIS Service Desk\tThis is a GIS dataset owned by the Local Authorities in Wales, and has been supplied by Welsh Government. It contains the location of village greens from across Wales.\tWelsh Government\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-03-07T16:51:08.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPrivate record\n17063\tEXT_DS100804\t2024-05-28T12:10:09.873Z\t0\tUnassessed\tEditable\tEnvironment Agency (EA): Licenced Water Abstraction - Water Resources Abstraction Areas (3rd Party Data)\t© Environment Agency Wales 2004 This dataset is owned by the Environment Agency Wales, and licensed to NRW for internal use only. Please contact the Environment Agency Wales before using the dataset for any other purpose\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313030383034\tX:\\Licensing and Permitting\\Water Abstractions \u0026amp; Discharges\\NALD Licence Abstraction Areas.lyr\t\tThis is a GIS dataset containing spatial objects such as polygons showing Licenced Water Abstraction data information.  This will not updated. Legacy dataset for licences for water abstraction and discharges.\tEnvironment Agency Wales (EA Wales)\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T11:49:26.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPrivate record\n17058\tEXT_DS100843\t2024-05-28T12:10:09.639Z\t934\tUnassessed\tEditable\tWoodland Trust: Sites (3rd Party Data)\t© Woodland Trust 2006. NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly. Attribution Statement: © Woodland Trust. Derived product © Contains Ordnance Survey data.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313030383433\tx:\\Ownership\\Woodland Trust\\Woodland Trust Sites.lyr\tGIS Service Desk External Contact: The Woodland Trust GIS Department\tThis is a GIS dataset of all Woodland Trust property boundaries. It is an external third party dataset supplied and owned by the Woodland Trust and licensed to Natural Resources Wales (NRW) for internal use only.\tWoodland Trust\t2020-04-30\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T11:49:28.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17059\tEXT_DS102087\t2024-05-28T12:10:09.638Z\t1515\tUnassessed\tEditable\tRSPB: Important Bird Areas (3rd Party Data)\t© RSPB 2006                                                                    NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly. Attribution Statement: Data reproduced with the permission of RSPB.   © Crown Copyright. Ordnance Survey licence number 100021787 (2018)\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313032303837\tX:\\Designations\\RSPB\\RSPB Important Bird Areas.lyr  x:\\Recreation and Access\\MCRA\\RSPB important bird areas coastal 2009.lyr   Legacy CCW Archive M:\\gis_data\\live\\biological\\species\\all_wales\\rspb\\important_bird_areas.TAB\tGIS Service Desk\tThis is a GIS dataset containing spatial boundaries of Important Bird Areas (IBAs) in Wales. IBAs are a world-wide network of areas, identified using internationally agreed set of criteria, highlighting defined areas an being important globally for the conservation of bird populations. Important Bird and Biodiversity Areas (IBAs) are: - Places of international significance for the conservation of birds and other biodiversity - Recognised world-wide as practical tools for conservation - Distinct areas amenable to practical conservation action - Identified using robust, standardised criteria - Sites that together form part of a wider integrated approach to the conservation and sustainable use of the natural environment. This is an external third party dataset owned in the UK by the Royal Society for the Protection of Birds (RSPB) and licensed to NRW for internal use only.\tRoyal Society for the Protection of Birds (RSPB)\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T11:49:52.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17057\tEXT_DS102091\t2024-05-28T12:10:09.483Z\t754\tUnassessed\tEditable\tRSPB: Reserves (3rd Party Data)\t© RSPB 2006                                                                    NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly. Attribution Statement:  Data reproduced with the permission of RSPB.   © Crown Copyright. Ordnance Survey licence number 100021787 (2018)\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313032303931\tX:\\Designations\\RSPB\\RSPB Reserves.lyr   Legacy CCW Archive M:\\gis_data\\live\\land_management\\external_agency\\rspb_reserves\\rspb_reserves.TAB\tGIS Service Desk\tThis is a GIS dataset containing the spatial boundaries of  Royal Society for the Protection of Birds reserves across the UK. This is an external third party dataset owned by RSPB and licensed to NRW for internal use only.  The RSPB Reserve Boundaries dataset contains the boundaries of all land managed, leased or owned as part of RSPB reserves.  Areas for which other rights are held or which are not classed as RSPB reserves are excluded (for exceptions please see individual site records).  Some reserves are only represented by an indicative boundary due to confidentiality issues surrounding the definitive boundary.\tRoyal Society for the Protection of Birds (RSPB)\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-03-07T16:46:48.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17056\tEXT_DS102211\t2024-05-28T12:10:09.326Z\t932\tUnassessed\tEditable\tCadw: Register of Historic Landscapes (3rd Party Data)\t© Cadw © Crown copyright Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and copyright of the owners.  It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose. Attribution Statement: Designated Historic Asset GIS Data, The Welsh Historic Environment Service (Cadw), 2018, licensed under the Open Government Licence http://www.nationalarchives.gov.uk/doc/open-government-licence/version/3/\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313032323131\tx:\\Designations\\CADW\\Register of Historic Landscapes.lyr\tGIS Service Desk\tNatural Resources of Wales (NRW) are supplied a number of historic and cultural datasets under a licence from Cadw. Cadw is the Welsh Government\u0027s historic environment service working for an accessible and well-protected historic environment for Wales. They were set up with the aim of conserving Wales\u0027s heritage, helping people understand and care about their history and helping to sustain the distinctive character of Wales.   The Register of Historic Landscapes were digitised from the original hardcopy depictions taken from Registers that were created in 1998 and 2001. They are used in the production and evaluation of EIA\u0027s and as an integrated information resource for local authorities\u0027 structure and development plans on the coast and for the consideration of planning applications.\tCadw. Welsh Historic Monuments\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T12:36:08.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17092\tEXT_DS108556\t2024-05-28T12:10:55.294Z\t679\tUnassessed\tEditable\tNational Trust Coastal Risk Assessment Database - Welsh Subset Only (3rd Party Data)\t© National Trust 2008. NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313038353536\tWelsh Subset of the data, and the report are held on the MFSG shared drive (File path: Z:\\Archive\\Legacy\\CCW_H_DRIVE\\Science\\MFSG\\Estuarine \u0026amp; Coastal Science\\NT_Coastal Risk Ass_Oct04   For full database please contact the National Trust.\tGIS Service Desk  Internal Custodian – Nicola Rimington, Lead Specialist Advisor, Marine and Coastal Physical Processes and Coastal Management, Marine and Coastal Policy \u0026amp; Planning Team External Custodian: Coast and Marine Support, The National Trust. (also contact: Adrian Woodhall adrianwoodhall@btinternet.com)\tNational Trust database detailing information including: Designations, Habitat and Species features, Geomorphology, Wrecks, Historical Landscapes and Features, Flood Data, Visitors, Access, Income etc. The purpose of this abstraction was to identify National Trust properties at risk from flooding due to future climate change and global warming.  The database was also collated to identify assests associated with the properties that may be at risk and to identify actions that may be taken to prevent flood damage to properties or their assets. The Welsh subset of data contains information about approximately 40 sites for the former Countryside Council for Wales (CCW) West Region and 30 for CCW North Region. Data was collected between August 2006 and May 2008 and will be updated as and when necessary. A high level of confidence in the source data  provided.  Ground-truthing of properties was carried out by the National Trust.\tNational Trust\t2008-05-31\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-03-07T15:52:06.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17099\tEXT_DS110030\t2024-05-28T12:10:55.552Z\t4\tUnassessed\tEditable\tEnvironment Agency (EA): Catalogue of Light Detection and Ranging (LIDAR) Coverage (3rd Party Data)\t© The Environment Agency NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313130303330\t\tGIS and Spatial Data Team, NRW\tLight Detection and Ranging (LIDAR) is an airborne mapping technique. The Environment Agency\u0027s LIDAR data archive contains digital elevation data derived from surveys carried out by the Environment Agency and represents over 10 years of survey work carried out by a specialist remote sensing team based in Bath and Coventry. Depending on the area, data is available at 25cm, 50cm, 1m and 2m resolution which can be supplied as a Digital Surface Model (includes heights of objects, such as vehicles, buildings and vegetation as well as terrain surfaces) and a Digital Terrain Model (a \\bare earth model\\\" with surface objects filtered out of the DSM by applying bespoke software techniques). The purpose of this data capture was to produce accurate elevation data and highly detailed digital surface and terrain models.\"\tEnvironment Agency (EA)\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T12:00:11.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPrivate record\n17094\tEXT_DS110041\t2024-05-28T12:10:55.429Z\t586\tUnassessed\tEditable\tSeasearch Marine Surveys in Wales 1995 onwards (3rd Party Data)\t© Marine Conservation Society 2013. NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313130303431\tNB - More recent data is available via the NRW All Wales snapshot for Marine Recorder.  Archived as Project 22, Media 135 (File path: K\\Archive\\Media 101to200\\Media 135) SeaSearch snapshot data is merged with NRW\u0027s and available to view through the Marine Wizard.   Related titles above for Seasearch reports available in NRW libraries.\tGIS Service Desk Internal Custodian: Kirsten Ramsay, Team Leader, Marine \u0026amp; Coastal Ecosystems Team External Contacts: - Seasearch National Coordinator. chris@seasearch.org.uk. Marine Conservation Society, Unit 3 Wolf Business Park, Alton Road, Ross on Wye, Herefordshire, HR95NB - Liz Morris, North Wales Local Seasearch Organiser. liz@marine-ecosol.com - Kate Lock, West and South Wales Local Seasearch Organiser. rumbalock@tiscali.co.uk\tSeasearch is a national project for volunteer sports divers who have an interest in what they\u0027re seeing under water, want to learn more and want to help protect the marine environment around the coasts of Britain and Ireland. This dataset contains the results of a number of Seasearch surveys carried out around the coast of Wales from 1995.  A snapshot of the SeaSearch data is merged with the NRW Marine Recorder snapshot. The main aim is to map out the various types of sea bed found in the near-shore zone. The data collected is also used to fill gaps in our knowledge about what lives where, what affect human activities are having on marine life and to help advise government and policy makers on actions needed to protect the marine wildlife and habitats e.g. by identifying sites where better protection may be needed.\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)\t2013-04-08\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T11:13:58.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17097\tEXT_DS110043\t2024-05-28T12:10:55.525Z\t531\tUnassessed\tEditable\tMarine Mammal and Marine Turtle Strandings (Welsh Coast) (3rd Party Data)\t© Marine Environmental Monitoring 2007.  NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313130303433\tArchived as Project 168 (media 497, 498, 499), project 171 (Media 501)\tGIS Service Desk  Marine Vertebrate Ecologist, NRW\tThis dataset contains information on marine mammal and turtle strandings along the Welsh coast. As contributors to the project, former Countryside Council for Wales (CCW) now part of Natural Resources Wales (NRW) hold a copy of the data up to 2006. The project is run by the Marine Environment Monitoring group and originally received sponsorship from DEFRA, Natural History Museum and funding from Special Areas of Conservation (SAC\u0027s). However the projects funding was cut. The purpose of this data capture was to obtain information on disease and cause of death within marine mammal and turtle populations along the Welsh Coastline.\tMarine Environmental Monitoring\t2007-02-28\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-03-07T16:58:48.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17101\tEXT_DS111151\t2024-05-28T12:10:55.518Z\t763\tUnassessed\tEditable\tLittoral Hard Substrata of the Menai Strait (3rd Party Data)\t© JNCC NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313131313531\tThe survey data has been entered into JNCC\u0027s copy of Marine Recorder (JNCCMNCR10000129)\tGIS Service Desk\tThis survey was undertaken as part of a general study of the Menai Strait, commissioned by JNCC, required to assist in decisions related to its designation as one of Britain\u0027s Marine Nature Reserves. Parallel surveys of the soft substrata and sublittoral hard substrata have also been conducted. The dataset includes detailed descriptions of the flora and fauna found on the littoral hard substrate of the Menai Strait, detailed site descriptions (including geological and topographical information and notes on special interest, access and pressures) and flora and faunal lists covering all substrata in the straits. The purpose of this data capture was to provide a topographical and biological description of the Anglesey and Arfon sides of the Menai Strait, concentrating on the hard or, more particularly, stable substrata and the animals and plants which live in these habitats.\tJoint Nature Conservancy Committee (JNCC)\t1983-08-31\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-03-07T16:58:55.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17105\tEXT_DS111486\t2024-05-28T12:10:55.651Z\t1057\tUnassessed\tEditable\tLocal Environmental Records Centre (LERC) Wales: Welsh Protected and Priority Species (PPS) Collation (3rd Party Data)\t© Cofnod, WWBIC, BIS, SEWBReC NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originators directly. For NRW internal use only.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313131343836\tX:\\Biological\\Local Record Centers\\LRC priority and protected species points.lyr  X:\\Biological\\Local Record Centers\\LRC priority and protected species regions.lyr  x:\\Biological\\Local Record Centers\\LRC PPS all bats points.lyr  x:\\Biological\\Local Record Centers\\LRC PPS all bats regions.lyr  x:\\Biological\\Local Record Centers\\LRC PPS All WCA points.lyr  x:\\Biological\\Local Record Centers\\LRC PPS Badgers points.lyr  x:\\Biological\\Local Record Centers\\LRC PPS Common Toad.lyr  x:\\Biological\\Local Record Centers\\LRC PPS Dormice points.lyr  x:\\Biological\\Local Record Centers\\LRC PPS EPS points.lyr  x:\\Biological\\Local Record Centers\\LRC PPS Great Crested Newt points.lyr  x:\\Biological\\Local Record Centers\\LRC PPS Marsh Fritilary points.lyr  x:\\Biological\\Local Record Centers\\LRC PPS Otter points.lyr  x:\\Biological\\Local Record Centers\\LRC PPS Red Squirrel points.lyr  x:\\Biological\\Local Record Centers\\LRC PPS Section 42 points.lyr  x:\\Biological\\Local Record Centers\\LRC PPS Water Vole points.lyr  x:\\Biological\\Local Record Centers\\LRC PPS WCA Sch1 Birds points.lyr  x:\\Biological\\Local Record Centers\\LRC PPS WCA Sch5 Animals points.lyr  x:\\Biological\\Local Record Centers\\LRC PPS WCA Sch8 Plants points.lyr\tInternal Custodian: GIS Service Desk Internal Custodian: Barnaby Letheren, Lead Specialist Advisor, Knowledge \u0026amp; Information Management\tThe data are collated from species datasets held by the Welsh Local Environmental Records Centres. Species are selected to form part of this dataset if they have international/national protection or national priority status (UKBAP or Section 42 of the NERC Act). The purpose of this data capture was to inform conservation management and decisions.   Data being recieved from LERC\u0027s does vary between centre. North Wales Environmental Information Centre (COFNOD) data only contains data that has been verified by trusted sources and specialists in the field.  South East Wales Biodiversity Records Centre (SEWBReC), West Wales Biodiversity Information Centre (WWBIC) and Biodiversity Information Service for Powys and Brecon Beacons National Park (BIS) data contains all protected and priority records including records that have been unverified.\tWWBIC (West Wales Biodiversity Information Centre)-SEWBReC (South East Wales Biodiversity Records Centre)-Cofnod (North Wales Environmental Information Service)-BIS (Biodiversity Information Service for Powys and Brecon Beacons National Park)\t2026-02-02\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2026-02-02T14:09:52.000Z\tMichael Goodrich\t-\tPublic record\n17100\tEXT_DS111947\t2024-05-28T12:10:55.522Z\t565\tUnassessed\tEditable\tCadw: Historic Parks and Gardens (3rd Party Data)\t© Cadw Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and Cadw\u0027s copyright. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose. Attribution Statement: Designated Historic Asset GIS Data, The Welsh Historic Environment Service (Cadw), 2018, licensed under the Open Government Licence http://www.nationalarchives.gov.uk/doc/open-government-licence/version/3/\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313131393437\tX:\\Designations\\CADW\\Historic Parks and Gardens X:\\Designations\\CADW\\Historic Parks and Gardens\\Historic Parks \u0026amp; Gardens - Essential Setting.lyr  X:\\Designations\\CADW\\Historic Parks and Gardens\\Historic Parks and Gardens.lyr  X:\\Designations\\CADW\\Historic Parks and Gardens\\Historic Parks and Gardens - Gardens and Kitchen Gardens.lyr  X:\\Designations\\CADW\\Historic Parks and Gardens\\Historic Parks and Gardens - Significant View.lyr  X:\\Designations\\CADW\\Historic Parks and Gardens\\Historic Parks and Gardens - Walks Seating.lyr   Used to be in the Legacy CCW Archive M:\\GIS_Data\\Live\\Physical\\historic_landscapes\\CADW\\Parks_\u0026amp;_gardens\\    \u0026gt;\u0026gt;\u0026gt; multiple MapInfo tables\tGIS Service Desk John Briggs, Landscape Architect, PPG, NRW External Contact: Nigel Davies, Cadw\tThis is a third party spatial dataset owned by Cadw, who are the Welsh Governments historic environment services working for an accessible and well-protected historic environment for Wales. Wales has a rich inheritance of historic parks and gardens. They form an important and integral part of the historic and cultural fabric of the country.  Starting in 1992, CADW has undertaken a comprehensive survey of historic parks and gardens in Wales. Parks and gardens thought to be of national importance have been included in the Register of Parks and Gardens of Special Historic Interest in Wales and this dataset contains the digitised boundaries for the areas included in the Register.  The register was compiled in order to aid the informed conservation of historic parks and gardens by owners, local planning authorities, developers, statutory bodies and all concerned with them. This spatial dataset NRW has access to as part of the Historic parks and Gardens are as follows:  - Historic Parks and Gardens - Essential Setting - Historic Parks and Gardens - Historic Parks and Gardens - Gardens and Kitchen Gardens - Historic Parks and Gardens - Significant View - Historic Parks and Gardens - Walks Seating\tCadw. Welsh Historic Monuments\t2023-10-02\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-03-21T10:34:57.000Z\tnobody nobody\t-\tPublic record\n17102\tEXT_DS111949\t2024-05-28T12:10:55.617Z\t877\tUnassessed\tEditable\tCadw: World Heritage Sites (3rd Party Data)\t© Cadw Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and Cadw\u0027s copyright. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose. Attribution Statement: Designated Historic Asset GIS Data, The Welsh Historic Environment Service (Cadw), 2018, licensed under the Open Government Licence http://www.nationalarchives.gov.uk/doc/open-government-licence/version/3/\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313131393439\tX:\\Designations\\CADW\\World Heritage Sites X:\\Designations\\CADW\\World Heritage Sites\\World Heritage  Arcs of View.lyr  X:\\Designations\\CADW\\World Heritage Sites\\World Heritage  Essential Setting.lyr  X:\\Designations\\CADW\\World Heritage Sites\\World Heritage  Significant View.lyr  X:\\Designations\\CADX:\\Designations\\CADW\\World Heritage Sites\\World Heritage Sites.lyr   Legacy CCW Archive M:\\GIS_Data\\Live\\Physical\\historic_landscapes\\World_Heritage_Sites\tGIS Service Desk  John Briggs, Landscape Architect, EPP, NRW External Custodian: CADW - the Welsh Government\u0027s historic environment service working for an accessible and well-protected historic environment for Wales.\tNatural Resources of Wales (NRW) are supplied a number of historic and cultural datasets under a licence from Cadw. Cadw is the Welsh Government’s historic environment service working for an accessible and well-protected historic environment for Wales. They were set up with the aim of conserving Wales’s heritage, helping people understand and care about their history and helping to sustain the distinctive character of Wales.This is a spatial dataset containing the digitised boundaries of World Heritage Sites. World Heritage Sites are places that the World Heritage Committee of UNESCO (United Nations Educational, Scientific and Cultural Organization) has inscribed on a list of international sites because of their outstanding universal value, the importance of which is so great as to transcend national boundaries. Wales currently has three world heritage sites - the Castles and Town Walls of Edward I in Gwynedd at Caernarfon, Conwy, Beaumaris and Harlech in north-west Wales; Blaenavon Industrial Landscape in south-east Wales; and Pontcysyllte Aqueduct and Canal in north-east Wales.  This spatial dataset for NRW is split into 4 different spatial layers: - Arcs of View - Essential Setting - Significant View - World Heritage Sites\tCadw. Welsh Historic Monuments\t2022-12-02\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T12:05:08.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17096\tEXT_DS111953\t2024-05-28T12:10:55.432Z\t1807\tUnassessed\tEditable\tCadw: Listed Buildings (3rd Party Data)\t© Cadw  Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and Cadw\u0027s copyright. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose. Attribution Statement: Designated Historic Asset GIS Data, The Welsh Historic Environment Service (Cadw), 2018, licensed under the Open Government Licence http://www.nationalarchives.gov.uk/doc/open-government-licence/version/3/\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313131393533\tX:\\Designations\\CADW\\Listed Buildings.lyr   Used to be: Legacy CCW Archive M:\\GIS_Data\\Live\\Physical\\historic_landscapes   \u0026gt;\u0026gt;\u0026gt; various MapInfo tables\tGIS Service Desk  John Briggs, Landscape Architect, NRW  For further information please contact Cadw at Plas Carew, Unit 5/7 Cefn Coed, Park Nantgarw, Cardiff, CF15 7QQ, www.cadw.wales.gov.uk.\tNatural Resources of Wales (NRW) are supplied a number of historic and cultural datasets under a licence from Cadw. Cadw is the Welsh Government’s historic environment service working for an accessible and well-protected historic environment for Wales. They were set up with the aim of conserving Wales’s heritage, helping people understand and care about their history and helping to sustain the distinctive character of Wales.  Buildings and structures of national importance are given legal protection by being placed on a ‘List’ of Buildings of Special Architectural or Historic Interest. This is a third party spatial dataset containing information on the CADW designated sites and listed buildings in Wales. In Wales there are over 29,000 buildings and structures on the list. Listed buildings range from Medieval Churches to modern commercial premises etc, structures can include railings, gate piers, walls, war memorials, gravestones, post boxes and telephone boxes.\tCadw. Welsh Historic Monuments\t2019-02-04\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-07-08T08:21:12.000Z\tnobody nobody\t-\tPublic record\n17104\tEXT_DS112025\t2024-05-28T12:10:55.619Z\t781\tUnassessed\tEditable\tArchaeological Trust Spatial Data (3rd Party Data)\t© Clwyd Powys Archaeological Trust NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly. The following acknowledgment must be included in any hard copy reports or printed publication: \u0027This report is based on Historic Environment Record Data. [insert relevant Archaeological Trust name here; Clwyd-Powys Archaeological Trust / Dyfed Archaeological Trust / Glamorgan-Gwent Archaeological Trust / Gwynedd Archaeological Trust] copyright.\u0027\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313132303235\tX:\\Designations\\Archaeological Trust\\Archaeological Trust Boundaries.lyr  X:\\Designations\\Archaeological Trust\\Archaeological Trust Points.lyr  x:\\Designations\\Archaeological Trust\\Archaeological Trust Polygons.lyr  x:\\Designations\\Archaeological Trust\\Archaeological Trust Lines.lyr    Legacy CCW Archive M:\\GIS_Data\\Live\\Physical\\historic_landscapes\\CPAT_SMR.TAB\tGIS Service Desk  John Briggs, Landscape Architect, Environmental Policy Group, NRW\tThe four Welsh archaeological trusts, which were established in the mid-1970s, are independent limited companies with charitable status providing a uniform local archaeological service across the whole of Wales. Natural Resources Wales (NRW) has licenced access to the Archaeological Trusts spatial data. In Wales there are four Archaeological Trusts: - Clwyd-Powys Archaeological Trust - Dyfed Archaeological Trust - Glamorgan-Gwent Archaeological Trust - Gwynedd Archaeological Trust\tClwyd-Powys Archaeological Trust-Dyfed Archaeological Trust-Gwynedd Archaeological Trust-Glamorgan-Gwent Archaeological Trust\t2026-02-10\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2026-02-10T10:26:34.000Z\tGary Eccleston\t-\tPublic record\n17098\tEXT_DS112026\t2024-05-28T12:10:55.561Z\t717\tUnassessed\tEditable\tRegister of Historic Landscapes: Historic Landscape Character Areas (3rd Party Data)\t© Cadw, Gwynedd Archaeological Trust, Dyfed Archaeological Trust, Clwyd-Powys Archaeological Trust, Glamorgan-Gwent Archaeological Trust. NRW owns the copyright of the collation, but the ownership of the records themselves rests with the originator. Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and NRW\u0027s copyright.  It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313132303236\tX:\\Physical\\Landscape\\Landmap\\LandMap Historic Landscape.lyr  X:\\Physical\\Landscape\\LandMap2017\\LANDMAP Historic Landscape.lyr\tGIS Service Desk Jill Bullen, Senior Landscape Specialist, Strategic Planning Group, NRW\tCare should be taken when using this data. The Register of Landscapes of Historic Interest in Wales has been divided into several areas called Historic Landscape Character Areas. This dataset contains the boundaries of these areas. The dataset is jointly owned by the Archaeological Trusts and Cadw. Cadw is the Welsh Governments historic environment service working for an accessible and well-protected historic environment for Wales. The datasets are essential for NRW in planning casework, to determine if particular developments will have an impact on a historic landscape. In collaboration with Cadw and the Archaeological Trusts jointly promotes the use of the Register and the Historic Landscape Character areas in the planning and development system, in which historic landscapes are a \u0027material consideration\u0027.\tGwynedd Archaeological Trust-Cadw. Welsh Historic Monuments-Dyfed Archaeological Trust-Clwyd-Powys Archaeological Trust-Glamorgan-Gwent Archaeological Trust\t2015-12-31\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-03-07T16:46:55.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17091\tEXT_DS112468\t2024-05-28T12:10:54.963Z\t678\tUnassessed\tEditable\tMarine Protected Areas (MPAs) Biophysical Data Layer Project (3rd Party Data)\t© DEFRA 2010 NRW have signed a licence with regards to the access and use of this dataset. Parts of the dataset are restricted, please see individual metadata entries for details. Derived data may be used within NRW exclusively within the scope of the aims of the DEFRA project. Derived data (as listed in the licence) may not be used for commercial gain therefore derived layers must not be made available in response to requests by external organisations that may profit from their use.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313132343638\tArchived as Project 271, Media 983 and 1000-1013 (File paths - K:\\Archive\\Media 901to1000\\Media 983,  K:\\Archive\\Media 901to1000\\Media 1000, K:\\Archive\\Media 1001to1100\\Media 1001 etc etc.)  In addition to Related Titles: DCT-10-184068 Distribution of highly mobile species 2010 DCT-12-049886 Spawning and nursery grounds of selected fish species in UK waters 2012. DCT-10-075940 Oceanic thermal fronts from Earth observation data - a potential surrogate for pelagic diversity Summary Document 2010 DCT-10-184095 Development of marine diversity data layer: review of approaches and proposed methods 2009 DCT-10-077540 Residual current flow datalayer: Description of approach 2010 DCT-10-077274 Development of a Benthic Productivity Datalayer: Assessing the available approaches 2009 DCT-10-078178 Benthic productivity data layer development-North Sea Pilot Study 2010\tGIS Service Desk Internal Custodian: Kirsten Ramsay, Team Leader, Marine \u0026amp; Coastal Ecosystems Team (Formerly James Dargie who now works at NatureScot)        See Also: Report No 6, Task 1A. Report No 13, Task 1B. Report No 8, Task 2A. Report No 14, Task 2B. Report No17: Task 2D. Report No 24, Task 2i. Report No 22, Task 3.\tMarine Protected Areas (MPAs) are a clearly defined geographical space, recognised, dedicated and managed, through legal or other effective means, to achieve the long-term conservation of nature with associated ecosystem services and cultural values. This network of MPAs will help meet commitments under the Convention on Biological Diversity and contribute to the measures needed to achieve Good Environmental Status across Europe’s seas by 2020 under the EU Marine Strategy Framework Directive. The United Kingdom (UK) is committed to the establishment of a network of  MPAs to conserve marine ecosystems and marine biodiversity. Selection of MPAs should be based on best available biological, physical, oceanographic and socio-economic data. Defra and partners have commissioned a consortium lead by ABPmer Ltd and partners to take forward a package of work to provide this data. This dataset contains the project outcomes. The purpose of this data capture was to collect the data that will be required for designating new MPAs following the Marine Bill. The overall aim is to ensure that the best available information is available for the selection of MPAs in UK waters, and that the data layers can be easily accessed and utilised by those whom will have responsibility for selecting sites. The data layers will also be of use in taking forward marine planning in UK waters. The project has been divided into a number of discrete tasks each of which has a specific temporal coverage (see separate metadata entries which will be added as and when tasks are completed). Data used is loosely taken between the following dates 1982-2008.\tVarious-Department for Environment, Food and Rural Affairs (DEFRA)-Joint Nature Conservation Committee (JNCC)-Natural Resources Wales (NRW)\t2008-12-31\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-04-17T12:26:17.000Z\tnobody nobody\t-\tPublic record\n17093\tEXT_DS112485\t2024-05-28T12:10:55.287Z\t763\tUnassessed\tEditable\tBritish Geological Survey (BGS): Maps and Memoirs (3rd Party Data)\t© BGS and NRW  There are no use restrictions on NRW owned data (GIS layer).  NRW data may be re-used under provision and in line with the terms of a NRW licence. NRW does NOT grant permission to disseminate or re-use any data that is not labelled as NRW ownership.  Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313132343835\tThe CCW MapInfo layer is available on Open Datasets when MapInfo is started up.  Selected memoirs and reports are held in CCW libraries and by Area Earth Science Officers.  X:\\Physical\\Geological\\ X:\\Physical\\Geological\\Mineral Resources\tGIS Service Desk Raymond Roberts, Senior Earth Scientist Geologist/ Earth Science Officer, NRW\tThe British Geological Survey (BGS) maps and memoirs are the principal geological data sources in Britain. Traditionally the 1:50,000 maps have been accompanied by explanatory volumes called Memoirs however now maps are often published with less comprehensive sets of explanatory notes.   Natural Resources Wales (NRW) holds a basic digital GIS layer of BGS geological data at 1:250,000 scale and selected memoirs and reports are held by NRW libraries.\tBritish Geological Society\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T12:05:26.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17103\tEXT_DS112862\t2024-05-28T12:10:55.622Z\t365\tValid\tEditable\tBangor University School of Ocean Science (SOS) Survey of Sabellaria Reefs at Criccieth North Wales (2001) (3rd Party Data)\t© Bangor University, 2014. NRW have received permission to release, publish or disseminate the data held in Marine Recorder freely. Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and NRW\u0027s copyright. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313132383632\tArchived as Project 284, Media 1110.  Species data is held in Marine Recorder [MRCCW30000000039]\tKirsten Ramsay, Subtidal Team Leader, MFSG, NRW\tUK Biodiversity Action Plan (BAP) priority habitats cover a wide range of semi-natural habitat types, and were those that were identified as being the most threatened and requiring conservation action under the UK Biodiversity Action Plan (UK BAP). The UK BAP habitats and species lists have been used to draw statutory lists of priority habitats as required under Section 42 of the Natural Environmental and Rural Communities (NERC) Act 2006.   Sabellaria alveolata reefs are formed by the honeycomb worm Sabellaria alveolata, a polychaete which constructs tubes in tightly packed masses with a distinctive honeycomb-like appearance. These reefs can be up to 30 or even 50 cm thick and take the form of hummocks, sheets or more massive formations. Reefs are mainly found on the bottom third of the shore, but may reach mean high water of neap tides and extend into the shallow subtidal in places. Few studies have directly examined the S.alveolata associated communities and the majority of which, were conducted abroad. Studies have been undertaken using quantitative sampling of algae and epifaunal communities, studying reefs around the UK, however, no examination was made of infauna.    This dataset is made up of the results of an investigation into the faunal and floral communities associated with intertidal Sabellaria alveolata reefs at Criccieth, North Wales.  The aims of the study were to provide further information regarding the dynamics of the flora/epifauna and infauna communities associated with S. alveolata reefs in the UK.\tUniversity of Wales, Bangor. School of Ocean Sciences-Natural Resources Wales (NRW)\t2001-12-31\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2026-01-09T14:20:42.000Z\tMonica Jones\tMEDIN\tPublic record\n17095\tEXT_DS113077\t2024-05-28T12:10:55.418Z\t344\tUnassessed\tEditable\t2 FULL FIELD TEST - marine data (3rd Party Data)\t© CCGC/CCW and various third party recorders 2011 CCW owns the copyright of the collation, but the ownership of the records themselves rests with the originator. There are no use restrictions on this data. Recipients may re-use, reproduce, disseminate this data free of charge in any format or medium, provided they do so accurately, acknowledging both the source and the copyright of CCW/third party recorders and do not use it in a misleading context. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose, that dissemination or publishing does not result in duplication and that it is fairly interpreted. Advice on interpretation should be sought where required. To avoid re-using old data, users should periodically obtain the latest version from the original source. Note to staff: Please attach the above statement to any data being issued.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313133303737\tArchive in media 205, project 102\tGabrielle Wyn, Intertidal Team Leader, Marine and Freshwater Science Group.       test\tTest export to MEDIN WAF 31-07-2012. Test that metadata date is reflecting the last data it was edited 28-09-2012    Testing OLIBWeb 24/01/2014  Based on the GIS non  native layers  Purpose of data capture: To test the system  Methods of data capture: Not real data but based on non native GIS layers metadata.  Geographic coverage: Wales  Temporal coverage: 1900 to 2010.  Some records are recorded to the day, whereas some can only be attributed to month or year.  Confidence in data: The majority of records are collected by specialists. Ad-hoc records are verified where possible.\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)\t2010-12-26\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T09:59:16.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17087\tEXT_DS114487\t2024-05-28T12:10:54.604Z\t724\tUnassessed\tEditable\tMarine Aggreggates Levy Sustainability Fund (MALSF) Outer Bristol Channel Marine Habitat Study (Biomor 4 report) - Multibeam Data (3rd Party Data)\t© Marine Aggreggates Levy Sustainability Fund NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313134343837\tArchived as Project 308, Media 1229 (File path is K:\\Archive\\Media 1201to1300\\Media 1229) MALSF data is managed by BGS as a MEDIN Data Archive Centre (DAC).  The data is available through the DAC network.\tGIS Service Desk  Internal Custodian: Kirsten Ramsay, Team Leader, Marine \u0026amp; Coastal Ecosystems Team       Vertical Extent:  -10. -60; metres (Tidal corrections carried out on the data during post processing)\tThe Outer Bristol Channel Marine Habitat Study was a multifaceted project involving scientific investigation Interpretation and education in an area with potential marine aggregate resources. The Bristol Channel and Severn Estuary boarded by Wales and England, has the largest tidal range in UK waters and is a multiple-use environment. Natural resource activities include aggregate extraction, fisheries and wind-farm developments. Marine nature conservation is prominent with Lundy Marine Nature Reserve in the south and, under the EC Habitats Directive, a Special Area of Conservation. The purpose of this study was to undertake a variety of work to collect and provide data and interpretations on the current physical state of the sea bed environment in terms of biology, sediment, geology and morphology. The study was jointly lead by the British Geological Survey (BGS) and Amgueddfa Cymru - National Museum Wales (NMW) and supported by core funding from the Aggregate Levy Sustainable Fund (ALSF) in Wales and England. Additional support came from The Crown Estate and the British Marine Aggregate Producers Association (BMAPA). There were numerous aims to this project, as outlined in the report (see related titles). This dataset just covers one specific aim: To undertake a marine geophysical survey utilising multibeam, sidescan sonar and sub-bottom seismic reflection systems. This dataset comprises of multibeam bathymetry data for the Outer Bristol Channel, including raw data files, cruise logs, calibration data, processed data and geotiffs. As well as the sidescan sonar and sub bottom profile data.  The purpose of this data capture was to collect multibeam data for the Biomor project to give a 3D image of the seabed, and enable display of sandbanks, ascertain slope steepness and identify other seabed features. Additional backscatter and acoustic data along with benthic sampling enabled the multibeam data to be used to classify and map the seabed.\tMarine Aggregates Levy Sustainability Fund\t2006-11-30\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T12:00:23.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17088\tEXT_DS114689\t2024-05-28T12:10:54.617Z\t631\tUnassessed\tEditable\tNational Water Vole (Arvicola amphibius) Database and Mapping Project (3rd Party Data)\t© Various Partners, 2010. The dataset is under joint ownership of various partners. NRW has a copy but is not one of the owners. NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313134363839\tThis dataset is currently managed and supplied by RSWT (hosted by Hampshire and Isle of Wight Wildlife Trust) on behalf of the Environment Agency. NRW hold this data currently on the M Drive: M:\\GIS_Data\\Live\\Biological\\Species\\all_wales\\Terrestrial\\Mammals\\Water_Voles\tGIS Service Desk  External Contact: Helen Perkins, Water for Wildlife Project (Royal Society of Wildlife Trusts)\tIn 2007 the UK Water Vole Steering Group highlighted the need for a concerted effort to collate and map available data in order to assess the national status and trend of the species and to report against national Biodiversity Action Plan (BAP) targets. It also recognised the potential of a spatial water vole layer which could be used to support conservation measures and enable more strategic working at local, regional and national level. The Water Vole Database and Mapping Project was established in January 2008 with funding provided by the Environment Agency, Royal Society of Wildlife Trusts (RSWT) and People\u0027s Trust for Endangered Species. Further funding was later provided by Scottish Natural Heritage. This dataset comprises a GIS of water vole alert areas, local key areas and regional key areas for England, Scotland and Wales 2004-2008. This GIS has been derived from water vole records provided to the project for this purpose by a total of 70 data providers. The GIS must be used in conjunction with the Guide to the Use of Project Outputs 2010 provided to recipients of the mapping outputs in 2010. The project is managed by RSWT, with work delivered by a Water Vole Information Officer based at Hampshire Wildlife Trust. Variable, information is from a wide range of suppliers.\tVarious\t2010-08-31\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-03-07T17:02:52.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17086\tEXT_DS114814\t2024-05-28T12:10:54.565Z\t874\tUnassessed\tEditable\tLuftwaffe Aerial Photographs for Anglesey (3rd Party Data)\t© NARA NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313134383134\tPrints are held in the aerial photo archive in North Region (Mike Willis room).   Negatives are held in the samples fridge in MYF Labroratory.   A crude CCW produced flight diagram is available on MapInfo.\tGIS Service Desk Sally Ellis, Conservation Officer, North West Wales Sites Team, NRW\tA copy of prints and negatives of the Luftwaffe aerial photography of Anglesey.  Flight diagrams are also available as negatives. The purpose of this data capture was to covert aerial photography of the UK before the outbreak of World War 2 (WW2).  Photos are available for areas that were considered possible military targets. Countryside Council for Wales (CCW) acquired a copy of the photos as reference to changes in the environment and to support conservation aims.\tNational Archives and Records Administration (NARA)\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T12:24:06.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17090\tEXT_DS114820\t2024-05-28T12:10:54.846Z\t654\tUnassessed\tEditable\tUK Centre for Ecology and Hydrology (UKCEH): Land Cover Map 2000 and 2007 (3rd Party Data)\t© UKCEH NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly. Attribution Statement: : © UKCEH. Contains Ordnance Survey data © Crown copyright and database right [year].\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313134383230\tX:\\Physical\\Landcover Map\\Landcover Map 2000.lyr  X:\\Physical\\Landcover Map\\Landcover Map 2007.lyr    Used to be in: Legacy CCW Archive M:\\GIS_Data\\Live\\Physical\\Land_Cover_Map_2007\\\tGIS Service Desk Subject Matter Experts: Helena Sykes, David Allen\tLand Cover Map is a UK Centre for Ecology and Hydrology (UKCEH) spatial dataset, which NRW acquires under licence. There are two datasets that NRW get from UKCEH, these being Land Cover Map 2000 and Land Cover Map 2007. NRW only has a segment of the data and not the whole of GB. This segment covers, the whole of Wales, cross boarder catchments and coastal areas around the Bristol Channel.   Land Cover Map 2000 (LCM2000) updates and substantially upgrade UKCEH\u0027s Land Cover Map of Great Britain (LCMGB) 1990 and also cover Northern Ireland. This was the first UKCEH all UK dataset. LCM200 was classified in relation to JNCC\u0027s Broad Habitats, and so encompasses the entire range of UK Habitats. LCM2000 is used for a wide range of applications including environmental character assessments, environmental protection, transport planning, animal disease distribution, bird and habitat relationships and forestry research. Land Cover Map 2007 (LMC2007) was released in July 2011, and is a parcel-based classification of UK land cover. LCM2007 builds upon the successes of the parcel-based mapping of LMC2000 and employs similar but enhanced classification techniques.\tCentre for Ecology and Hydrology (CEH)\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T12:00:54.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17085\tEXT_DS114947\t2024-05-28T12:10:54.547Z\t354\tUnassessed\tEditable\tUKHO/Royal Navy Acoustic Multibeam Echosounder Survey of Outer Cardigan Bay and Caernarfon Bay, Irish Sea. Summer 2010 (3rd Party Data)\t© UKHO 2010.   NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly.  INFORMATION WARNING: Not to be used for navigation.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313134393437\tArchived as Project 364, Media 1351.   Any processed data will be unique to NRW. Source data is available from UK Hydrographic Office.\tGIS Service Desk  Marine Mapping Specialist, NRW External Contact: UKHO       We do have an MOU for this dataset currently saved in Ffynnon: ref DCT-11-107096 .\tIn summer 2010, the Royal Navy Survey vessel HMS ECHO carried out a multibeam echosounder survey of outer Cardigan Bay and Caernarfon Bay. This dataset is the multibeam data coverage from the voyage, surveyed to IHO standards and released by the UKHO after verification. The purpose of this data capture was to obtain bathymetry and backscatter datasets of the study area with 100% coverage.\tUnited Kingdom Hydrographic Office (UKHO)\t2012-10-28\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T12:24:24.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17089\tEXT_DS114950\t2024-05-28T12:10:54.677Z\t325\tUnassessed\tEditable\tIMAGIN Acoustic Multibeam Survey of the North Coast of Wales (3rd Party Data)\t© IMAGIN 2005 NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313134393530\tArchived as Project 312, Media 1235.   Reports available online through http://imagin.ucc.ie.   Master copy of data stored by the IMAGIN project and available on the IMAGIN website.\tGIS Service Desk  Marine Mapping Scientist, NRW\tMultibeam data for the North Wales part of the Irish Sea Marine Aggregates Initiative (IMAGIN) project. This includes GeoTiffs (Black and white), navigation data from the vessel and raw data in CARIS HIPS format. Collect multibeam data to support the IMAGIN project (Geological appraisal of marine aggregate resources in the Southern Irish Sea).\tMarine Institute-Geoscience Wales-Coastal and Marine Resources Centre-Geological Survey of Ireland\t2008-12-31\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T12:00:12.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17084\tEXT_DS114968\t2024-05-28T12:10:54.549Z\t639\tUnassessed\tEditable\tBangor University Acoustic Multibeam Echosounder Survey of the North Llyn Modiolus Bed 2008 (3rd Party Data)\t© Bangor University 2012. NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313134393638\tArchived as Project 234, Media 1354,1355,1356.   Raw data is stored at the School of Ocean Sciences, Bangor University\tGIS Service Desk  Subtidal Team, MFEG, NRW External Custodian:  Dr. Jim Burnell (Experimental Physicist), Ocean Sciences, Craig Mair Building, Bangor University The data was then processed by Christian Wilson at CEFAS\tThis is a multibeam echosounder (MBES) dataset covering the extent of the original horse mussel (Modiolus modiolus) bed off the north coast of the Llyn Peninsular, just west of Porth Dinllaen. The area surveyed is approximately 13 km long and 4 km wide.  Additional boat time between British Geological Survey (BGS) surveys was utilised to provide coverage of the North Llyn Modiolus bed. The dataset has been subsequently used by former Countryside Council for Wales (CCW), now Natural Resources Wales (NRW) for modiolus monitoring work; and, by Bangor University for teaching and Master of Science (MSc) project work.  The confidence in this dataset is high. The data has been tidally corrected although a couple of small gaps exist.  It is not clear whether the data meets International Hydrographic Organisation (IHO) order 1 standards.\tUniversity of Wales, Bangor. School of Ocean Sciences\t2012-07-06\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-07-08T08:21:13.000Z\tnobody nobody\t-\tPublic record\n17081\tEXT_DS114969\t2024-05-28T12:10:54.456Z\t346\tUnassessed\tEditable\tJNCC Acoustic Multibeam Echosounder Survey of Selected Sites off the North Coast of Anglesey as part of the Mapping European Seabed Habitats (MESH) Project (3rd Party Data)\t© JNCC 2008.  NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313134393639\tArchived as Project 179, Media 1357.   Master data is stored at JNCC.    Raw multibeam data is on CD-ROM (OF1001) as is processed multibeam data (OF1049), and in GIS format with other GIS data\tGIS Service Desk Subtidal Team, MFEG, NRW\tDuring the summer of 2005, JNCC collaborated with partners of the HABMAP project to survey areas of potential Annex 1 habitat (primarily reef) in the Irish Sea. This was to support nature conservation initiatives beyond 12 nm North of Anglesey. This multibeam echosounder survey was carried out alongside single-beam data collection, seabed sampling and towed video imaging. Four areas of seabed covering approximately 140 sq km were surveyed and following data analysis, the area of study was broadly characterised by a complex topography and mixed sediment mosaics. The purpose of this data capture was to obtain MBES coverage of the study areas for further interpretation and analysis in conjunction with other data gathered in the area, for the purpose of identifying Annex 1 subtidal habitats.  Confidence in data is high. Data depth corrected for tide using POLPRED software which utilises one or more of Proudman Oceanographic Laboratory\u0027s hydrodyamic models. CARIS HIPS / SIPS software used to create surfaces and gridded datasets by experienced surveyors.\tJoint Nature Conservancy Committee (JNCC)\t2012-07-09\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-07-08T08:21:13.000Z\tnobody nobody\t-\tPublic record\n17082\tEXT_DS115118\t2024-05-28T12:10:54.461Z\t488\tValid\tEditable\tRSPB Invertebrate and Algae Inventory of the Skerries (2011) (3rd Party Data)\t© RSPB 2011 There are no access restrictions on this data. Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and copyright of the owners. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313135313138\tArchived as Project 349, Media 1326 and 1366.   Species data available through Marine Recorder [MRCCW31600000005]. We had permission to digitise and enter into Marine Recorder\tPaul Brazier, Intertidal Ecologist, NRW External Contact: David Tompkins, RSPB (The Skerries)\tThe aim of this data capture was to develop an inventory of species for the Skerries around North Anglesey. Data was supplied to Countryside Council for Wales (CCW) to provide contextual information about seal habitats on the Skerries.    In 2011 the RSPB conducted an intertidal survey of the Skerries, off North Anglesey to create an inventory of species found there. 5 sites were surveyed to represent different intertidal environments with respect to exposure to wave action, silt and sediment level, tidal current exposure and shoreline substrata. At each location the shore was surveyed at high, mid and low tide levels. This provided an inventory of algal species and invertebrate species at the 5 locations recording presence/absence.   RSPB have given Natural Resources Wales (NRW) permission to include this data with its own data holdings in Marine Recorder and release with the rest of the collation.\tRoyal Society for the Protection of Birds (RSPB)\t2011-12-31\tpublication\tnull\thttps://registry.nbnatlas.org/public/show/dp122\t2026-01-09T14:21:22.000Z\tMonica Jones\tMEDIN\tPublic record\n17083\tEXT_DS115163\t2024-05-28T12:10:54.433Z\t813\tUnassessed\tEditable\tEIRGrid plc East West Interconnector Project in the Irish Sea (3rd Party Data)\t© EirGrid plc. NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313135313633\tArchived as Project 374, Media 1384 (File path: K:\\Archive\\Media 1301to1400\\Media 1384)  [A] Reports and appendices in .pdf format [B] Report Images/charts for each of the above [C] GIS data in ArcView and for use with ERMapper. Include habitat data (grab Photo locations, contours, seabed photo locations, side Scan locations, Video footage locations) [D] SideScan images in GeoTiff format [E] Source data.  unprocessed XYZ data for Bathymetry and sidescan data. [F] Processed gridded xyz data in tiff form [G] Images of sediment grabs and seabed [H] Video data in .VOB format (for use with DVD) [I] Supporting information as txt and pdf files.  Information about data and permissions for use\tInternal Custodian: Kirsten Ramsay, Team Leader, Marine \u0026amp; Coastal Ecosystems Team GIS Service Desk  External Custodian: EirGrid Plc\tFUGRO OSAE GmbH was contracted by EirGrid to survey an electrical cable route for the East West Interconnector Project which links the Republic of Ireland and the United Kingdom by a power cable.  The final selected route links Rush North Beach in Ireland and Barkby Beach in North Wales.  JP Kenny acted as marine engineering advisor.  This route was fully surveyed with bathymetric, environmental, geophysical and geotechnical methods from landing site to landing site. The total length of the final selected route from Rush North Beach to Barkby Beach is approximately 186 km and between 400 to 500 m wide. This data was required to plan the most favourable route option for installation of the cable link between Ireland (Rush, North Beach) to North Wales (Prestatyn, Barkby Beach).\tEirGrid Plc\t2009-01-08\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-07-08T08:21:14.000Z\tnobody nobody\t-\tPublic record\n17129\tEXT_DS115167\t2024-05-28T12:11:57.422Z\t648\tUnassessed\tEditable\tJNCC Acoustic Multibeam Echosounder Survey of two sites off North West Anglesey 2009 (3rd Party Data)\t© JNCC 2009 NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313135313637\tArchived as Project 381, Media 1392. Subsequent drop down video surveys carried out in the same areas are: Archived as Project 268, Media 1309.\tGIS Service Desk  External Contact: Offshore Survey Manager, JNCC\tIn summer 2009, JNCC commissioned Cefas to carry out a multibeam echosounder survey within two Areas of Search (AoS) for offshore Special Areas of Conservation (SACs) off the North West coast of Anglesey. These areas were selected by JNCC as historic data and evidence suggested that Modiolus modiolus beds, (a subtype of Annex I reef), had been recorded within these areas. The purpose of this data capture was to obtain multibeam (MBES) coverage of two areas of search, in order to carry out seabed interpretation and identify potential drop-camera locations for possible Modiolus modiolus biogenic reef presence. The interpretation of these data was to be used to identify potential drop-camera locations.\tJoint Nature Conservancy Committee (JNCC)\t2012-07-18\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T12:08:46.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17130\tEXT_DS115179\t2024-05-28T12:11:57.520Z\t596\tUnassessed\tEditable\tSwansea Bay Tidal Lagoon Geophysical Investigation (February 2012) (3rd Party Data)\t© Titan Environmental Surveys Ltd, 2012. NRW cannot disseminate this data. Those seeking the data such permission should approach the originator directly.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313135313739\tArchived as Project 384, Media 1398\tData Services Team Sean Evans/ Laura Grant, Team Leader Marine Ecologist or Marine Ecologist, NRW\tA hydrographic and geophysical survey of the proposed Swansea tidal lagoon in Swansea Bay was carried out by Titan Environmental Surveys Ltd in the winter of 2011/12. This included singlebeam echosounder, sidescan sonar, surface tow boomer and magnetometer surveys. All data were referenced to OSGB36 datum using OSTN02 datum transformation, and seabed bathymetry was reduced to chart datum using the UKHO Vertical Offshore reference frame (VORF) model. The dataset shows a gently sloping seabed of thin sand and gravels overlying a sequence of fine sediments of up to 20m thickness on top of boulder clay. An outcrop of boulder clay divides the site into E and W zones with featureless smooth sands in the E, and predominantly gravel in the W. No bedforms large enough to produce bathymetric features were identified. The purpose of this data capture was to carry out a hydrographic and geophysical survey of the proposed Swansea Tidal Lagoon site in Swansea Bay.  Data provided to Countryside Council for Wales (CCW) for internal business use only - for consultation on the Swansea Bay Tidal lagoon casework .  Data is considered confidential and may not be disseminated.\tTitan Environmental Survey Ltd-INAZIN Power Ltd\t2012-02-28\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-03-21T10:52:38.000Z\tnobody nobody\t-\tPublic record\n17122\tEXT_DS115256\t2024-05-28T12:11:57.299Z\t302\tUnassessed\tEditable\tRisso\u0027s Dolphin (Grampus griseus) Surveys Conducted in North Wales (2012) (3rd Party Data)\t© Whale and Dolphin Conservation 2012. Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and copyright of the owners. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313135323536\tArchived as Project 390, Media 1406   Excel spreadsheets are stored on the WDC server.\tGIS Service Desk Team Leader Marine Vertebrates, NRW. External Custodian: Sonja Mareike Eisfeld, WDC.         We have listed as not for re-supply externally.  As WG ERF grant, we are only aware of the condition that allows NRW to produce and  publish a NRW Scientific report.  It is not clear if we also have the right to distribute the data.\tA Welsh Government (ERF) grant funded project carried out by Whale and Dolphin Conservation (WDC).  WDC have studies cetaceans in the area around Ynys Enlli, Bardsey for 13 years.  The long-term dataset helps describe the occurrence, distribution, site fidelity, habitat use and behaviour of small cetaceans.  The data described here relates to the 2012 annual survey.  The collated information will help provide the basis for future surveys, comparisons to determine population densities for small cetacean species and also provide information for local conservation and management plans.  The seas around Ynys Enlli/Bardsey Island and the sound between Ynys Enlli and the mainland.\tWhale and Dolphin Conservation\t2013-03-31\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-04-17T12:30:17.000Z\tnobody nobody\t-\tPublic record\n17127\tEXT_DS115367\t2024-05-28T12:11:57.302Z\t709\tUnassessed\tEditable\tAudit of Marsh Fritillary (Euphydryas aurinia) Habitat Management in Bridgend County Borough Council (CBC) area August 2002 (3rd Party Data)\t© Bridgend CBC.  NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313135333637\tLegacy CCW Archive M:\\GIS_Users\\Adrian_f\\MapInfo Data\\Marsh Fritillary\\Habitat Quality Surveys\\SWales LA surveys (RSmith) revised\tGIS Service Desk  Mike Howe, Senior Invertebrate Ecologist, NRW Formerly: Adrian Fowles in CCW\tThe Marsh fritillary Euphydryas aurinia is a UK Biodiversity Action Plan (UK BAP) priority species and has been listed by the Welsh Government as species of Principal Importance for the Conservation of Biological Diversity in Wales (Section 74 species Countryside and Rights of Way Act 2000). This species in now confined to the south-western counties of England, south and west Wales, western Scotland and Ireland. There is some evidence to suggest that the species range is continuing to contract along eastern edge having previously been lost in central and eastern parts of England. It has also become scarcer within this range with healthy populations now any appearing to persist where there is sufficient habitat to support their meta-populations (dynamic network of colonies) in which the species naturally occurs. Nevertheless in parts of this range its status maybe poorly known due to recording issues.  For species existing in meta-populations, as is the case with many of our scarce butterflies, the quality and abundance of available habitat within colonising distance of local populations is extremely important. In Wales there is increasing emphasis on mapping these patches of habitat to complement surveys of marsh fritillary Euphydryas aurinia adults and larval webs.   This data consists of a MapInfo polygon layer illustrating the condition of habitats for marsh fritillaries in Bridgend. The purpose of this data capture was to ascertain the extent and condition of habitat capable of supporting populations of marsh fritillaries in order to provide scientifically-justified guidance to inform planning decisions. Confidence in this data is high because the data was collected under contract by experienced surveyors.\tBridgend County Borough Council\t2002-12-31\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-03-21T10:54:35.000Z\tnobody nobody\t-\tPublic record\n17121\tEXT_DS115368\t2024-05-28T12:11:57.248Z\t377\tUnassessed\tEditable\tAssessment of Rhos Pasture Habitat in Caerphilly County Borough Council (CBC) in respect of its Suitability and Condition for the Priority Butterfly Marsh Fritillary (Euphydryas aurinia) (3rd Party Data)\t© Caerphilly County Borough Council (CBC). NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313135333638\tLegacy CCW Archive M:\\GIS_Users\\Adrian_f\\MapInfo Data\\Marsh Fritillary\\Habitat Quality Surveys\\SWales LA surveys (RSmith) revised This data should be obtained from it\u0027s owner Caerphilly County Borough Council (CBC) to ensure you have the most up-to-date copy of the data.\tGIS Service Desk  Dr Mike Howe, Senior Invertebrate Ecologist, NRW   Formerly: Adrian Fowles in CCW\tThe Marsh fritillary Euphydryas aurinia is a UK Biodiversity Action Plan (UK BAP) priority species and has been listed by the Welsh Government as species of Principal Importance for the Conservation of Biological Diversity in Wales (Section 74 species Countryside and Rights of Way Act 2000). This species in now confined to the south-western counties of England, south and west Wales, western Scotland and Ireland. There is some evidence to suggest that the species range is continuing to contract along eastern edge having previously been lost in central and eastern parts of England. It has also become scarcer within this range with healthy populations now any appearing to persist where there is sufficient habitat to support their meta-populations (dynamic network of colonies) in which the species naturally occurs. Nevertheless in parts of this range its status maybe poorly known due to recording issues.  For species existing in meta-populations, as is the case with many of our scarce butterflies, the quality and abundance of available habitat within colonising distance of local populations is extremely important. In Wales there is increasing emphasis on mapping these patches of habitat to complement surveys of marsh fritillary Euphydryas aurinia adults and larval webs.   This data consists of a MapInfo polygon layer illustrating the condition of habitats for marsh fritillaries in Caerphilly County Borough Council (CBC). The purpose of this data capture was to ascertain the extent and condition of habitat capable of supporting populations of marsh fritillaries in order to provide scientifically-justified guidance to inform planning decisions. Confidence in this data is high because the data was collected under contract by experienced surveyors.\tCaerphilly County Borough Council\t2004-12-31\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-03-07T17:02:49.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17126\tEXT_DS115369\t2024-05-28T12:11:57.392Z\t576\tUnassessed\tEditable\tAudit of Marsh Fritillary (Euphydryas aurinia) within the Mynydd Mawr Special Area of Conservation (SAC) Extended Landscape for Habitat Management in Carmarthen County Borough Council (CBC) (3rd Party Data)\t© Carmarthen CBC. NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313135333639\tLegacy CCW Archive M:\\GIS_Users\\Adrian_f\\MapInfo Data\\Marsh Fritillary\\Habitat Quality Surveys\\Mynydd Mawr\\CCC~RGS MMawr Final GIS 2010\tGIS Service Desk Mike Howe, Senior Invertebrate Ecologist, NRW Formerly:  Adrian Fowels in CCW\tThe Marsh fritillary Euphydryas aurinia is a UK Biodiversity Action Plan (UK BAP) priority species and has been listed by the Welsh Government as species of Principal Importance for the Conservation of Biological Diversity in Wales (Section 74 species Countryside and Rights of Way Act 2000). This species is now confined to the south-western counties of England, south and west Wales, western Scotland and Ireland. There is some evidence to suggest that the species range is continuing to contract along eastern edge having previously been lost in central and eastern parts of England. It has also become scarcer within this range with healthy populations now only appearing to persist where there is sufficient habitat to support their meta-populations (dynamic network of colonies) in which the species naturally occurs. Nevertheless in parts of this range its status maybe poorly known due to recording issues. For species existing in meta-populations, as is the case with many of our scarce butterflies, the quality and abundance of available habitat within colonising distance of local populations is extremely important. In Wales there is increasing emphasis on mapping these patches of habitat to complement surveys of marsh fritillary Euphydryas aurinia adults and larval webs.  This data consists of an ArcMap polygon layer illustrating the condition of habitats for marsh fritillaries in the landscape outside the Mynydd Mawr Special Area of Conservation (SAC) Project Area to help inform planning decisions with regard to Favourable Conservation Status of the SAC Feature in order to provide scientifically-justified guidance to inform planning decisions.\tCarmarthenshire County Council\t2009-12-31\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-03-07T16:58:42.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17124\tEXT_DS115370\t2024-05-28T12:11:57.327Z\t406\tUnassessed\tEditable\tAudit of Marsh Fritillary (Euphydryas aurinia) Habitat Management in Neath Port Talbot (3rd Party Data)\t© Neath Port Talbot CBC. NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313135333730\tLegacy CCW Archive M:\\GIS_Users\\Adrian_f\\MapInfo Data\\Marsh Fritillary\\Habitat Quality Surveys\\SWales LA surveys (RSmith) revised\tGIS Service Desk  Mike Howe, Senior Invertebrate Ecologist, Terrestrial Ecosystem Group, NRW\tThe Marsh fritillary Euphydryas aurinia is a UK Biodiversity Action Plan (UK BAP) priority species and has been listed by the Welsh Government as species of Principal Importance for the Conservation of Biological Diversity in Wales (Section 74 species Countryside and Rights of Way Act 2000). This species in now confined to the south-western counties of England, south and west Wales, western Scotland and Ireland. This dataset is a MapInfo layer of the condition of habitat polygons for marsh fritillaries in Neath Port Talbot produced to help inform planning decisions.  The purpose of this data capture was to ascertain the extent and condition of habitat capable of supporting populations of marsh fritillaries in order to provide scientifically-justified guidance to inform planning decisions. This dataset is of a high quality collected under contract by experienced surveyors.\tNeath Port Talbot County Borough Council\t2003-12-31\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-03-07T16:58:50.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17128\tEXT_DS115371\t2024-05-28T12:11:57.399Z\t270\tUnassessed\tEditable\tAudit of Marsh Fritillary (Euphydryas aurinia) Habitat Management in Merthyr Tydfil County Borough Council (CBC) (3rd Party Data)\t© Merthyr Tydfil CBC NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313135333731\tM Drive\tGIS Service Desk  Mike Howe, Senior Invertebrate Ecologist, NRW Formerly Adrian Fowles in CCW\tThe Marsh fritillary Euphydryas aurinia is a UK Biodiversity Action Plan (UK BAP) priority species and has been listed by the Welsh Government as species of Principal Importance for the Conservation of Biological Diversity in Wales (Section 74 species Countryside and Rights of Way Act 2000). This species is now confined to the south-western counties of England, south and west Wales, western Scotland and Ireland. There is some evidence to suggest that the species range is continuing to contract along eastern edge having previously been lost in central and eastern parts of England. It has also become scarcer within this range with healthy populations now any appearing to persist where there is sufficient habitat to support their meta-populations (dynamic network of colonies) in which the species naturally occurs. Nevertheless in parts of this range its status maybe poorly known due to recording issues. For species existing in meta-populations, as is the case with many of our scarce butterflies, the quality and abundance of available habitat within colonising distance of local populations is extremely important. In Wales there is increasing emphasis on mapping these patches of habitat to complement surveys of marsh fritillary Euphydryas aurinia adults and larval webs.   This dataset consists of an ArcMap layer of the condition of habitat polygons for marsh fritillaries in Merthyr Tydfil  County Borough Council (CBC) to help inform planning decisions.  The purpose of this data capture was to ascertain the extent and condition of habitat capable of supporting populations of marsh fritillaries in order to provide scientifically-justified guidance to inform planning decisions.\tMerthyr Tydfil County Borough Council\t2003-12-31\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-04-17T10:01:49.000Z\tnobody nobody\t-\tPublic record\n17123\tEXT_DS115372\t2024-05-28T12:11:57.317Z\t666\tUnassessed\tEditable\tAudit of Marsh Fritillary (Euphydryas aurinia) Habitat Management in Rhondda Cynon Taff County Borough Council (CBC) (3rd Party Data)\t© Rhondda Cynon Taff County Borough Council (CBC) NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313135333732\tLegacy CCW Archive M:\\GIS_Users\\Adrian_f\\MapInfo Data\\Marsh Fritillary\\Habitat Quality Surveys\\RCT post Dec, 2004 RGS\tGIS Service Desk  Mike Howe, Invertebrate Ecologist, NRW\tThe Marsh fritillary Euphydryas aurinia is a UK Biodiversity Action Plan (UK BAP) priority species and has been listed by the Welsh Government as species of Principal Importance for the Conservation of Biological Diversity in Wales (Section 74 species Countryside and Rights of Way Act 2000). This species in now confined to the south-western counties of England, south and west Wales, western Scotland and Ireland. There is some evidence to suggest that the species range is continuing to contract along eastern edge having previously been lost in central and eastern parts of England. It has also become scarcer within this range with healthy populations now any appearing to persist where there is sufficient habitat to support their meta-populations (dynamic network of colonies) in which the species naturally occurs. Nevertheless in parts of this range its status maybe poorly known due to recording issues. For species existing in meta-populations, as is the case with many of our scarce butterflies, the quality and abundance of available habitat within colonising distance of local populations is extremely important. In Wales there is increasing emphasis on mapping these patches of habitat to complement surveys of marsh fritillary Euphydryas aurinia adults and larval webs.   This dataset consists of a MapInfo layer of the condition of habitat polygons for marsh fritillaries in Rhondda Cynon Taff. The purpose of this data capture was to ascertain the extent and condition of habitat capable of supporting populations of marsh fritillaries in order to provide scientifically-justified guidance to inform planning decisions.\tRhondda Cynon Taf County Borough Council\t2003-12-31\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-03-07T16:58:49.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17125\tEXT_DS115522\t2024-05-28T12:11:57.294Z\t301\tUnassessed\tEditable\tSwansea Bay and Carmarthen Bay Coastal Group Beach Monitoring Campaign 2013 (3rd Party Data)\t© Carmarthenshire County Council 2013.  NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313135353232\tData is archived as project 433, media 1470\tGIS Service Desk  Ceri Seaton, Marine and Coastal Physical Scientist, NRW\tData comprises of beach profile measurements for both Swansea Bay and Carmarthen Bay area. This data is available for Internal NRW use only.\tCarmarthenshire County Council\t2013-08-31\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T12:08:48.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17119\tEXT_DS115541\t2024-05-28T12:11:57.247Z\t853\tUnassessed\tEditable\tBotanical Society of Britain and Ireland (BSBI): Rare Plants Register for Wales (3rd Party Data)\t© Botanical Society of the British Isles NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313135353431\tX:\\Biological\\Rare plants register\\BSBI RPR 1 and 2km sq.lyr  X:\\Biological\\Rare plants register\\BSBI RPR 10km sq.lyr  X:\\Biological\\Rare plants register\\BSBI RPR points.lyr   Should contact BSBI for the most up to date information.\tGIS Service Desk  Terrestrial Environmental Evidence Manager, NRW  External Contact: Welsh Officer, BSBI\tThis dataset is wholly owned by Botanical Society of Britain and Ireland (BSBI) which has been licensed to Natural Resources Wales (NRW) for use. County Rare Plant Registers are prepared by Botanical Society of the British Isles (BSBI) using data from Vice-county recorders from a range of data sources including their own records, those sent to them, and those seen from other sources including Local Environmental Records Centres (LERCs). Records are validated by recorders, and provide a summary of the best available data for selected species including: - Red Data species: A subset of the International Union for Conservation of Nature (IUCN) Red Data Book criteria and categories related to species in the UK - Section 42 species: The Section 42 list of habitats and species of principal importance in Wales is the definite list and is a key requirement of the National Environment Research Council (NERC) Biodiversity Duty.   - Nationally Rare and Scarce species: Excludes rare species qualifying under the main IUCN criteria. - Locally Rare (and sometimes Scarce) species: A species should be defined as \u0027locally rare\u0027 if it was known to be present within three or fewer \u0027sites\u0027 within a vice-county.\tBotanical Society Of The British Isles (BSBI)\t2017-12-31\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-04-17T12:18:00.000Z\tnobody nobody\t-\tPublic record\n17116\tEXT_DS115861\t2024-05-28T12:11:57.215Z\t349\tUnassessed\tEditable\tPhase 1 Intertidal Biotope Mapping for Severn Estuary 2002 - 2004 (3rd Party Data)\t© Natural England, 2015.   NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313135383631\tArchived as Project 186 Media 528, 1185 (File paths K:\\Archive\\Media 501to1000\\Media 528 and K:\\Archive\\Media 1101to1200\\Media 1185)\tInternal Custodian: Paul Brazier, Senior Marine Environmental Assessment Officer, Marine  Environmental Assessment \u0026amp; Advice Team  GIS Service Desk  External Contact: Natural England\tThis is a 3rd party spatial dataset for Phase 1 intertidal biotope data for the English side of the Severn Estuary as an addition to the Welsh side which was completed by Countryside Council for Wales. The Severn Estuary has long been regarded as a site of international natural heritage importance but managing the wide variety of significant wildlife interests against a background of increasing human pressures represents huge challenges for the UK statutory conservation agencies. The study aim was to provide a powerful management GIS tool to support decision making processes and allow rapid assessments of the effects of human activities on local intertidal ecological features. The project involved the construct a Geographical Information System (GIS) database populated with Phase I level intertidal biotope data for the entire Severn Estuary site (English side). The study aim was to provide a powerful management GIS tool to support decision making processes and allow rapid assessments of the effects of human activities on local intertidal ecological features.  The objectives of the study are summarised below: - Conduct Phase I mapping field surveys to classify and map (at 1:5000 scale) intertidal biotopes along the English side of the Severn Estuary possible Special Area of Conservation (pSAC) including Bridgwater Bay Special Protection Area (SPA). - Present a consistent biotope dataset for intertidal areas throughout the site and to compliment similar previous mapping work of sub-tidal environments (Posford Duvivier) and saltmarshes (Dargie, 1998).  - Construct a Geographical Information System (GIS) database present a report giving a descriptive account of the site, highlighting significant habitats and species, and providing an interpretation of observations. - Present a report giving a descriptive account of the site, highlighting significant habitats and species, and providing an interpretation of observations.\tNatural England\t2005-02-28\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T12:05:12.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17117\tEXT_DS115864\t2024-05-28T12:11:57.284Z\t902\tUnassessed\tEditable\tCardigan Bay Marine Wildlife Centre Welsh Bottlenose Dolphin (Tursiops truncatus) Photo-identification Catalogue (2005-2012) (3rd Party Data)\t© Cardigan Bay Marine Wildlife Centre, 2014 NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313135383634\tArchived as Project 414, Media 1432 - data supplied in 2011 Archived as Project 453, Media 1495 - data supplied 2012/2013\tGIS Service Desk  Tom Stringell, Senior Marine Mammal Ecologist, NRW       Data is provided to NRW as a condition of the European Species Licence.  We have listed and would normally treat as third party data and therefore not for re-use (especially as this data I snot current) but in reality it depends on the T\u0026amp;Cs listed in the EPS licences, which do allow re-use and are as follows: 252.     Within four weeks after the expiry of this licence the Licensee shall submit to NRW copies of catalogued images and associated data obtained, subject to the terms and conditions of this licence. NRW has the Licensee’s permission to store, copy, use, and release or publish  any biodiversity records associated with the issue of this licence. Where NRW’s policy on public access to data states that the information is sensitive, publication and public access will be restricted in accordance with both the Environmental Information Regulations (2004) and NRW\u0027s guidance on access to data on sensitive biodiversity features. Where NRW\u0027s policy on public access to data states that the information is sensitive any such release will be under restrictive licence conditions in accordance with NRW’s guidance on access to data on sensitive biodiversity features. NRW may share the biodiversity records supplied with conservation organisations and research programmes selected by it. The licensee agrees that such third parties will have use of the images and associated data for the purposes of research programmes contributing to the conservation management of the species concerned; these purposes will include storage, copying, use, and publication where required. Please note that an inadequate return will prejudice future licence applications.   Additional guidance is provided for the documentation of images as part of the licence \\Protocols to avoid excess disturbance during photo-identification studies for SWF and CBMWC licensees.doc\\\"  Available from the species licence team.\"\tThe conservation status of bottlenose dolphin (Tursiops truncatus) has been categorised by Convention on International Trade in Endangered Species of Wild Fauna and Flora (CITES) as data deficient, indicating that inadequate information exists for this species concerning its distribution and population status. The only two areas in UK waters that have been identified as having the physical and biological factors essential to the life and reproduction of a population of bottlenose dolphins Tursiops truncatus are Cardigan Bay, Wales and the Moray Firth, Scotland.  The bottlenose dolphin Tursiops truncatus population of Cardigan Bay off the west coast of Wales has been estimated to consist of around 125 individuals. The dolphins appear to use the inshore waters of Cardigan Bay for both feeding and reproduction, and in the summer months calves and juveniles are often observed with adult individuals or groups.  The dataset contains photographic images of cetaceans from Cardigan Bay, Pwllheli and Fishguard. This photo-identification catalogue consists of an identification sheet for each bottlenose dolphin that has been successfully identified by volunteer researchers at Cardigan Bay Marine Wildlife Centre. The recognition of individual bottlenose dolphin is essential to the studies associated with animal behaviour and ecology.  Photo-identification was conducted to create a permanent record of bottlenose dolphins encountered around Cardigan Bay and facilitate in the identification of individual bottlenose dolphins as an individual, enabling future identification.\tCardigan Bay Marine Wildlife Centre\t2011-12-31\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-03-07T16:36:27.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17118\tEXT_DS115879\t2024-05-28T12:11:57.247Z\t818\tUnassessed\tEditable\tAcoustic Multibeam Echosounder Survey of Ramsey Sound, Pembrokeshire November 2008 (3rd Party Data)\t© Longdin and Browning. NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313135383739\tArchived as Project 400, Media 1417 Marine networked external hard drive available through VMWare P:\\TEL multibeam Ramsey - The physical hard drive is located with the Marine Team contact Kirsten Ramsey.\tGIS Service Desk  Kirsten Ramsey, Marine Ecosystems (subtidal) Team Leader, Marine and Freshwater Ecosystems Group, or James Moon (South Ops) External Custodian: TEL (Tital Environmental Ltd) or Longdin and Browning (who commission Clydeside Surveys Ltd).        According to the Marine Archive Access Database Project Number 400 - No information supplied about this data or where it came from.  Thought that this data was provided by Tital Environmental Ltd (along with the Swansea Bay data), however report that saved with it indicates that it was commissioned by Longdin \u0026amp; Browning.  The Ramsay data is potentially confidential.\tA multibeam bathymetric survey was commissioned by Longdin and Browning Ltd, and carried out by Clydeside Surveys Ltd, to carry out a cable route survey in Ramsey Sound, Pembrokeshire. This was carried out to assist the planning of a cable route and any further survey work. The main objectives of the survey were to provide the following: - Accurate and repeatable Bathymetric survey - Acoustic imaging of the seabed to identify seabed features. The most important aspect of this survey was to obtain accurate bathymetric survey data, over the entire survey area and also to check the digital imaging data for changes in seabed type.\tLongdin and Browning (Surveys) Limited\t2008-11-06\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T12:09:20.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17113\tEXT_DS116260\t2024-05-28T12:11:56.643Z\t1163\tUnassessed\tEditable\tBritish Geological Survey (BGS): Areas Susceptible to Groundwater Flooding (2010) (3rd Party Data)\tBritish Geological Survey © UKRI. NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly. The following acknowledgement should accompany any materials derived from the Data, for internal usage: \\Based upon Data provided by the British Geological Survey © UKRI. All rights reserved.\\\"\"\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313136323630\tX:\\Flood Risk\\Flood Risk Management\\Areas Susceptible to Groundwater Flooding 2010.lyr\tCustodian: Mark Pugh, Principal Advisor, FIRM, NRW\t2010 1km Gridded \u0027Areas Susceptible to Groundwater Flooding \u0027data is derived from BGS \u0027Susceptibility to Groundwater Flooding\u0027 dataset.   The data is a 1 kilometre square grid that identifies at a broad scale areas susceptible to flooding from groundwater on the basis of geological and hydrogeological conditions. It does not show the likelihood of groundwater flooding occurring and therefore is a hazard not risk-based dataset.  It does not take account areas where groundwater is likely to pond or flow, but simply considers where groundwater might emerge.  Hazard is represented by one of four area categories showing the proportion of each 1 km square that is susceptible to groundwater flood emergence \u0026lt; 25%, \u0026gt;\u003d 25% \u0026lt;50%, \u0026gt;\u003d50% \u0026lt;75%, \u0026gt;\u003d 75%, Absence of a value means that no risk is anticipated to be present.\tBritish Geological Survey (BGS)\t2010-12-31\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T13:06:14.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17120\tEXT_DS116286\t2024-05-28T12:11:57.151Z\t326\tUnassessed\tEditable\tForesty Commission Great Britain (FCGB): National Forest Estate - Forest District Boundaries (3rd Party Data)\t© Forestry Commission Great Britain Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and NRW\u0027s copyright. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313136323836\tX:\\Resource Management\\NRW Operational Areas\\FCGB Forest Districts.lyr\tGIS Service Desk  Keith Harri Jones, GIS and Spatial Services Team Leader, NRW\tThis is a spatial dataset based on a generalised version of the Great Britain wide forest district information. Natural Resources Wales has the whole of the UK Boundaries which includes, Forestry Commission England and Scotland and Wales.\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)\t2013-04-01\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T12:05:28.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17112\tEXT_DS116795\t2024-05-28T12:11:56.601Z\t611\tUnassessed\tEditable\tForestry Commission England (FCE): Forest SubCompartments (3rd Party Data)\t© The Forestry Commission. Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and copyright of the owners. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose. Attribution Statement: Contains, or is based on, information supplied by the Forestry Commission. © Crown copyright and database right [2018] Ordnance Survey [100021242] Attribution statement: Contains OS data © Crown copyright [and database right] [2018].\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313136373935\tx:\\Resource Management\\Land Management\\FC England Woodland Comp_Subcomp.lyr\tCustodian: Geraint Morgan and Arpana Chunihal   Metadata contact: GIS and Spatial Services Team , NRW\tThis is a spatial dataset detailing the extent and location of forest sub-compartments in England. Forestry Commission England (FCE) own this data, and have licenced Natural Resources Wales to use it under an OGL. The Forestry Commission holds information on trees and forests. The role of the Forest Inventory (the Sub-compartment Database (SCDB) and the stock maps) is to be their authoritative data source, giving them information for recording, monitoring, analysis and reporting.\tForestry Commission (FC)\t2019-01-17\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-10-10T07:51:23.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17115\tEXT_DS119070\t2024-05-28T12:11:56.644Z\t1885\tUnassessed\tEditable\tWelsh Government: Agricultural Land Classification (3rd Party Data)\t© Crown Copyright: Welsh Government. NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly. Attribution Statement: © Crown copyright: Welsh Government. Mapping derived from soils data © Cranfield University (NSRI) and for the Controller of HMSO 2017. © Crown copyright 2017, the Met Office. Contains OS data © Crown copyright and database right 2017. Contains Natural Resources Wales information © Natural Resources Wales and Database Right. All rights Reserved.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313139303730\tX:\\Physical\\Agricultural\\Agricultural Land Classification.lyr  X:\\Physical\\Agricultural\\Predictive Agricultural Land Classification Map.lyr  x:\\Physical\\Agricultural\\Predictive Agricultural Land Classification Map Attributed.lyr   Version 2 layers: X:\\Resource Management\\Welsh Government\\Soil Series on 50m Grid.lyr  X:\\Resource Management\\Welsh Government\\Soils of Wales.lyr  X:\\Resource Management\\Welsh Government\\Agri Land Class V2\\ALC Climatic Limitation Grade.lyr  X:\\Resource Management\\Welsh Government\\Agri Land Class V2\\ALC Depth to Slowly Permeable Layer (SPL).lyr  X:\\Resource Management\\Welsh Government\\Agri Land Class V2\\ALC Droughtiness Limitation Grade.lyr  X:\\Resource Management\\Welsh Government\\Agri Land Class V2\\ALC Field Capacity Days.lyr  X:\\Resource Management\\Welsh Government\\Agri Land Class V2\\ALC Grade – No masking layers applied.lyr  X:\\Resource Management\\Welsh Government\\Agri Land Class V2\\ALC grade for each 50m point.lyr  X:\\Resource Management\\Welsh Government\\Agri Land Class V2\\ALC Gradient Limitation Grade.lyr  X:\\Resource Management\\Welsh Government\\Agri Land Class V2\\ALC Overall Predicted ALC Grade.lyr  X:\\Resource Management\\Welsh Government\\Agri Land Class V2\\ALC Soil Depth Limitation Grade.lyr  X:\\Resource Management\\Welsh Government\\Agri Land Class V2\\ALC Soil Wetness Class.lyr  X:\\Resource Management\\Welsh Government\\Agri Land Class V2\\ALC Stoniness Limitation Grade.lyr  X:\\Resource Management\\Welsh Government\\Agri Land Class V2\\ALC Topsoil Texture.lyr  X:\\Resource Management\\Welsh Government\\Agri Land Class V2\\ALC Wetness and Workability Limitation Grade.lyr\tKeith Jones, Spatial Evidence Manager, Evidence, Knowledge and Advice\tThese are Welsh Government owned datasets licenced to Natural Resources Wales (NRW) under and Open Government Licence (OGL). The Agricultural Land Classification (ALC) system is used to grade the quality of agricultural land. The Predictive ALC map for Wales is based on the principles of the Agricultural Land Classification System of England and Wales, the Revised Guidelines and Criteria for Grading the Quality of Agricultural Land. The ALC system classifies land into one of the following five grades:  Grade 1 - excellent quality agricultural land;  Grade 2 - good quality agricultural land;  Grade 3a - good to moderate quality agricultural land;  Grade 3b - moderate quality agricultural land;  Grade 4 - poor quality agricultural land;  Grade 5 - very poor quality agricultural land.  Planning policy defines the top three grades (1-3a) as the \u0027Best and Most Versatile\u0027 agricultural land. Best and Most Versatile agricultural land accounts for approximately 7% of total land in Wales.\tWelsh Government\t2023-07-28\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-07-08T08:21:12.000Z\tnobody nobody\t-\tPublic record\n17114\tEXT_DS119113\t2024-05-28T12:11:56.601Z\t397\tUnassessed\tEditable\tKeep Wales Tidy: Blue Flag Awards (3rd Party Data)\t©  Keep Wales Tidy NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313139313133\tX:\\EU Directives\\Bathing Waters Directive\\Blue Flag Awards.lyr\tGIS Service Desk\tThis is a spatial dataset showing the location of Blue Flag beaches across Wales. 2018 marked the 30th year of the Blue Flag Award in Wales, which is generally considered the \u0027gold standard\u0027 for beaches across the world. The Blue Flag Programme is owned by the non-governmental, non-profit organisation \u0027Foundation for Enivronmental Education\u0027 (FEE). The Blue Flag Programme was started in France in 1985. It has been operating in Europe since 1987 and in areas outside of Europe since 2001. The programme is currently in operation in 46 countries across the world. In Wales, the award is managed by Keep Wales Tidy.\tKeep Wales Tidy\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T12:00:56.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17111\tEXT_DS119114\t2024-05-28T12:11:56.507Z\t683\tUnassessed\tEditable\tKeep Wales Tidy: Green Coast Awards (3rd Party Data)\t© Keep Wales Tidy NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313139313134\tX:\\EU Directives\\Bathing Waters Directive\\Green Coast Awards.lyr\tHelena Skyes\tThis is a spatial dataset detailing the extent and location of beaches with Green Coast Awards across Wales. The Green Coast Award recognises those beaches that are \u0027hidden gems\u0027 - the beautiful, untouched, rugged beaches that line so much of the Welsh coast.  The award recognises the excellent water quality and unspoiled environment, but unlike a Blue Flag Award beach, these sites won\u0027t have the infrastructure and intensive management generally associated with more traditional seaside resorts. The Green Coast Award is important in recognising all of Wales\u0027 top beach destinations, with our small (but mighty!) country boasting 19 Green Coast Awards during 2018.\tKeep Wales Tidy\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T12:05:26.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17109\tEXT_DS119177\t2024-05-28T12:11:56.487Z\t2038\tUnassessed\tEditable\tWelsh Government: Welsh Index of Multiple Deprivation (WIMD) (3rd Party Data)\t© Crown Copyright: Welsh Government Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and copyright of the owners. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose. Attribution Statement: © Crown copyright: Welsh Government. Ordnance Survey 100021874\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313139313737\tX:\\Social Economic\\Welsh Index of Multiple Deprivation\\WIMD 2000.lyr ,     X:\\Social Economic\\Welsh Index of Multiple Deprivation\\WIMD 2005.lyr ,     X:\\Social Economic\\Welsh Index of Multiple Deprivation\\WIMD 2008.lyr ,     X:\\Social Economic\\Welsh Index of Multiple Deprivation\\WIMD 2011.lyr ,     X:\\Social Economic\\Welsh Index of Multiple Deprivation\\WIMD 2014.lyr ,     x:\\Social Economic\\Welsh Index of Multiple Deprivation\\WIMD 2019.lyr , X:\\Social Economic\\Welsh Index of Multiple Deprivation\\WIMD 2025\\WIMD 2025 Access to Services.lyr, X:\\Social Economic\\Welsh Index of Multiple Deprivation\\WIMD 2025\\WIMD 2025 Community Safety.lyr, X:\\Social Economic\\Welsh Index of Multiple Deprivation\\WIMD 2025\\WIMD 2025 Education.lyr, X:\\Social Economic\\Welsh Index of Multiple Deprivation\\WIMD 2025\\WIMD 2025 Employment.lyr, X:\\Social Economic\\Welsh Index of Multiple Deprivation\\WIMD 2025\\WIMD 2025 Health.lyr, X:\\Social Economic\\Welsh Index of Multiple Deprivation\\WIMD 2025\\WIMD 2025 Housing.lyr, X:\\Social Economic\\Welsh Index of Multiple Deprivation\\WIMD 2025\\WIMD 2025 Income.lyr, X:\\Social Economic\\Welsh Index of Multiple Deprivation\\WIMD 2025\\WIMD 2025 Overall.lyr, X:\\Social Economic\\Welsh Index of Multiple Deprivation\\WIMD 2025\\WIMD 2025 Physical Environment.lyr,\tGIS Service Desk Julie Boswell, State of Natural Resources Reporting Specialist Advisor, Environment Assessment, Reporting and GIS, NRW\tThe Welsh Index of Multiple Deprivation (WIMD) is the Welsh Governments official measure of relative deprivation for small areas in Wales. It is designed to identify those small areas where there are the highest concentrations of several different types of deprivation. Deprivation is the lack of access to opportunities and resources which we might expect in our society. This can be in terms of material goods or the ability of an individual to participate in the normal social life of the community. An Index is a group of separate measurements which are combined into a single number. WIMD ranks all small areas in Wales from 1 (most deprived) to 1,909 (least deprived). It does not provide a measure of the level of deprivation in an area.\tWelsh Government\t2026-01-27\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2026-01-27T16:42:53.000Z\tKeith Jones\t-\tPublic record\n17110\tEXT_DS119198\t2024-05-28T12:11:56.505Z\t719\tUnassessed\tEditable\tWelsh Government: Phytophthora Core Disease Zone (3rd Party Data)\t© Crown Copyright: Welsh Government. NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313139313938\tX:\\Incidents\\Forest Health\\Phytophthora Core Disease Zone.lyr\tInternal Data Custodian(s):  Andrew Wright Tree Health Team Leader  (andrew.wright@cyfoethnaturiolcymru.gov.uk)  Metadata Point of Contact:  Andrew Wright Tree Health Team Leader  (andrew.wright@cyfoethnaturiolcymru.gov.uk)\tPhytophthora ramorum (P. ramorum) is a fungus-like pathogen called a water mould. It causes extensive damage and death to a wide range of trees and other plants. This spatial data is owned by Welsh Government (WG) and shows the boundary for the Phytophthora ramorum disease Core Disease Zone.  The boundary data is used to determine the Statutory Action required for infected sites and is based on OS data for physical features such as roads, rivers. Natural Resources Wales (NRW) draft this on-behalf of WG who then quality check the data and get it signed off for use by the Welsh Tree and Plant Health Steering Group. The master or top copy of this dataset is held by Welsh Government and a copy is retained by the NRW Tree Health Team.\tWelsh Government\t2015-01-01\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-05-13T10:39:22.743Z\tnobody nobody\t-\tPublic record\n17107\tEXT_DS119247\t2024-05-28T12:11:56.346Z\t553\tUnassessed\tEditable\tCranfield University: Soil Carbon Density Data Wales (3rd Party Data)\t© Cranfield University. NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313139323437\tX:\\Physical\\Soils\\Soil Carbon Density.lyr\tGIS Service Desk  Dylan L Williams, Soil Use and Management Advisor, NRW       http://www.landis.org.uk/data/nmcarbon.cfm\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW) holds copies of Cranfield datasets which containing soil and soil-related information for Wales. This is a spatial dataset owned by Cranfield University detailing the soil\u0027s carbon density across Wales at a 1km grid cell scale. This dataset provides users with a summary of the stock carbon in the soils across three layer depths 0-30 cm (map 30), 30-100 cm (map 100) and 100-150 cm (map GT100) based on the averages associated with Cranfield University\u0027s Horizon data.\tCranfield University\t2005-01-01\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-07-08T08:21:13.000Z\tnobody nobody\t-\tPublic record\n17108\tEXT_DS119264\t2024-05-28T12:11:56.345Z\t1340\tUnassessed\tEditable\tCranfield University: Land Information System (LandIS) Soil data (3rd Party Data)\t© Cranfield University NRW does NOT grant permission to 3rd parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the owner directly. Attribution Statement: Soils Data © Cranfield University (NSRI) and the Controller of HMSO (yyyy).\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313139323634\tSpatial Data: X:\\Physical\\Soils\\NATMAP vector Wales.lyr   Non spatial data: Y:\\NATMAP SOIL\\HORIZONfundamentalsV2.csv\tGIS Service Desk Keith H. Jones, GIS and Spatial Information Services Team Leader, Evidence Knowledge and Advice, NRW\tCranfield University maintains all the published and unpublished paper soil reports and maps for England and Wales, and market and lease a wide body of digital soil information. These datasets are held in the LandIS relational \u0027land information system\u0027 and National Soils Inventory (NSI) both are maintained by Cranfield.   Natural Resources Wales (NRW) holds copies of these datasets which contain soil and soil-related information for Wales. These include both spatial and non spatial data as follows:   Spatial Data:  NATMAP vector: Derived from the National Soil Map, this displays the 300 mapped soil associations at a scale of 1:250,000 and urban soil linework to 1:50,000.    NSI - point set data covering England and Wales on a 5km grid providing detailed information including erosion, landuse, lithological information.  Originally sampling from the 1980 with some re-sampling in the mid 1990s.   NSI Topsoil - includes information on Erosion, landuse and lithological information  NSI Profile - Detailed soil description and boundary information.   NSI Topsoil - Detailed measures of over 20 elements in the soil including pH  NSI Textures - soil texture  NSI Features - Provides depth data  Non spatial datasets:  HORIZON Fundamentals: Includes very detailed descriptions of the texture and other properties pertaining to the soils. This dataset provides the most detailed description of each horizon, or horizontal layer, determined for the soil series. It is based heavily on laboratory based analyses. -   HORIZON Hydraulics: Includes very detailed descriptions of the hydraulic properties pertaining to each layer, or horizon for each of the soils. This data is based heavily on laboratory based analyses. -   HORIZON Structure: This product contains soil series-layer properties which describe the respective structural properties of four successive nominal layers within each soil topsoil, upper subsoil, lower subsoil and substrate.  -   NAPMAP Associations: List of soil series components of soil associations with proportions (%). - NATMAP Legend: Text descriptions of Geology, Soil and Site characteristics and of Cropping and Land Use for each map unit of the National Map. -   Soil Series Hydrology: This product contains many properties of soil series, most of which are hydrological in nature.  - Soil Series Info: List of the basic soil types (or SERIES) which are components of the soil associations on the National Soil Map. - Soil Series Pesticide:  Includes information useful for pesticide control such as pesticide leaching and runoff classes.\tCranfield University\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-26T09:07:07.000Z\tnobody nobody\t-\tPublic record\n17106\tEXT_DS119265\t2024-05-28T12:11:56.142Z\t737\tUnassessed\tEditable\tWelsh Government: Shellfish Water Protected Areas (3rd Party Data)\t© Crown Copyright: Welsh Government Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and copyright of the owners.  It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose. Attribution Statement: © Crown copyright: Welsh Government. This data has been produced by Cefas for the purposes of the Surface Waters (Shellfish) (Classifications) (Amendment) Regulations 2009. © Crown copyright and Database 2013.  All rights reserved. Ordnance Survey Licence Number 10000356745.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313139323635\tX:\\EU Directives\\Shellfish Water Directive\\Shellfish Water Protected Areas 2013.lyr  X:\\EU Directives\\Shellfish Water Directive\\Shellfish Waters Pre 2013.lyr  X:\\EU Directives\\Shellfish Water Directive\\Shellfish Water Protected Areas 2022.lyr\tMark Charlesworth, SUW Senior Advisor Wales, WFD and Marine Team, NRW (mark.charlesworth@cyfoethnaturiolcymru.gov.uk)\tThe Water Framework Directive requires the specification of protected areas for the protection of economically significant species. This dataset shows the location of coastal and brackish waters that have been designated as Shellfish Waters under the EC Shellfish Waters Directive (2006/113/EEC). This dataset is wholly owned by Welsh Government, but has been made available to Natural Resources Wales (NRW) who are required to make it open on behalf of Welsh Government.\tWelsh Government\t2022-05-20\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-03-21T10:16:59.307Z\tnobody nobody\t-\tPublic record\n17154\tEXT_DS119283\t2024-05-28T12:14:11.154Z\t934\tUnassessed\tEditable\tSustrans: The National Cycle Network (3rd Party Data)\t© Sustrans Cymru NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly. Attribution Statement: © Sustrans Cymru and Ordnance Survey.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313139323833\tData is stored in the 3rd Party geodatabase.  It may be accessed through:  X:\\Recreation and Access\\Cycling and walking routes\\Sustrans Cycle Network Link.lyr  X:\\Recreation and Access\\Cycling and walking routes\\Sustrans National Route.lyr  X:\\Recreation and Access\\Cycling and walking routes\\Sustrans Regional route.lyr\tGIS Service Desk   Was - Jill Meyer, Recreation and Data Access Advisor, PPG, NRW\tThis is a spatial dataset wholly owned by Sustrans Cymru, showing the location of their cycle network, national routes and regional routes. Collectively these are known as The National Cycle Network. The National Cycle Network is a series of safe, traffic-free paths and quiet on-road cycling and walking routes that connect to every major town and city. The National Cycle Network is made up of 13,400 miles of walking and cycling routes across the UK. This includes a mixture of quiet lanes, on-road routes and traffic-free paths. Natural Resources Wales has access to this data under licence.\tSustrans Cymru\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-07-08T08:21:14.000Z\tnobody nobody\t-\tPublic record\n17151\tEXT_DS119298\t2024-05-28T12:14:10.838Z\t738\tUnassessed\tEditable\tOffice of National Statistics (ONS): Built Up Areas (3rd Party Data)\t© Office of National Statistics (ONS) Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and owners copyright. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose. Attribution Statement: Contains National Statistics data © Crown copyright and database right [2015]\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313139323938\tX:\\Social Economic\\Office of National Statistics\\ONS Built up areas.lyr\tCustodian: GIS Service Desk Business contact: NRW statistician\tThis dataset is owned by the Office of National Statistics (ONS). Natural Resources Wales (NRW) has access to the Welsh extent (plus some border areas) for this dataset. This spatial data provides information on the villages, towns and cities where people live, and allows comparisons between people living in built-up areas and those living elsewhere. Census data for these areas (previously called urban areas) has been produced every 10 years since 1981.\tOffice of National Statistics (ONS)\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T10:10:25.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17139\tEXT_DS119306\t2024-05-28T12:14:10.325Z\t1\tUnassessed\tEditable\tForestry Commission England (FCE): National Forest Estate Ownership England (3rd Party Data)\t© The Forestry Commission.  Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and copyright of the owners.  It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose. Attribution Statement: Contains, or is based on, information supplied by the Forestry Commission. © Crown copyright and database right [2018] Ordnance Survey [100021242] Attribution statement: Contains OS data © Crown copyright [and database right] [2018].\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313139333036\tx:\\Ownership\\Forestry Commission\\FCE Forest Ownership.lyr  x:\\Ownership\\Forestry Commission\\FCE Legal Boundary.lyr  x:\\Ownership\\Forestry Commission\\FCE_Forest Deeds.lyr   SDE Feature Class: NRWGDBTP.GISDATA.FC_NFE_OWNERSHIP\tGIS Service Desk\tThis collection of dataset details the location of external legal boundaries of land within FC ownership, and the acquisitions that have created the Forestry Commission England (FCE) Forestry Estate. This dataset is owned by Forest Commission England (FCE) and has been licenced to NRW under and OGL Licence.\tForestry Commission (FC)\t2022-02-07\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T12:05:12.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPrivate record\n17155\tEXT_DS119894\t2024-05-28T12:14:11.175Z\t713\tUnassessed\tEditable\tWelsh Government: Unified Peatland (3rd Party Data)\t© Crown Copyright: Welsh Government / BGS NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset.  Attribution Statement: © Crown copyright: Welsh Government. Derived in part from British Geological Survey geology data @ 1:50,000 scale. BGS©UKRI.  Contains Natural Resources Wales information © Natural Resources Wales and Database Right. All rights Reserved.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313139383934\tx:\\Physical\\Peat\\Unified Peatland.lyr\tGIS and Spatial Data Team Colin Chapman from WG confirmed this recently and James.Skates@gov.wales is the WG contact\tThis dataset was created by CEH on behalf of Welsh Government, therefore this data is wholly owned by Welsh Government and licenced to Natural Resources Wales (NRW) for use. Peatlands (defined here as deep (\u003d/\u0026gt;0.4 m) peat soils and supporting both mire habitats and other habitat/land-use types) cover 4.3% of Wales, and represent Wales largest terrestrial ecosystem store of carbon, as well as important reservoirs of biodiversity. This work in creating this dataset was undertaken as part of the Glastir Monitoring and Evaluation Programme (GMEP) in order to provide improved data on the extent and condition (in terms of broad habitat cover and drainage, as opposed to the nature conservation definition) of Welsh Peatlands, as a basis for: - prioritising areas for restoration - monitoring long-term change in the status of the Welsh peat resource - estimating current greenhouse gas (GHG) emissions from Welsh peatlands as a result of drainage and land-use change, and  - estimating the future climate mitigation potential of peat restoration.\tWelsh Government\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-07-08T08:21:14.000Z\tnobody nobody\t-\tPublic record\n17132\tEXT_DS119898\t2024-05-28T12:14:10.048Z\t368\tUnassessed\tEditable\tBritish Geological Survey (BGS): Ad hoc Offshore and UK Continental Shelf (UKCS) Geological Datasets (3rd Party Data)\t© British Geological Society and © DEFRA NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313139383938\tx:\\Physical\\Geological\\BGS Details survey UKCS WGS84.lyr  x:\\Physical\\Geological\\BGS Boulders cobbles UKCS WGS84.lyr  x:\\Physical\\Geological\\BGS Rockhard substrate UKCS WGS84.lyr  x:\\Physical\\Geological\\BGS Hard Substrates_WGS84.lyr\tGIS and Spatial Data Team       • In 2010, BGS and JNCC produced the UKSeaMap 2010 substrate layer containing the 4 broad EUNIS sediment types plus rock o The dataset has joint ownership and BGS IPR were happy for us to supply the data to anyone who made a formal request via email   • In 2011, BGS published DigHardSubstrate250 dataset which is a further improvement on MB0103 Made avaiable as an extra for people who licence digi map products from BGS  Andrew Jeffery emailing Helen Lili from JNCC to find this information- JNCC  were currently letting a contract to replace these datasets,and were written in to be made OGL.\tThe British Geological Survey (BGS) is a UK provider of geoscientific data, information and knowledge. Natural Resources Wales has licenced access to a number of BGS datasets. This particular spatial data is a collation of licenced data from BGS for offshore and UK Continental Shelf (UKCS) geology.\tBritish Geological Survey (BGS)-DEFRA (Department for Environment, Food and Rural Affairs)\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2026-01-07T16:52:03.000Z\tMonica Jones\t-\tPublic record\n17143\tEXT_DS120011\t2024-05-28T12:14:10.701Z\t620\tUnassessed\tEditable\tWestern Power: Utilities Electricity Components  (3rd Party Data)\t© Western Power Distribution.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313230303131\tX:\\Utilities\\Electricity\\Western Power Poles.LYR x:\\Utilities\\Electricity\\Western Power Underground Powerlines.lyr  x:\\Utilities\\Electricity\\Western Power Overhead Powerlines.lyr  x:\\Utilities\\Electricity\\Western Power Towers.lyr  x:\\Utilities\\Electricity\\Western Power Substations.lyr\tGIS Service Desk: Louise Harris\tThis collation contains information around the location of the electrical components owned or managed by Western Power.  This is a collation of a limited range of data owned by Western Power, downloaded from Western Power’s DataPortal and licenced to Natural Resources Wales (NRW) for internal re-use for specific purposes only, i.e. network planning and design. Currently this data will not be updated.  The data must not be used for asset location/health and safety plans when conducting operational field work and to prevent accidental damage to the assets. Please refer to www.lsbud.co.uk to download pdf plans intended for this type of use.\tWestern Power\t2022-01-17\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T12:14:04.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17137\tEXT_DS120174\t2024-05-28T12:14:10.212Z\t836\tUnassessed\tEditable\tDefra: National Atmospheric Emissions Inventory (NAEI) (3rd party data)\t© DEFRA Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and owners copyright. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313230313734\tX:\\Resource Management\\Air Quality\tGIS Service Desk\tThe UK National Atmospheric Emissions Inventory (NAEI) is developed and maintained by Ricardo Energy \u0026amp; Environment, in collaboration with Aether, CEH, and Gluckman Consulting. The NAEI is funded by the Department for Business, Energy and Industrial Strategy (BEIS), Department for Environment, Food and Rural Affairs (Defra), the Scottish Government, the Welsh Government and the Northern Ireland Department of Agriculture, Environment and Rural Affairs.   Natural Resources Wales (NRW) obtains the spatial layers from some of the datasets associated with the NAEI under licence from Defra. NRW only gets the Wales area for the majority of the dataset, the acception being the Defra air quality management areas (2015). This includes the following:  - Modelled Air Quality Concentrations for 2008, 2009, 2010, 2011, 2012, 2013, 2015, 2015 and 2016 - Modelled Air Quality Emissions 2008, 2009 and 2010 - Air Quality Management Areas  - Defra Air Quality Management Areas 2015 - Defra Nitrogen Dioxide Concentrations - Defra Ozone Concentrations - Defra Particulate Matter Concentrations\tDEFRA (Department for Environment, Food and Rural Affairs)\t2020-10-22\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T09:13:42.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17142\tEXT_DS120344\t2024-05-28T12:14:10.624Z\t756\tUnassessed\tEditable\tSevern Trent: Utilities Data (3rd Party Data)\t© Severn Trent Water Ltd.  NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Attribution Statement: © Severn Trent Water\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313230333434\tX:\\Utilities\\Water\\Severn Trent Sewer Lines.lyr  X:\\Utilities\\Water\\Severn Trent Sewer point.lyr  X:\\Utilities\\Water\\Severn Trent Water Mains.lyr  X:\\Utilities\\Water\\Severn Trent Water Point.lyr  X:\\Utilities\\Water\\Severn Trent Water Mains Operational Area.lyr  X:\\Utilities\\Water\\Severn Trent Sewer Operational Area.lyr\tGIS and Spatial Data Team\tThis is a collation of datasets detailing the extent and location of water utilities owned or managed by Severn Trent Water plc which is the parent company for several Water Companies (Severn Trent Water, Hafren Dyfrdwy and Severn Trent Services).  This dataset only covers the area under management of Hafren Dyfrdwy (Severn Dee) Water Company. Natural Resources Wales (NRW) has access to this collation for internal use only.\tSevern Trent Water Ltd\t2021-06-21\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T12:09:12.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17133\tEXT_DS120572\t2024-05-28T12:14:10.203Z\t1023\tUnassessed\tEditable\tDudley Stamp Land Utilisation Survey for Wales 1933-1949\t© L. Dudley Stamp/Geographical Publications Ltd, Audrey N. Clark, Environment Agency/DEFRA and Great Britain Historical GIS. NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313230353732\tX:\\Physical\\Landscape\\Dudley Stamp Land utilisation survey 1933 to 49.lyr\tGIS Service Desk Jonathan Rothwell, Terrestrial Mapping Specialist, Terrestrial Ecosystems Team / Terrestrial Ecosystems Group, NRW Barnaby Letheren, Specialist Advisor Enterprise Data Management, Evidence Knowledge and Advice, NRW\tThis spatial dataset - for the Wales geographic area only - is held by Natural Resources Wales (NRW). The dataset is a digital version of the 1 inch to 1 mile \u0027Dudley Stamp Maps\u0027 that provide a pre-war land survey. The Environment Agency carried out the digitisation of the survey data for all of Great Britain.\tEnvironment Agency (EA)-Various\t1949-12-31\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2026-01-19T16:24:52.000Z\tMonica Jones\t-\tPublic record\n17148\tEXT_DS120645\t2024-05-28T12:14:10.803Z\t850\tUnassessed\tEditable\tNetwork Rail: Level Crossings (3rd Party Data)\t© Network Rail. Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and owners copyright. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose. Attribution Statement: Information provided by Network Rail - https://www.networkrail.co.uk/transparency/datasets/\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313230363435\tX:\\Transport\\Railway\\Network Rail level crossings.lyr\tExternal data owner - Network Rail  The request for this data came from: Nicolas Pritchard, Flood Risk Strategy Officer, KSP - Sustainable Communities Internal Custodian GIS and Spatial Data Services\tNational Rail have more than 6,300 level crossings on their rail network, with multiple crossing types at some sites. They have a legal duty to assess, manage and control the risk for every crossing. Natural Resources Wales have a welsh and boarders cut of this spatial dataset on the corporate data stores.\tNational Rail\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2026-02-26T15:12:40.000Z\tMonica Jones\t-\tPublic record\n17136\tEXT_DS120732\t2024-05-28T12:14:10.234Z\t480\tUnassessed\tEditable\tEnvironment Agency (EA): KiWQM English Stations (3rd Party Data)\t© Environment Agency  NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313230373332\tX:\\Monitoring\\Sampling Points\\KiWQM English Stations.lyr\tGIS Service Desk\tThis is the English locations for stations or monitoring locations held within WISKI\u0027s Water Quality Module - KiWQM. This data is owned by the Environment Agency and comes in as part of a data exchange agreement.\tEnvironment Agency (EA)\t2022-03-03\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T12:00:53.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17141\tEXT_DS120801\t2024-05-28T12:14:10.737Z\t718\tUnassessed\tEditable\tPlantlife International: Important Arable Plant Area Data for Wales (3rd Party Data)\t© 2017 Plantlife International. All Rights Reserved. NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly. The Plantlife logo must be included in all publications and one copy of all publications and reports using data supplied by Plantlife International shall be supplied free of charge to Plantlife International.  Attribution Statement: Copyright © 2018 Plantlife International. All Rights Reserved.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313230383031\tX:\\Biological\\Plant Life\\Plant Life Arable plant species point.lyr  X:\\Biological\\Plant Life\\Plant Life Arable plant species poly.lyr  X:\\Biological\\Plant Life\\Plant Life IAPA richness.lyr  X:\\Biological\\Plant Life\\Plant Life IAPA stat tetrad grid.lyr\tInternal Custodian: Claire Burrows, Lead Specialist Advisor, Terrestrial Ecosystems \u0026amp; Species, Terrestrial Ecosystems \u0026amp; Species Team External Contact: Beth Halski, Biological Data and GIS Manager, Plantlife International - The Wild Plant Conservation Charity Email: beth.halski@plantlife.org.uk\tPlantlife International collects and holds a large quantity of data on plants and habitats of conservation importance throughout the UK from a network of individuals and organisations. The Important Arable Plant Area (IAPA) are based on the presence of particular threatened species, exceptional plant assemblages and priority habitats and this method is used to highlight arable farmland in the UK of three levels of importance: Sites of European Importance; Sites of National Importance; Sites of County Importance. The datasets include: - The Welsh Important Arable Plant Area (IAPA) Status Tetrad data contains information at the 2x2 km scale for the presence of individual UK IAPA species which has been totalled to provide the IAPA score for each tetrad. This has been assessed against the broad-soil present in each tetrad to conclude whether each tetrad is of County, National or European Importance for UK IAPA plants and the number of rare and threatened arable plants (Criteria A) has been summed. - The Wales Arable Plant Species Data, which contains information on 30 arable plants that are rare and threatened in Wales. Each species has either or both a point or polygon Shapefile containing location and date information. - The Wales Field IAPA and Richness dataset contains information of the presence of each UK IAPA species at a field level. This includes the data of the last survey for each field, the last time when each species was recorded in the field, the UK IAPA score for the field, a count of the IAPA species in each field (species richness) and the area of each field. - The Wales vice-counties IAPA map contains information of the Important Arable Plant Area (IAPA) score for each Welsh vice-county.\tPlantlife\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-03-27T09:10:53.000Z\tnobody nobody\t-\tPublic record\n17138\tEXT_DS121393\t2024-05-28T12:14:10.243Z\t806\tUnassessed\tEditable\tJNCC Management Units for Cetaceans in UK waters (3rd Party Data)\t© Joint Nature Conservation Committee Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and owners copyright. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose. If you re-use this data you must acknowledge the source of the information in your product or application by including or linking to the following attribution statement: \\Contains JNCC © copyright and database right 2015. Boundaries defined through discussions of the Inter-Agency Marine Mammal Working Group (IAMMWG).\\\"\"\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231333933\tX:\\Biological\\Species sourced by NRW\\Marine\\Cetaceans\\ X:\\Biological\\Species sourced by NRW\\Marine\\Cetaceans\\Bottlenose dolphin management units.lyr  X:\\Biological\\Species sourced by NRW\\Marine\\Cetaceans\\Common dolphin management units.lyr  X:\\Biological\\Species sourced by NRW\\Marine\\Cetaceans\\Harbour porpoise management units.lyr  X:\\Biological\\Species sourced by NRW\\Marine\\Cetaceans\\Minke whale management units.lyr  X:\\Biological\\Species sourced by NRW\\Marine\\Cetaceans\\Rissos dolphin management units.lyr  X:\\Biological\\Species sourced by NRW\\Marine\\Cetaceans\\Whitebeaked dolphin management units.lyr  X:\\Biological\\Species sourced by NRW\\Marine\\Cetaceans\\Whitesided dolphin management units.lyr  Data is stored in the 3rd Party geodatabase.\tTom Stringell, Senior Marine Mammal Ecologist (tom.stringell@cyfoethnaturiolcymru.gov.uk) Ceri Morris,  Marine Mammal Ecologist (ceri.morris@cyfoethnaturiolcymru.gov.uk)       The data can be downloaded from: http://jncc.defra.gov.uk/page-6943 which also has some more information attached as well.\tThis is a collation of spatial datasets detailing the extent and location of the final agreed Management Units (MUs) for the seven most common cetacean species in UK waters. This dataset is wholly owned by JNCC and Natural Resources Wales (NRW) can access the data through an Open Government Licence.   Almost all species of cetacean found in UK waters are part of larger biological populations whose range extends into the waters of other European States and/or the High Seas. Equally, the number of individuals present at any one time may be only a small proportion of those that make use of UK waters throughout the year. In order to obtain the best conservation outcomes for many species, it is necessary to consider the division of populations into smaller management units. Management Units (MUs) should be based on our best understanding of the structure of biological populations and any ecological differentiation within such populations (as outlined in the Appendix). However, the boundaries between MUs may be determined by either political boundaries (e.g. the boundary between Ireland and the UK) or the management of human activities (e.g. ICES divisions used for the collection of fisheries data and management of fisheries). As far as possible, the management units defined in this report have been based on the presence of known populations, with divisions proposed on the basis of ecological evidence and/or divisions used for the management of human activities. Therefore, whilst being consistent with the best biological understanding, an MU refers to the animals of a particular species in a geographical area to which management of human activities is also applied. As such, these MUs comprise partially artificial divisions of often slightly uncertain biological populations.\tJoint Nature Conservation Committee (JNCC)\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2026-02-26T15:13:51.000Z\tMonica Jones\t-\tPublic record\n17146\tEXT_DS121542\t2024-05-28T12:14:10.671Z\t631\tUnassessed\tEditable\tScottish Power: Utilities Electricity Components (3rd Party Data)\t© Scottish Power NRW does NOT grant permission to 3rd Parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the owner directly. Attribution Statement: © SP Power Systems Ltd\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231353432\tX:\\Utilities\\Electricity\\Scottish Power De-Energised Overhead Lines.lyr  X:\\Utilities\\Electricity\\Scottish Power De-Energised Underground Cables.lyr  X:\\Utilities\\Electricity\\Scottish Power Overhead Lines.lyr  X:\\Utilities\\Electricity\\Scottish Power Poles.lyr  X:\\Utilities\\Electricity\\Scottish Power Substations.lyr  X:\\Utilities\\Electricity\\Scottish Power Towers.lyr  X:\\Utilities\\Electricity\\Scottish Power Undergound Cables.lyr\tGIS and Spatial Data Team\tThis collation of datasets is owned by Scottish Power. The data have been licenced to Natural Resources Wales for internal use only. Scottish Power own and manage a number of electrical components, both on and underground, helping to supply electricity to households across Wales.\tScottish Power (SP Power Systems Ltd)\t2021-03-05\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T12:14:15.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17140\tEXT_DS121553\t2024-05-28T12:14:10.296Z\t897\tUnassessed\tEditable\tEuropean Environment Agency (EEA): CORINE Land Cover (CLC) 2012 - Peat and Urban (3rd Party Data)\t©  European Environment Agency (EEA) - Copernicus Data Services. Data may be re-used under provision and in line with the terms outlined by the European Environment Agency. Attribution Statement: The data were produced by the Copernicus Data Services with funding by the European Union.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231353533\tX:\\Flood Risk\\Working with Natural Processes\\Corine Land Cover 2012 Peat.lyr  X:\\Flood Risk\\Working with Natural Processes\\Corine Land Cover 2012 Urban.lyr\tMetadata Contact: GIS and Data Services Team. Internal Contact: Mark Pugh - Flood risk management  External responsibility lies with - European Environment Agency (EEA) under the framework of the Copernicus programme - copernicus@eea.europa.eu\tThese dataset was produced under the Copernicus Initial Operations (GIO) which forms part of the Copernicus Data Services in the European Environment Agency. Natural Resources Wales (NRW) has access to these datasets under an open licence. CORINE Land Cover (CLC) was specified to standardize data collection on land in Europe to support environmental policy development.  Natural Resources Wales has access to the following CORINE Land Cover 2012 Datasets: - Peat - Urban\tEuropean Environment Agency (EEA)\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-07-08T08:21:13.000Z\tnobody nobody\t-\tPublic record\n17134\tEXT_DS121601\t2024-05-28T12:14:10.101Z\t400\tUnassessed\tEditable\tCadw: Designated Shipwreck Sites (3rd Party Data)\t© Cadw Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and Cadw\u0027s copyright. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose. Attribution Statement: Designated Historic Asset GIS Data, The Welsh Historic Environment Service (Cadw), 2018, licensed under the Open Government Licence http://www.nationalarchives.gov.uk/doc/open-government-licence/version/3/\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231363031\tX:\\Designations\\CADW\\Designated Shipwreck Sites.lyr\tInternal Custodian: GIS and Spatial Data Team\tNatural Resources of Wales (NRW) are supplied a number of historic and cultural datasets under a licence from Cadw. Cadw is the Welsh Government’s historic environment service working for an accessible and well-protected historic environment for Wales. They were set up with the aim of conserving Wales’s heritage, helping people understand and care about their history and helping to sustain the distinctive character of Wales.  \u0027Wrecks\u0027 are designated under the 1973 Protection of Wrecks Act. There are numerous maritime wrecks in the seas around Wales. Although all of them have historic value, six currently have legal protection. These six are known as \u0027designated wrecks\u0027 or \u0027protected wrecks\u0027.\tCadw. Welsh Historic Monuments\t2021-03-25\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T12:23:56.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17153\tEXT_DS121606\t2024-05-28T12:14:11.076Z\t9\tUnassessed\tEditable\tNational Trust Data (3rd Party Data)\t© National Trust Use Constraints for these datasets vary depending on the nature of the dataset. Attribution Statement: National Trust\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231363036\tVarious Locations (see specific metadata for further details) Spatial Data is held on the X Drive.\tJoe Bloggs\tIn Natural Resources Wales we obtain a variety of data from the National Trust. These relate to a wide variety of topics, such as coastal management, land and property ownership and species data.\tNational Trust\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2026-02-26T15:14:42.000Z\tMonica Jones\t-\tPrivate record\n17149\tEXT_DS121609\t2024-05-28T12:14:10.834Z\t514\tUnassessed\tEditable\tOffice of National Statistics (ONS): Spatial Data (3rd Party Data)\t© Office of National Statistics (ONS) Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and owners copyright. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose. Attribution Statement: Contains National Statistics data © Crown copyright and database right [2015]\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231363039\tX:\\Social Economic\\Office of National Statistics  to see a variety of data layers.   For Admin boundaries:  x:\\Basemapping\\Admin Boundaries\\NUTS Level 1.lyr ,  x:\\Basemapping\\Admin Boundaries\\NUTS Level 2.lyr ,  x:\\Basemapping\\Admin Boundaries\\NUTS Level 3.lyr\tInternal Custodian: GIS Service Desk\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW) obtains a large variety of spatial data from the Office of National Statistics (ONS). The majority of the dataset obtained from ONS are for Wales plus border areas, however some datasets do cover the whole of England and Wales.\tOffice of National Statistics (ONS)\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-03-27T09:17:32.000Z\tnobody nobody\t-\tPublic record\n17135\tEXT_DS121611\t2024-05-28T12:14:10.166Z\t2113\tUnassessed\tEditable\tCoal Authority: Past and Current Mining Data (3rd Party Data)\t© The Coal Authority Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and owners copyright.  It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose.  Attribution Statement: © The Coal Authority\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231363131\t\tNo current data custodian identified  Internal Custodian: GIS Service Desk  External Contact: Louise Tipper, Information Management, The Coal Authority mailing and physical address: 200 Lichfield Lane Mansfield Nottinghamshire NG18 4RG England +44(0) 345 762 6848       Louise Tipper, Information Management, The Coal Authority mailing and physical address: 200 Lichfield Lane Mansfield Nottinghamshire NG18 4RG England +44(0) 345 762 6848\tThe Coal Authority (CA) works to resolve the impacts of mining, by managing the effects of past coal mining and dealing with mine water pollution and other mining legacy issues. This spatial dataset provided to Natural Resources Wales by the CA under and Open Government Licence, is available through a Web Mapping Service to enable analysis of data. The datasets are provide in raster format and does not include full vector information. Datasets available via WMS include:  - Mine Entry - Abandoned Mines Catalogue - Development High Risk Area - Surface Coal Resource Areas - Mine Entry Potential Zone of Influence - Fissures and Breaklines - Surface Mining (Past and Current) - Past Shallow Coal Mine Workings - Coal Outcrops - NE Mining \u0026amp; Groundwater Constraints - Coal Mining Reporting Area\tCoal Authority\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-07-08T08:21:13.000Z\tnobody nobody\t-\tPublic record\n17150\tEXT_DS121613\t2024-05-28T12:14:10.835Z\t286\tUnassessed\tEditable\tJNCC: Offshore Special Area of Conservation (SAC) (3rd Party Data)\t© JNCC Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and owners copyright.  It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose.   The following Attribution Statement should be used: © Crown copyright. All rights reserved. Joint Nature Conservation Committee Support Co [2018]\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231363133\tX:\\Designations\\JNCC\\JNCC Offshore SAC WGS84.lyr\tKeith Jones, Spatial Evidence Manager, Evidence, Knowledge and Advice        data downloads: http://jncc.defra.gov.uk/protectedsites/SACselection/gis_data/terms_conditions.asp\tThe spatial dataset containing the boundaries of Special Areas of Conservation designated in Welsh waters beyond 12 nautical miles offshore. The dataset is owned by Joint Nature Conservation Committee (JNCC), and Natural Resources Wales (NRW) have access to this dataset under an Open Government Licence.\tJoint Nature Conservancy Committee (JNCC)\t2020-02-14\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-03-21T10:34:59.000Z\tnobody nobody\t-\tPublic record\n17147\tEXT_DS121615\t2024-05-28T12:14:10.676Z\t651\tUnassessed\tEditable\tJNCC: Offshore Special Protection Area (SPA) (3rd Party Data)\t© JNCC Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and owners copyright.  It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose.  The following Attribution Statement should be used: © Crown copyright. All rights reserved. Joint Nature Conservation Committee Support Co [2018]\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231363135\tX:\\Designations\\JNCC\\JNCC Offshore SPA WGS84.lyr\tKeith Jones, Spatial Evidence Manager, Evidence, Knowledge and Advice\tThe spatial dataset containing the boundaries of Special Protection Area designated in Welsh waters beyond 12 nautical miles offshore. The dataset is owned by Joint Nature Conservation Committee (JNCC), and Natural Resources Wales (NRW) have access to this dataset under an Open Government Licence.\tJoint Nature Conservancy Committee (JNCC)\t2018-06-13\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-03-21T10:52:38.000Z\tnobody nobody\t-\tPublic record\n17144\tEXT_DS121617\t2024-05-28T12:14:10.646Z\t4748\tUnassessed\tEditable\tSites of Importance for Nature Conservation (SINC) (3rd Party Data)\t© Local Authority\u0027s NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231363137\tX:\\Designations\\Local Authorities\\Sites of Interest for Nature Conservation (SINC).lyr  X:\\Designations\\Local Authorities\\Wrexham Wildlife Sites.lyr  X:\\Designations\\Local Authorities\\Flint Wildlife Sites.lyr  X:\\Designations\\Local Authorities\\Denbigh Wildlife Sites.lyr  X:\\Designations\\Local Authorities\\Conwy Wildlife Sites.lyr\tKeith Jones GIS team (keith.jones@cyfoethnaturiolcymru.gov.uk)\tThis is a spatial dataset detailing the extent and location of the boundaries of all Sites of Interest for Nature Conservation (SINCs), also known as Wildlife Sites, in Wales, owned by the Local Authorities and licenced to Natural Resources Wales. SINC\u0027s are intended to provide comprehensive coverage of sites of nature conservation value. SINC\u0027s do not have statutory protection (unless they are also SSSIs or LNRs), but local authorities are expected to take account of the need to protect them in deciding their planning and development policies. SINC\u0027s sites are designated by local authorities in cooperation with local wildlife trusts and other local stakeholders. Information includes site name, site description, reason for designation, total area (ha) and which local record centre area the site is in.\t\t2020-03-27\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T11:49:20.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17145\tEXT_DS121619\t2024-05-28T12:14:10.760Z\t1030\tUnassessed\tEditable\tWelsh Government: Environmental Noise Mapping (3rd Party Data)\t© Crown Copyright: Welsh Government Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and owners copyright.  It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231363139\tX:\\Resource Management\\Environmental Noise Mapping\\\tGIS Spatial Team: Keith Jones (keith.jones@cyfoethnaturiolcymru.gov.uk\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW) holds data provided by Welsh Government giving information on noise maps for major roads across Wales, and for industry in our largest towns and cities. Noise data for all the sound level contours calculated in 2017 are provided in 5-decibel \\A-weighted\\\" contour bands. The noise maps for Wales are based on calculation rather than measurement. They should only be considered a starting point for identifying areas that need priority action.\"\tWelsh Government\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-07-08T08:21:14.000Z\tnobody nobody\t-\tPublic record\n17152\tEXT_DS121623\t2024-05-28T12:14:11.092Z\t676\tUnassessed\tEditable\tNational Trust: Neptune Coastline Campaign (3rd Party Data)\t© National Trust Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and copyright of the owners.  It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose. Attribution Statement: © National Trust\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231363233\tX:\\Physical\\Landscape\\National Trust\\Neptune Coastline Campaign Land Use 2014.lyr  X:\\Physical\\Landscape\\National Trust\\Neptune Coastline Campaign Land Use 1965.lyr\tInternal Custodian – Nicola Rimington, Lead Specialist Advisor, Marine and Coastal Physical Processes and Coastal Management, Marine and Coastal Policy \u0026amp; Planning Team GIS and Spatial Dataset\tThese spatial datasets details over 50 years of land use change around the coast of Wales in areas owned by the National Trust. Natural Resources Wales (NRW) has access to this data through an Open Government Licence (OGL).\tNational Trust\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T12:14:14.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17175\tEXT_DS121635\t2024-05-28T12:15:05.642Z\t2\tUnassessed\tEditable\tSea Visibility From Land (3rd Party Data)\t© Marine Management Organisation Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and owners copyright. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231363335\tX:\\Physical\\Seascapes\\Sea Visibility From Land.lyr\tJohn Briggs, Landscape Architect (john.briggs@cyfoethnaturiolcymru.gov.uk) Steven Newstead, Data and GIS for SMNR Officer (steven.newstead@cyfoethnaturiolcymru.gov.uk)       MMO metadata found here: https://data.gov.uk/dataset/6f46c292-4eab-4870-95af-39aecc9ab3c2/marine-management-organisation-visibility-of-sea-from-land\tThe Marine Management Organisation (MMO) has produced a dataset which models the sea visibility from land to understand the extent of intervisibility (the ability to see in a direct line of sight from one position on the earth\u0027s surface to another). This dataset is a clip (Wales only) from the MMO\u0027s full dataset that is available for download on the governments spatial data catalogue under an OGL licence (see resource locator).\tMarine Management Organisation (MMO)\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2026-02-26T15:15:26.000Z\tMonica Jones\t-\tPrivate record\n17178\tEXT_DS121638\t2024-05-28T12:15:05.668Z\t597\tUnassessed\tEditable\tCefas: Spawning and Nursery Grounds of Selected Fish in UK Waters (3rd Party Data)\t© CEFAS Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and owners copyright.  It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231363338\tX:\\Biological\\Marine Habitat\\Fisheries habitat and sensitivity\\CEFAS\\CEFAS Fisheries nursery grounds WGS84.lyr  X:\\Biological\\Marine Habitat\\Fisheries habitat and sensitivity\\CEFAS\\CEFAS Fisheries nursery points WGS84.lyr  X:\\Biological\\Marine Habitat\\Fisheries habitat and sensitivity\\CEFAS\\CEFAS Fisheries spawning grounds WGS84.lyr  X:\\Biological\\Marine Habitat\\Fisheries habitat and sensitivity\\CEFAS\\CEFAS Fisheries spawning points WGS84.lyr\tInternal Contact: Colin Charman, Lead Specialist Advisor – Marine Fisheries, Marine \u0026amp; Coastal Policy \u0026amp; Planning Team\tThis is a third party spatial dataset detailing the extent and location of spawning and nursery ground of selected fish in UK waters. NRW holds data from Cefas on the spawning and nursery grounds of selected fish in UK waters on a OGL licence.  NB While we have the data set under general licence, it is preferable users go to Cefas direct for the dataset.  This dataset was created by Cefas for additional analyses to complement the original maps produced in \u0027Coull, K.A., Johnstone, R., and S.I. Rogers. 1998. Fisheries Sensitivity Maps in British Waters\u0027 (published and distributed by UKOOA Ltd.) and to: (a)  Provide supporting evidence for the maps of spawning and nursery grounds; (b) Provide some of the more recent data that has become available since the original Fisheries Sensitivity Maps were produced; (c)  Increase the number of species for which maps are available;(d) Plot the spawning areas as rectangles, so that the user is more likely to infer that the boundaries of such areas are not fixed delineations between spawning and non-spawning areas; (e) Provide more information on those grounds likely to be of greater importance to the stock(s).\tCentre for Environmental Fisheries and Aquatic Sciences (CEFAS)\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-07-08T08:21:14.000Z\tnobody nobody\t-\tPublic record\n17176\tEXT_DS121643\t2024-05-28T12:15:05.677Z\t543\tUnassessed\tEditable\tCefas: Shellfish Classification Zones (3rd Party Data)\t© CEFAS Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and owners copyright.  It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231363433\tX:\\Biological\\Marine Habitat\\Fisheries habitat and sensitivity\\CEFAS\\CEFAS Shellfish Classification Zones 2015.lyr  X:\\Biological\\Marine Habitat\\Fisheries habitat and sensitivity\\CEFAS\\CEFAS Shellfish Classification Zones Pre 2015.lyr  X:\\Biological\\Marine Habitat\\Fisheries habitat and sensitivity\\CEFAS\\CEFAS Shellfish Classification Zones.lyr\tMetadata - Geospatial Team  Internal Contact: Rowland Sharp, Senior Advisor, SW Area Operations (Marine)\tThis is a third party spatial dataset detailing the extent and location of Shellfish Classification Zones of England and Wales. Natural Resources Wales (NRW) has access to this data from Cefas under an Open Government Licence (OGL). NRW holds historic versions of the data as well as up to date versions of the data. For instance: - CEFAS Shellfish Classification Zones 2015 (SWF Hygine) - CEFAS Shellfish Classification Zones pre 2015 (Bivalve) - CEFAS Shellfish Classification Zones\tCentre for Environmental Fisheries and Aquatic Sciences (CEFAS)\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T12:17:42.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17179\tEXT_DS121652\t2024-05-28T12:15:05.694Z\t630\tUnassessed\tEditable\tSEA 6 Inshore Sector Geophysical Report Summer 2004 OSIRIS Project (3rd Party Data)\tNRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231363532\tStored in Project Number 170 media number 500\tDave Tavner - Marine Mapping Scientist, Evidence Analysis  OSIRIS Projects Old Contact Details - this became part of BibbyHydromap in 2012. Lockside House, 80 Eastham Village Road Eastham Wirral CH62 0AW Tel. 0151 328 1120. Fax / ISDN 0151 328 1139 e-mail:  enquires@osirisprojects.co.uk\tThe region encompassed by the strategic environmental assessment No. 6 (SEA 6) represents the central Irish Sea, with specific focus given to the areas of Liverpool Bay and Tremadog Bay. At the onset of the contract, the broad aim of the survey was to acquire data representative of the geology, bathymetry and ecology of Tremadog Bay and surrounding areas. Osiris Projects had been contracted by Geotek Ltd, on behalf of the Department of Trade and Industry (DTI), to undertake a programme of shallow marine survey work as part of the SEA 6 initiative.  This work was predominantly focussed on the Tremadog bay area of the Irish Sea as part of the inshore sector of the SEA 6 region.  Offshore Survey and Engineering (OSAE) performed survey work in the offshore sector of the SEA 6 region. The scope of the work performed by Osiris Projects as part of the SEA 6 inshore sector included the following elements: - Geophysical survey work using side scan sonar and sub-bottom profiler - Hydrographic survey work using swathe bathymetry and single beam bathymetry - Benthic survey work, including grab sampling and photographic imagery\tDepartment for Business, Energy and Industrial Strategy\t2004-08-09\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-03-07T15:43:50.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17177\tEXT_DS121661\t2024-05-28T12:15:05.626Z\t2352\tUnassessed\tEditable\tAerial Photography Great Britain (APGB): Welsh Digital Aerial Photography and DSM/DTM models supplied by GetMapping and Bluesky International Limited (3rd Party Data)\tNRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly. This dataset has been licenced for Internal Use to NRW and Appointed Contractors only. Copyright Statement for internal use: © Getmapping Plc and Bluesky International Limited [yyyy].\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231363631\tService: X:\\Basemapping\\Air Photos\\WMS services\\Getmapping 12.5cm WMS 2009 to 2019.lyr  X:\\Basemapping\\Air Photos\\WMS services\\Getmapping 25cm WMS 2009 to 2019.lyr   Data - Aerial Photos: X:\\Basemapping\\Air Photos\\Aerial Images 2000.lyr  X:\\Basemapping\\Air Photos\\Air photos index\\Air photo index 2001.lyr  X:\\Basemapping\\Air Photos\\Aerial Images 2009.lyr  X:\\Basemapping\\Air Photos\\Air photos index\\Air photo index 2009.lyr  X:\\Basemapping\\Air Photos\\Aerial Images 2013-14.lyr  X:\\Basemapping\\Air Photos\\Air photos index\\Air photo index 2013.lyr  X:\\Basemapping\\Air Photos\\Air photos index\\Air photo index 2013 14.lyr  X:\\Basemapping\\Air Photos\\Aerial Images 2013-14_NIR.lyr  X:\\Basemapping\\Air Photos\\Aerial Images 2013 to 2017.lyr  X:\\Basemapping\\Air Photos\\Air photos index\\Air photo index 2013 to 2017.lyr  X:\\Basemapping\\Air Photos\\Aerial Images 2017.lyr  X:\\Basemapping\\Air Photos\\Air photos index\\Air photo index 2013 to 2018.lyr  X:\\Basemapping\\Air Photos\\Aerial Images 2013 to 2018.lyr  X:\\Basemapping\\Air Photos\\Aerial Images 2013 to 2019.lyr   Data - DEM 5m (single band 32 bit float GeoTIFF) X:\\Basemapping\\Height\\APGB_5m_DEM.lyr  (Also available in Z:\\Processing\\Knowledge Data \u0026amp; Information Management\\1 - Geospatial\\APGB_5m_DTM\\Output\\Wales_5m_DEM.tif)  X:\\Basemapping\\Air Photos\\APGB Services\\Aerial Photography 12.5cm 2025.lyr X:\\Basemapping\\Air Photos\\APGB Services\\Aerial Photography 25cm 2025.lyr X:\\Basemapping\\Air Photos\\Air photos index\\APGB Air Photos Indexes\\Indexing for 12.5cm 2025.lyr X:\\Basemapping\\Air Photos\\Air photos index\\APGB Air Photos Indexes\\Indexing for 25cm 2025.lyr\tGIS and Spatial Data Team\tGetMapping and Bluesky International supplied NRW this data under licence for the following years; 2000, 2009, 2013-14, 2013-17, 2015, 2017, 2018, 2020, 2021 and 2025.   In 2006 the Aerial Images were produced by Cowi (see metadata number 121879).    Aerial Photography Great Britain (APGB) is a raster dataset containing aerial imagery produced by Getmapping and Bluesky International. Natural Resources Wales (NRW) has access to the Welsh extent of this dataset as a member of the APGB. The licencing conditions mean that NRW can only use this data for internal use.   APGB comprises aerial photography and height data (2m DSM, 5m DTM, 5m contours), for government. The data itself is captured, processed and delivered by Bluesky International Ltd and Getmapping Plc, two of the premier aerial survey companies in the UK, on a rolling three year update programme.  This date is available as a service as well as holding the actual data.\tBlueksy International Ltd.-Getmapping\t2018-12-11\tpublication\tnull\thttps://www.apgb.co.uk/products\t2025-10-23T14:30:48.000Z\tRachel Morris\t-\tPublic record\n17173\tEXT_DS121663\t2024-05-28T12:15:05.631Z\t810\tUnassessed\tEditable\tWelsh Government: Active Travel Approved Routes (3rd Party Data)\t© Crown Copyright: Welsh Government. © Crown Copyright and database right. Joint Ownership between Welsh Government and Ordnance Survey. NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231363633\tX:\\Recreation and Access\\Active Travel\\Active Travel Approved Routes.lyr\tGIS and Spatial Data Team\tThis is a spatial dataset containing the location of existing active travel routes for walking and cycling. Natural Resources Wales (NRW) obtained a copy of this dataset from Lle, where is has been published by Welsh Government and made available under a Public Sector Mapping Agreement.  Please note - this dataset contains spatial errors with some data being mapped in the wrong place.\tOrdnance Survey (OS)-Welsh Government\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T12:18:17.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17180\tEXT_DS121664\t2024-05-28T12:15:05.880Z\t601\tUnassessed\tEditable\tWelsh Government: Active Travel Designated Localities (Wales) (3rd Party Data)\t© Crown Copyright: Welsh Government. Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and owners copyright.  It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231363634\tX:\\Recreation and Access\\Active Travel\\Active Travel Designated Localities.lyr\tGIS and Spatial Data Team\tThis is a spatial dataset containing the location of designated localities in relation to active travel routes. Natural Resources Wales (NRW) have been granted access to this dataset from Welsh Government under and Open Government Licence.\tWelsh Government\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T13:06:29.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17165\tEXT_DS121665\t2024-05-28T12:15:05.157Z\t870\tUnassessed\tEditable\tAPBMer: Data from the Atlas of UK Marine Renewable Energy Resources (3rd Party Data)\tNRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Should NRW wish to publish material from the Atlas then please include the following citation:  \"Atlas of UK Marine Renewable Energy Resources. 2008. ABPmer. Date of access (30 March 2017) http://www.renewables-atlas.info/   All data remains Crown Copyright and figures using the Atlas data or images should include the statement:  \"Reproduced from http://www.renewables-atlas.info/ © Crown Copyright\"\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231363635\tX:\\Flood Risk\\Coastal Erosion Risk\\ABPMer Tidal stream WGS84.lyr  X:\\Flood Risk\\Coastal Erosion Risk\\ABPMer Wave height WGS84.lyr\tGIS and Spatial Data Team\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW) has accesses to some of the datasets which form part of the Atlas of UK Marine Renewables Energy Resources, which is owned by ABPmer. Working with major marine data holders, Met Office and Proudman Oceanographic Laboratory (POL), ABPmer’s Data Team managed the delivery of the Atlas bringing the data together into GIS data layers (maps). NRW has access to this data through a data licencing agreement, which is signed upon download.\tABPmer\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T12:18:15.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17170\tEXT_DS121666\t2024-05-28T12:15:05.424Z\t637\tUnassessed\tEditable\tBritish Mountaineering Council (BMC) Coastal Climbing (3rd Party Data)\t© British Mountaineering Council 2008 NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231363636\tX:\\Recreation and Access\\MCRA\\BMC coastal climbing lines.lyr  X:\\Recreation and Access\\MCRA\\BMC coastal climbing points.lyr\tGIS and Spatial Data Team\tThis dataset was obtained in 2009 as part of the Marine Coastal Recreation Audit (MCRA).  It is thought that this data is owned by the British Mountaineering Council (BMC) and was obtained by the contractors for Natural Resources Wales, under a licence. However there is also  potential that this product was derived from the BMC Data.  This dataset is for internal use only as part of work for the MCRA. For a more up to date version of the data which is advised if you are planning to use the data, please contact the spatial data team, who can obtain a copy from the BMC.\tBritish Mountaineering Council\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-04-17T09:58:05.000Z\tnobody nobody\t-\tPublic record\n17172\tEXT_DS121667\t2024-05-28T12:15:05.631Z\t1101\tUnassessed\tEditable\tCanal and River Trust: Canals and Rivers Infrastructure (3rd Party Data)\t© The Canal \u0026amp; River Trust  Attribution Statement: © The Canal \u0026amp; River Trust copyright and database rights reserved 2018 and © Ordnance Survey Crown copyright. All rights reserved 2018\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231363637\tX:\\Physical\\Hydrological\\Canals and rivers trust aqueducts.lyr  X:\\Physical\\Hydrological\\Canals and rivers trust bridges.lyr  X:\\Physical\\Hydrological\\Canals and rivers trust canals.lyr  X:\\Physical\\Hydrological\\Canals and rivers trust embankments.lyr  X:\\Physical\\Hydrological\\Canals and rivers trust locks.lyr  X:\\Physical\\Hydrological\\Canals and rivers trust reservoirs.lyr\tGIS and Spatial Data Team       A copy for the third party data licence is available here: https://canalrivertrust.org.uk/refresh/media/thumbnail/26503-CRT-Data-Licence.pdf  It is very similar to a CC-BY\tThis is a collation of spatial datasets related to canals and river\u0027s infrastructure that run through Wales. Natural Resources Wales obtained this data from the Canal and Rivers Trust through an end user licence. The Canal and River Trust are a charity who look after over 2000 miles of waters across the UK. Natural Resources Wales only have access to the welsh relevant data points.\tCanal and River Trust\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-03-21T10:32:24.000Z\tnobody nobody\t-\tPublic record\n17166\tEXT_DS121678\t2024-05-28T12:15:05.255Z\t400\tUnassessed\tEditable\tThe Crown Estate: Offshore Aggregates Data (3rd Party Data)\t© The Crown Estate NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly. All copies of the data must use the following attribution statement: © Crown Copyright (2018)\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231363738\tx:\\Resource Management\\The Crown Estate\\Offshore Aggregates Application.lyr  x:\\Resource Management\\The Crown Estate\\Offshore Aggregates Exploration.lyr  x:\\Resource Management\\The Crown Estate\\Offshore Aggregates Licences.lyr  x:\\Resource Management\\The Crown Estate\\Offshore Aggregates Option.lyr\tGIS and Spatial Data Services Team       The dataset is available to download here:  https://www.thecrownestate.co.uk/en-gb/resources/maps-and-gis-data/\tThis dataset shows the location of Marine Aggregate Agreements issued on Crown Estate owned seabed. Natural Resources Wales (NRW) has access to a number of Crown Estate datasets associated with the offshore aggregates industry. NRW can use this dataset under the terms and conditions of a bespoke Crown Estate Licence called \u0027the Data Means Aggregate Production Licence\u0027.  The data can be used for internal business use only.\tThe Crown Estate\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-04-17T09:58:01.000Z\tnobody nobody\t-\tPublic record\n17167\tEXT_DS121679\t2024-05-28T12:15:05.463Z\t1289\tUnassessed\tEditable\tThe Crown Estate: Offshore Wind Energy Site Data (3rd Party Data)\t© The Crown Estate NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly. All copies of the data must use the following attribution statement: © Crown Copyright (2018)\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231363739\tx:\\Resource Management\\The Crown Estate\\Offshore Wind farm cable agreements WGS84.lyr  x:\\Resource Management\\The Crown Estate\\Offshore Wind Farms WGS84.lyr  X:\\Utilities\\Renewables\\Crown Estate off shore wind farms.lyr  X:\\Utilities\\Renewables\\Crown Estate wind farm agreement.lyr\tGIS and Spatial Data team       Data can be accessed via: https://www.thecrownestate.co.uk/en-gb/resources/maps-and-gis-data/\tThis is a collation of datasets associated with the offshore wind energy.  Natural Resources Wales (NRW) has access to a number of Crown Estate datasets associated with the offshore renewable wind industry.  NRW can use this dataset under the terms and conditions of a bespoke Crown Estate Licence. NRW has access to \u0027Offshore Farm Cable Agreements\u0027 and \u0027Offshore Wind Farms\u0027. According to The Crown Estate: \u0027Offshore Wind Farms spatial data represent all offshore wind farms in pre-planning, planning, construction and operational phases in United Kingdom waters. Leasing rounds 1, 2 and 3 are included along with round 1 and 2 extension, Scottish exclusivity award applications, Demonstration wind farms and Northern Ireland Offshore Wind Resource Area.  The boundaries are a true reflection of what has been signed in the Agreement for Lease and Lease documents\u0027\tThe Crown Estate\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T12:56:43.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17171\tEXT_DS121680\t2024-05-28T12:15:05.549Z\t557\tUnassessed\tEditable\tThe Crown Estate: Offshore Tidal and Wave Energy Site Data (3rd Party Data)\t© The Crown Estate NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly. All copies of the data must use the following attribution statement: © Crown Copyright (2018)\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231363830\tx:\\Resource Management\\The Crown Estate\\Offshore Wave Site.lyr  x:\\Resource Management\\The Crown Estate\\Offshore Tidal Sites.lyr\tInternal Contact: GIS and Spatial Data Team Internal Custodian: James Moon, Lead Specialist Advisor: Offshore Renewable Energy Programme, Marine \u0026amp; Coastal Policy \u0026amp; Planning Team       The dataset is available to download here:  https://www.thecrownestate.co.uk/en-gb/resources/maps-and-gis-data/\tThis dataset shows the location of offshore tidal and wave energy sites for renewable energy projects issued on Crown Estate owned seabed. Natural Resources Wales (NRW) has access to a number of Crown Estate datasets associated with the offshore renewable industries associated with tidal and wave energy. NRW can use this dataset under the terms and conditions of a bespoke Crown Estate Licence which means we can only use this data for internal business use.  NRW has access to two dataset: Tidal Sites and Wave Sites.\tThe Crown Estate\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-03-27T13:30:31.000Z\tnobody nobody\t-\tPublic record\n17169\tEXT_DS121681\t2024-05-28T12:15:05.499Z\t418\tUnassessed\tEditable\tThe Crown Estate: Offshore meteorological equipment WGS84 (3rd Party Data)\t© The Crown Estate NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly. All copies of the data must use the following attribution statement: © Crown Copyright (2018)\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231363831\tX:\\Resource Management\\The Crown Estate\\Offshore meteorological equipment WGS84.lyr\tGIS and Spatial Data team\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW) has access to a number of Crown Estate datasets. NRW can use this dataset under the terms and conditions of a bespoke Crown Estate Licence which states we can only use this data for internal business use. This spatial dataset details the location of offshore meteorological equipement around the UK.\tThe Crown Estate\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2026-02-26T15:18:54.000Z\tMonica Jones\t-\tPublic record\n17174\tEXT_DS121682\t2024-05-28T12:15:05.652Z\t328\tUnassessed\tEditable\tThe Crown Estate: Offshore Sand and Gravel Resources (3rd Party Data)\t© The Crown Estate NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly. All copies of the data must use the following attribution statement: © Crown Copyright (2018)\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231363832\tX:\\Physical\\Minerals\\Offshore Sand and Gravel Resources.lyr\tGIS and Spatial Data Team\tThis is a spatial dataset detailing the extent and location of aggregates across the welsh waters. Natural Resources Wales has access to this dataset through a bespoke licence issued by The Crown Estate as part of this access to the dataset.  The UK has one of the largest dredging industries in the world. Marine-sourced aggregates make a vital contribution to UK aggregate supply for the construction sector and for coastal protection and land reclamation. However, activities on the UK Continental Shelf (UKCS) are currently undergoing significant change due to a changing planning regime, brought about by the Marine and Coastal Access Act 2009 and the Marine (Scotland) Act 2010, and increased pressure on the sea bed from new developments, such as renewable energy. As a result, to enhance understanding of the distribution of marine mineral resources, The Crown Estate (TCE), as owners of these resources, has commissioned British Geological Society (BGS) to produce maps of sand and gravel, as well as other mineral resources, such as coal, metallic minerals and evaporites for the UKCS. These maps provide spatial data for use in strategic planning for marine minerals and form an accessible information-base to assist protection of these non-renewable resources against sterilisation.\tThe Crown Estate\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-07-08T08:21:12.000Z\tnobody nobody\t-\tPublic record\n17164\tEXT_DS121685\t2024-05-28T12:15:05.010Z\t729\tUnassessed\tEditable\tHistoric England: Historic Areas and Buildings in England (3rd Party Data)\t© Historic England NRW may provide access to this dataset on request in some circumstances.  However, enquirers are advised to obtain a copy from the owner/originator directly, rather than NRW. NRW may NOT publish or disseminate it in its entirety.  Attribution Statement: © Historic England\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231363835\tX:\\Designations\\English Heritage\\English Heritage Scheduled Ancient Monuments.lyr   X:\\Designations\\English Heritage\\English Heritage Listed Buildings.lyr  X:\\Designations\\English Heritage\\Engish Heritage Parks and Garderns.lyr\tGIS Service Desk\tThis is a collation of spatial datasets associated with historic area and buildings that sit along the English side of the Welsh border and so are still of interest to Natural Resources Wales (NRW). NRW has obtained these dataset from Historic England under an Open Government Licence. Historic England are a public body that helps people care for, enjoy and celebrate England\u0027s spectacular historic environment.\tHistoric England\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-03-27T13:30:34.000Z\tnobody nobody\t-\tPublic record\n17168\tEXT_DS121689\t2024-05-28T12:15:05.499Z\t926\tUnassessed\tEditable\tJNCC: UK SeaMap Predictive Habitat Model (3rd Party Data)\t© Joint Nature Conservation Committee Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and copyright of the owners.  It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose.   Attribution Statement: Contains JNCC © copyright and database right 2015. Boundaries defined through discussions of the Inter-Agency Marine Mammal Working Group (IAMMWG).\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231363839\tX:\\Biological\\Marine Habitat\\UK SeaMap\\UK SEAMAP predictive habitat model.lyr\tMarine Evidence Team, JNCC euseamap@jncc.gov.uk\tThe UKSeaMap is a spatial dataset detailing the extent and location of habitats from UK Waters. This map is generated by JNCC as a by product from the EMODnet Seabed Habitats Consortium. Natural Resources Wales (NRW) have access to this data through an Open Government Licence.\tJoint Nature Conservation Committee (JNCC)\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T12:17:41.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17161\tEXT_DS121845\t2024-05-28T12:15:04.988Z\t2\tUnassessed\tEditable\tOil and Gas Authority (3rd Party Data)\t© [OGA (Oil and Gas Authority)] Data may be re-used under the terms of the 3rd Party Suppliers Open Licence  providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and owners copyright.  It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231383435\tX:\\Licensing and Permitting\\Oil and Gas Authority\\OGA Licences WGS84.lyr  X:\\Licensing and Permitting\\Oil and Gas Authority\\OGA Wells WGS84.lyr\tGeospatial Team\tThese datasets are wholly owned by the Oil and Gas Authority and contain spatial data detailing the extent and location of licencing blocks, Licences, Sub Areas and Wells across the terrestrial and marine areas of Wales and England.  Licences: A Licence is a geographically defined area for prospecting, exploration or extraction of petroleum resources. The Oil and Gas Authority’s licensing system covers oil and gas within Great Britain, its territorial sea and on the UK Continental Shelf (UKCS). The Petroleum Act 1998 vests all rights to the nation’s petroleum resources in the Crown, but the OGA can grant licences that confer exclusive rights to ‘search and bore for and get’ petroleum. Licences fall into several categories. The principal distinctions are between onshore and offshore licences, and between exploration licences (which cover exploration alone) and production licences (which cover both exploration and production). The OGA has discretion in the granting of licences to help maximise the economic recovery of the UK’s oil and gas resources. Licence data is represented by 3 different datasets; Licences, Licence Blocks and Sub Areas. Licence polygons represent the whole licence and have one polygon per licence. Licenced Blocks and Sub areas represent finer divisions of these licences and may have many polygons per licence. Most Licenced Blocks are split with several sub areas, sometimes with differing operators and beneficiaries. Licence types included are detailed as follows:  Landward Exploration Licences have the prefix ‘LX’ (e.g. LX001). CCS Licences have the prefix ‘CS’ (e.g. CS001) and Gas Storage Licences have the prefix ‘GS’ (e.g. GS001). Other prefixes (e.g. PEDL001, EXL001, PL001, ML001) indicate a Landward Production Licence of various vintages.  Wells: A wellbore is a path of drilled footage from the Well Origin to a terminating point. The location of each wellbore in this dataset is the wellbore’s well origin. A well origin is the location on the surface of the earth or sea bed where the drill bit penetrates the earth to establish or rework a well. Definitions for wellbore and well origin taken from PPDM ‘what is a well’: https://whatisawell.ppdm.org/. Data collection starts once a well has been spudded when the operator submits a spud notification on WONS. The OGA will issue an official well number via WONS, which is to be used for all data and records resulting from the well’s drilling. All well data requirements are set out in the documents Petroleum Operations Notices (PON) 9 (offshore) and PON 9b (onshore). Onshore operators have a statutory obligation to also supply well data to the British Geological Survey (BGS). Visit the BGS website for more information.\t\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T12:13:41.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPrivate record\n17163\tEXT_DS121846\t2024-05-28T12:15:05.036Z\t559\tUnassessed\tEditable\tBritish Geological Survey (BGS): 250k Onshore and Offshore Geology (3rd Party Data)\t© British Geological Society NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly. Attribution Statement: British Geological Survey BGS Digital Data under Licence Number 2013/062 ©NERC; Contains Ordnance Survey Data. Ordnance Survey Licence number AC0000849444. Crown Copyright and Database Right\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231383436\tX:\\Physical\\Geological\\BGS 250k Bedrock.lyr  X:\\Physical\\Geological\\BGS 250k Bedrock Off shore WGS84.lyr  X:\\Physical\\Geological\\BGS 250k Fault Line.lyr  X:\\Physical\\Geological\\BGS 250k Irishsea geology.lyr  X:\\Physical\\Geological\\BGS 250k Linear Bedrock Offshore WGS84.lyr  X:\\Physical\\Geological\\BGS 250k SeaBed Sediments WGS84  RCS.lyr  X:\\Physical\\Geological\\BGS 250k SeaBed Sediments WGS84 FOLK.lyr\tGIS and Spatial Data Team\tThe British Geological Survey (BGS) is a UK provider of geoscientific data, information and knowledge. Natural Resources Wales has licenced access to a number of BGS datasets. This particular spatial data is a collation of licenced data from DiGMapGB-250, DigSBS250 and DigRock250 all of which depict the data at a scale of 1:250,000.\tBritish Geological Survey (BGS)\t2025-10-28\trevision\tnull\tnull\t2025-10-28T11:41:16.000Z\tGary Eccleston\t-\tPublic record\n17160\tEXT_DS121847\t2024-05-28T12:15:04.933Z\t421\tUnassessed\tEditable\tBritish Geological Survey (BGS): 50k Onshore Geology (3rd Party Data)\t© British Geological Society NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231383437\tx:\\Physical\\Geological\\BGS 50k Artificial.lyr  x:\\Physical\\Geological\\BGS 50k Linear.lyr  x:\\Physical\\Geological\\BGS 50k Mass Movement.lyr  x:\\Physical\\Geological\\BGS 50k Bedrock.lyr  x:\\Physical\\Geological\\BGS 50k Superficial.lyr\tGIS and Spatial Data Team\tThe British Geological Survey (BGS) is a UK provider of geoscientific data, information and knowledge. Natural Resources Wales (NRW) has licenced access to a number of BGS datasets. This particular spatial data is a collation of licenced data from BGS Geology 50k: DiGMapGB-50 all of which depict the data at a scale of 1:50,000. This data is split into the following themes: - Bedrock Geology - Superficial deposits - Mass movement - Artificial ground - Linear Features\tBritish Geological Survey (BGS)\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T12:17:46.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17162\tEXT_DS121848\t2024-05-28T12:15:04.878Z\t1355\tUnassessed\tEditable\tBritish Geological Survey (BGS): British Pits, Active and Historic Quarries (3rd Party Data)\t© British Geological Society NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly. Attribution Statement: British Geological Survey BGS Digital Data under Licence Number 2013/062 ©NERC; Contains Ordnance Survey Data. Ordnance Survey Licence number AC0000849444. Crown Copyright and Database Right\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231383438\tx:\\Physical\\Geological\\BGS British Pits.lyr  x:\\Physical\\Geological\\Mineral Resources\\BGS Active quarries.lyr  x:\\Physical\\Geological\\Mineral Resources\\BGS Historic slate quarries.lyr  x:\\Physical\\Geological\\Mineral Resources\\BGS Significant building stone quarries.lyr\tGIS and Spatial Data Team\tThe British Geological Survey (BGS) is a UK provider of geoscientific data, information and knowledge. Natural Resources Wales has licenced access to a number of BGS datasets. These particular licenced spatial data products are known as BRITPITS, active quarries, historic slate quarries and significant building stone quarries, and they depict the location of surface and underground mineral workings across the UK.\tBritish Geological Survey (BGS)\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-03-21T10:52:42.000Z\tnobody nobody\t-\tPublic record\n17159\tEXT_DS121849\t2024-05-28T12:15:04.816Z\t880\tUnassessed\tEditable\tBritish Geological Survey (BGS): Mass Movement and Landslide data (3rd Party Data)\t© British Geological Society NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly. Attribution Statement: British Geological Survey BGS Digital Data under Licence Number 2013/062 ©NERC; Contains Ordnance Survey Data. Ordnance Survey Licence number AC0000849444. Crown Copyright and Database Right\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231383439\tx:\\Physical\\Geological\\Landslide Records.lyr  x:\\Physical\\Geological\\Mass Movement Hazard on Forestry Land.lyr\tGIS and Spatial Data Team\tThe British Geological Survey (BGS) is a UK provider of geoscientific data, information and knowledge. Natural Resources Wales has licenced access to a number of BGS datasets. These licenced dataset include mass movement and landslip data.\tBritish Geological Survey (BGS)\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-03-27T13:30:34.000Z\tnobody nobody\t-\tPublic record\n17157\tEXT_DS121850\t2024-05-28T12:15:04.672Z\t1094\tUnassessed\tEditable\tBritish Geological Survey (BGS): 625k Onshore Geology (3rd Party Data)\t© BGS Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and copyright of the owners.  It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose The following acknowledgement must accompany the reproduced BGS material: \u0027Reproduced with the permission of the British Geological Survey ©UKRI. All rights Reserved\u0027 Where figures, sketches, illustrations, diagrams, map extracts or cross-sections are used as the basis of specifically generated illustrations, the source of the material should be cited as follows:  \u0027Based upon DiGMapGB-625, with the permission of the British Geological Survey\u0027.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231383530\tx:\\Physical\\Geological\\BGS 625k Bedrock.lyr  x:\\Physical\\Geological\\BGS 625k Superficial.lyr\tGIS and Spatial Data Team\tThe British Geological Survey (BGS) is a UK provider of geoscientific data, information and knowledge. Natural Resources Wales has licenced access to a number of BGS datasets. This particular spatial data is a collation of licenced data from BGS Geology 625k DiGMapGB-625, all of which depict the data at a scale of 1:625,000.\tBritish Geological Survey (BGS)\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-04-17T10:01:44.000Z\tnobody nobody\t-\tPublic record\n17158\tEXT_DS121851\t2024-05-28T12:15:04.616Z\t581\tUnassessed\tEditable\tBritish Geological Survey (BGS): Mineral Resources (3rd Party Data)\t© British Geological Survey NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly. Attribution Statement: British Geological Survey BGS Digital Data under Licence Number 2013/062 ©NERC; Contains Ordnance Survey Data. Ordnance Survey Licence number AC0000849444. Crown Copyright and Database Right\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231383531\tx:\\Physical\\Geological\\Mineral Resources\\BGS Bedrock resources.lyr  x:\\Physical\\Geological\\Mineral Resources\\BGS Coal resources.lyr  x:\\Physical\\Geological\\Mineral Resources\\BGS Metallic mineral occurence.lyr  x:\\Physical\\Geological\\Mineral Resources\\BGS Mudstone and sandstone resources.lyr  x:\\Physical\\Geological\\Mineral Resources\\BGS Mudstone and slate resources.lyr  x:\\Physical\\Geological\\Mineral Resources\\BGS Slate waste resources.lyr  x:\\Physical\\Geological\\Mineral Resources\\BGS Superficial resources.lyr\tGIS and Spatial Data Team\tThe British Geological Survey (BGS) is a UK provider of geoscientific data, information and knowledge. Natural Resources Wales has licenced access to a number of BGS datasets. This particular spatial data is a collation of licenced data from BGS mineral resources depicted at a 1:50,000 scale.\t\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T13:06:04.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17156\tEXT_DS121864\t2024-05-28T12:15:04.480Z\t816\tUnassessed\tEditable\tMarine Conservation Society: Beachwatch data Wales (3rd Party Data)\t© Marine Conservation Society NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231383634\tNon Spatial Data: https://cyfoethnaturiolcymru.sharepoint.com/teams/kdim/Data-Management/dai/Third%20Party%20Data/Forms/NRW%20View.aspx X:\\Monitoring\\Marine\\Marine Conservation Society\\MCS Beachwatch marine litter 2015 to17 WGS84.lyr\tBusiness Contacts are: Matt Green (marine) Harriet Robinson (marine)  GIS and Spatial Data Team for spatial layer. Data Services for Licence and non spatial layer.  Marine Conservation Society for original data.\tThis is a Marine Conservation Society non-spatial dataset, the Natural Resources Wales (NRW) has for internal use only. NRW has converted this non-spatial dataset, into a spatial data layer for their corporate internal use. Beachwatch is Marine Conservation Society\u0027s national beach cleaning and litter survey programme, helping people all around the UK to care for their coastline. This dataset contains the results of the cleaning a litter programme between 2015 and 2017.\tMarine Conservation Society (MCS)\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-04-17T12:30:18.000Z\tnobody nobody\t-\tPublic record\n17207\tEXT_DS121865\t2024-05-28T12:16:00.485Z\t816\tUnassessed\tEditable\tCanal and River Trust: Ownership (3rd Party Data)\t© The Canal \u0026amp; River Trust  NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly.  Attribution Statement: © The Canal \u0026amp; River Trust copyright and database rights reserved. All rights reserved. Contains Ordnance Survey Data. Ordnance Survey Licence number AC0000849444. Crown Copyright and Database Right.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231383635\tx:\\Ownership\\Canals and rivers trust\\Canals and rivers trust Ownership Line.lyr  x:\\Ownership\\Canals and rivers trust\\Canals and rivers trust Ownership.lyr  x:\\Physical\\Hydrological\\Canals and rivers trust feeders.lyr\tGIS and Spatial Data Team\tThis is a spatial third party dataset, detailing the extent and location of Canal and River Trust Ownership in Wales. The Canals and Rivers Trust has licenced Natural Resources Wales (NRW)\tCanal and River Trust\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T12:27:32.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17203\tEXT_DS121866\t2024-05-28T12:16:00.235Z\t751\tUnassessed\tEditable\tUK Centre for Ecology and Hydrology (UKCEH): Hydrological and Catchment Areas (3rd Party Data)\t© UKCEH NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly. Attribution Statement: © UKCEH. Contains Ordnance Survey data © Crown copyright and database right [year].\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231383636\tx:\\Physical\\Hydrological\\CEH Catchments 10k.lyr,  x:\\Physical\\Hydrological\\CEH Catchments 50k.lyr,  x:\\Physical\\Hydrological\\CEH Hydrological Areas.lyr. X:\\Flood Risk\\Flood Risk Management\\FEH drainage network.lyr,\tGIS and Spatial Data team\tThis is a UK Centre for Ecology and Hydrology (UKCEH) owned dataset containing the extent and location of catchment and hydrological areas in Wales. This dataset has been licenced to Natural Resources Wales for internal use and can be sub-licenced to NRW contractors.\tCentre for Ecology and Hydrology (CEH)\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-10-16T13:39:27.072Z\tMonica Jones\t-\tPublic record\n17194\tEXT_DS121867\t2024-05-28T12:16:00.084Z\t970\tUnassessed\tEditable\tUK Centre for Ecology and Hydrology (UKCEH): Rivers (3rd Party Data)\t© UKCEH NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly.  Attribution Statement: © UKCEH. Contains Ordnance Survey data © Crown copyright and database right [year].\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231383637\tx:\\Physical\\Hydrological\\CEH Rivers 250K.lyr  x:\\Physical\\Hydrological\\CEH Rivers 50k Shreve .lyr  x:\\Physical\\Hydrological\\CEH Rivers 50k Strahler.lyr  x:\\Physical\\Hydrological\\CEH Rivers 50K.lyr  x:\\Physical\\Hydrological\\CEH Rivers.lyr\tGIS and Spatial Data Team\tThe UK Centre for Ecology and Hydrology (UKCEH) is a research organisation focusing on land and freshwater ecosystems and their interaction with the atmosphere. This is a UKCEH owned dataset containing the extent and location of rivers in Wales. This dataset has been licenced to Natural Resources Wales for use.\tCentre for Ecology and Hydrology (CEH)\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-04-17T12:26:18.000Z\tnobody nobody\t-\tPublic record\n17198\tEXT_DS121869\t2024-05-28T12:16:00.213Z\t302\tUnassessed\tEditable\tEnvironment Agency (EA): Water Resource Permit Locations (3rd Party Data)\t© Environment Agency  NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly. Attribution Statement: © Environment Agency\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231383639\tX:\\Licensing and Permitting\\Water Abstractions \u0026amp; Discharges\\EA Water quality permits.lyr  X:\\Licensing and Permitting\\Water Abstractions \u0026amp; Discharges\\EA Water resource permits area.lyr  X:\\Licensing and Permitting\\Water Abstractions \u0026amp; Discharges\\EA Water resource permits points.lyr  X:\\Licensing and Permitting\\Water Abstractions \u0026amp; Discharges\\EA Water resource permits reach.lyr\tHenry Forest - Permitting Officer, Wales Permitting Centre Cardiff (Water Resources)  GIS and Spatial Data Team\tThis is an Environment Agency (EA) collection of datasets related to the location of Water Resource Permits in England. Natural Resource Wales (NRW) has access to this data via a data exchange agreement with EA. This is for internal use only.\tEnvironment Agency (EA)\t2018-12-11\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-07-08T08:21:14.000Z\tnobody nobody\t-\tPublic record\n17199\tEXT_DS121874\t2024-05-28T12:16:00.197Z\t406\tUnassessed\tEditable\tForestry Commission England (FCE): Forest Recreation (3rd Party Data)\t© The Forestry Commission. Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and copyright of the owners. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose. Attribution Statement: Contains, or is based on, information supplied by the Forestry Commission. © Crown copyright and database right [2018] Ordnance Survey [100021242] Attribution statement: Contains OS data © Crown copyright [and database right] [2018].\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231383734\tx:\\Recreation and Access\\Recreation\\FCE Recreation Areas.lyr  x:\\Recreation and Access\\Recreation\\FCE Recreation Points.lyr  x:\\Recreation and Access\\Recreation\\FCE Recreation Routes.lyr\tGIS and Spatial Data Team\tThis is a spatial dataset owned by Forest Commission England (FCE) detailing the extent and location of places where forest recreation occurs in England. Natural Resources Wales (NRW) has access to this dataset under an Open Government Licence (OGL).\tForestry Commission (FC)\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2026-02-26T15:20:05.000Z\tMonica Jones\t-\tPublic record\n17192\tEXT_DS121875\t2024-05-28T12:16:00.190Z\t5\tUnassessed\tEditable\tForest Research: Soil Map Coverage (3rd Party Data)\t\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231383735\tx:\\Physical\\Soils\\FCE Soil Map Coverage.lyr  x:\\Physical\\Soils\\Local Soil Information.lyr\tGIS and Spatial Data Team\tThis dataset is wholly owned by Forestry Commission Great Britain and licence to Natural Resources Wales (NRW) for use. It shows the local soil map coverage information. These datasets remain relatively static.\t\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T10:17:11.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPrivate record\n17193\tEXT_DS121876\t2024-05-28T12:16:00.229Z\t453\tUnassessed\tEditable\tForestry Commission England (FCE): Forest Roads (3rd Party Data)\t© The Forestry Commission.  Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and copyright of the owners.  It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose. Attribution Statement: Contains, or is based on, information supplied by the Forestry Commission. © Crown copyright and database right [2018] Ordnance Survey [100021242] Attribution statement: Contains OS data © Crown copyright [and database right] [2018].\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231383736\tx:\\Transport\\Forest Roads\\FCE Forest Roads.lyr\tGIS and Spatial Data Team\tThis is a Forestry Commission England (FCE) spatial dataset detailing the extent and location of forest roads in England. Natural Resources Wales (NRW) has access to this data via a OGL.\tForestry Commission (FC)\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-07-08T08:24:54.000Z\tnobody nobody\t-\tPublic record\n17208\tEXT_DS121877\t2024-05-28T12:16:00.477Z\t2\tUnassessed\tEditable\tForestry Commission Great Britain (FCGB): National Forest Inventory Felled and Windblown (3rd Party Data)\t© [Forestry Commission] Data may be reused by Public Sector Mapping Agreement (PSMA) Members Only, under the terms and conditions of the PSMA licence, acknowledging both the source and owners copyright.  It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose.  NRW does NOT grant permission to non PSMA members to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly. Attribution Statement: © Crown copyright and database rights [2019] Ordnance Survey licence number [100021242]\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231383737\tX:\\Physical\\Forestry\\National Forest Inventory Felled 2016.lyr  X:\\Physical\\Forestry\\National Forest Inventory Felled 2017.lyr  X:\\Physical\\Forestry\\National Forest Inventory Felled 2018.lyr  X:\\Physical\\Forestry\\National Forest Inventory Felled 2021.lyr  X:\\Physical\\Forestry\\National Forest Inventory Windblow 2016.lyr  X:\\Physical\\Forestry\\National Forest Inventory Windblow 2017.lyr  X:\\Physical\\Forestry\\National Forest Inventory Windblow 2018.lyr  X:\\Physical\\Forestry\\National Forest Inventory Windblow 2021.lyr\tGeospatial Services Team\tThis is a subset of the National Forest Inventory, and specifically details the felled and windblown datasets.\tForestry Commission (FC)\t2023-11-16\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T12:27:19.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPrivate record\n17205\tEXT_DS121878\t2024-05-28T12:16:00.484Z\t587\tUnassessed\tEditable\tForestry Commission Great Britain (FCGB): National Forest Inventory (3rd Party Data)\t© The Forestry Commission Great Britain. Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and copyright of the owners. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231383738\tX:\\Physical\\Forestry\\National Forest Inventory 2012.lyr  X:\\Physical\\Forestry\\FCE National Forest Inventory 2014.lyr  X:\\Physical\\Forestry\\National Forest Inventory England 2015.lyr  X:\\Physical\\Forestry\\National Forest Inventory 2016.lyr  X:\\Physical\\Forestry\\National Forest Inventory 2017.lyr  X:\\Physical\\Forestry\\National Forest Inventory 2018.lyr  X:\\Physical\\Forestry\\National Forest Inventory 2018 (Service).lyr  X:\\Physical\\Forestry\\National Forest Inventory 2020.lyr  X:\\Physical\\Forestry\\National Forest Inventory 2021.lyr X:\\Physical\\Forestry\\National Forest Inventory 2022.lyr X:\\Physical\\Forestry\\National Forest Inventory 2023.lyr X:\\Physical\\Forestry\\National Forest Inventory 2024.lyr\tGIS and Spatial Data Team\tThis is the Forestry Commission National Forest Inventory (NFI) Map for Great Britain and is wholly owned by the Forestry Commission Great Britain (FCGB).   The NFI programme monitors woodland and trees across Great Britain. The NFI provides an extensive and unique record of key information about our forests and woodlands.   This dataset includes Interpreted Forest Types (IFTs) for all woodland over 0.5ha and Interpreted Open Area (IOA) information for areas over 0.5ha that are completely surrounded by woodland.\tForestry Commission (FC)\t2025-10-28\trevision\tnull\thttps://data-forestry.opendata.arcgis.com/search?tags\u003dWales\t2025-11-05T13:23:01.277Z\tMonica Jones\t-\tPublic record\n17206\tEXT_DS121879\t2024-05-28T12:16:00.399Z\t778\tUnassessed\tEditable\tCowi: Welsh Digital Aerial Photography 2006 (3rd Party Data)\tNRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset Copyright Statement for internal use: Cowi [2006]\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231383739\tX:\\Basemapping\\Air Photos\\Aerial Images 2006.lyr  X:\\Basemapping\\Air Photos\\Air photos index\\Air photo index 2006.lyr\tGIS and Spatial Data Team\tIn 2006 the Aerial Images were produced by Cowi. GetMapping and Bluesky International supplied NRW this data under licence for the following years; 2000, 2009, 2013-14, 2013-17, 2015 and 2017 (see metadata number 121661 for more information about these datasets).   This Cowi raster dataset contains aerial imagery for 2006. Natural Resources Wales (NRW) has access to the Welsh extent of this dataset as part of a Public Sector Mapping Agreement (PSMA). The licencing conditions mean that NRW can only use this data for internal use.\tCOWI Mapping UK Ltd.\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-07-08T08:24:54.000Z\tnobody nobody\t-\tPublic record\n17197\tEXT_DS121881\t2024-05-28T12:16:00.237Z\t941\tUnassessed\tEditable\tLocal Environmental Records Centres (LERCS) Wales: Boundaries (3rd Party Data)\t© Cofnod North Wales Environmental Information Service, BIS Biodiversity Information Service for Powys and Brecon Beacons National Park BIS, WWBIC West Wales Biodiversity Information Centre, SEWBReC South East Wales Biodiversity Record Centre. Data may be re-used under the terms of the 3rd Party Open Data licence. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231383831\tX:\\Biological\\Local Record Centers\\Local Record Centre Boundary.lyr\tGIS and Spatial Data Team\tThis is a spatial dataset detailing the areas covered by each Local Environmental Record Centre in Wales. Natural Resources Wales (NRW) has access to this dataset through a licence set up under the Local Environmental Records Centres Wales (LERC) Wales.\tCofnod (North Wales Environmental Information Service)-WWBIC (West Wales Biodiversity Information Centre)-SEWBReC (South East Wales Biodiversity Records Centre)-BIS (Biodiversity Information Service for Powys and Brecon Beacons National Park)\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-07-08T08:24:56.000Z\tnobody nobody\t-\tPublic record\n17202\tEXT_DS121882\t2024-05-28T12:16:00.221Z\t1670\tUnassessed\tEditable\tMet Office: Met Office Rainfall and Evapo-transpiration Calculation System (MORECS) (3rd Party Data)\t© The Met Office NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly. Attribution Statement: © Crown Copyright 2011, The Met Office\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231383832\tX:\\Physical\\Meteorological\\Met Office Rainfall Evaporation Calc Sys (MORECS) squares.lyr   More up to date data is held in the DMS: https://cyfoethnaturiolcymru.sharepoint.com/teams/waterman/wrmr/ww/Morecs%20Data/Forms/NRW%20View.aspx\tGIS and Spatial Data Team\tThis is the Met Office Rainfall and Evapo-transpiration Calculation System (MORECS) 40km x 40km squared averages. Natural Resources Wales (NRW) have access to a licenced welsh cut of this data from the Met Office. The Met Office is the UK National Meteorological Service set up to research the possibilities of forecasting the weather, and now uses more than 10 million weather observation from across the UK to create advanced atmospheric models to predict upcoming forecasts and longer term climate change scenarios.\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2026-02-26T15:22:10.000Z\tMonica Jones\t-\tPublic record\n17200\tEXT_DS121883\t2024-05-28T12:16:00.233Z\t740\tUnassessed\tEditable\tMet Office: Average Rainfall (3rd Party Data)\t© The Met Office NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231383833\tx:\\Physical\\Meteorological\\Met Office Rainfall Annual Averages 1Km.lyr  x:\\Physical\\Meteorological\\Met Office Rainfall Annual Avg Contours 1941-1970.lyr\tGIS and Spatial Data Team\tThis is a spatial datasets for annual average rainfall obtained from the Met Office. Natural Resources Wales (NRW) have obtained this dataset via a bespoke licence from the Met Office. The Met Office is the UK National Meteorological Service set up to research the possibilities of forecasting the weather, and now uses more than 10 million weather observation from across the UK to create advanced atmospheric models to predict upcoming forecasts and longer term climate change scenarios.\tMet Office\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2026-01-07T16:54:26.000Z\tMonica Jones\t-\tPublic record\n17191\tEXT_DS121885\t2024-05-28T12:16:00.230Z\t1182\tUnassessed\tEditable\tMet Office: Rain Gauge (3rd Party Data)\t© The Met Office NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly. Attribution Statement: © Crown Copyright 2011, The Met Office\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231383835\tx:\\Physical\\Meteorological\\Met Office Raingauge Closed.lyr  x:\\Physical\\Meteorological\\Met Office Raingauge Open.lyr\tGIS and Spatial Data Team\tThese spatial datasets show the location of open and closed rain gauges from across Wales. This data is owned by the Met Office and Natural Resources Wales (NRW) have access to a licenced welsh cut of this data from the Met Office. The Met Office is the UK National Meteorological Service set up to research the possibilities of forecasting the weather, and now uses more than 10 million weather observation from across the UK to create advanced atmospheric models to predict upcoming forecasts and longer term climate change scenarios.\tMet Office\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T12:23:57.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17209\tEXT_DS121886\t2024-05-28T12:16:00.467Z\t1077\tUnassessed\tEditable\tMinistry of Defence (MoD): Land Ownership (3rd Party Data)\t© MoD. NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly. Attribution Statement: © Crown Copyright and database rights (insert year of supply). Ordnance Survey 100023818\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231383836\tX:\\Ownership\\MOD\\MOD Land.lyr\tGIS and Spatial Data Team\tThis spatial dataset details the extent and location of land owned by the Ministry of Defence (MoD) in Wales. Natural Resources Wales (NRW) has access to this data through a licence agreement with the MoD.\tMinistry of Defence (MoD)\t2021-04-13\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-07-08T08:24:56.000Z\tnobody nobody\t-\tPublic record\n17210\tEXT_DS121887\t2024-05-28T12:16:00.676Z\t391\tUnassessed\tEditable\tNational Grid: Electricity and Gas Infrastructure (3rd Party Data)\t© National Grid UK NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly. Attribution Statement: \"© National Grid UK\"\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231383837\tX:\\Utilities\\Electricity\\National Grid cable fibre lines.lyr  X:\\Utilities\\Electricity\\National Grid high voltage lines.lyr  X:\\Utilities\\Electricity\\National Grid Line towers.lyr  X:\\Utilities\\Electricity\\National Grid overhead line routes.lyr  X:\\Utilities\\Electricity\\National Grid Substations.lyr  X:\\Utilities\\Electricity\\National Grid Underground cable lines.lyr  X:\\Utilities\\Gas\\National Grid Gas sites.lyr  X:\\Utilities\\Gas\\National Grid High pressure gas mains.lyr\tGIS and Spatial Data Team\tThese datasets detail the extent and location of various electricity and gas infrastructure that are managed and owned by the National Grid. Natural Resources Wales (NRW) has access to these datasets through a licence agreement.\tNational Gird\t2023-12-12\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-07-08T08:24:56.000Z\tnobody nobody\t-\tPublic record\n17201\tEXT_DS121890\t2024-05-28T12:16:00.087Z\t609\tUnassessed\tEditable\tNational Trust: Land Access (3rd Party Data)\t© National Trust Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and copyright of the owners.  It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose. Attribution Statement: © National Trust\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231383930\tx:\\Recreation and Access\\National Trust\\National Trust land that has limited access.lyr  x:\\Recreation and Access\\National Trust\\National Trust land that is always open.lyr\tGIS and Spatial Data Team\tThese datasets detail area of access, or limited access to National Trust Land. Natural Resources Wales (NRW) has access to this data through an Open Government Licence.\tNational Trust\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-03-21T10:38:24.000Z\tnobody nobody\t-\tPublic record\n17196\tEXT_DS121891\t2024-05-28T12:16:00.233Z\t836\tUnassessed\tEditable\tNatural England: Designated Sites (3rd Party Data)\t© Natural England Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and owners copyright.  It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose.  © Natural England copyright. Contains Ordnance Survey data © Crown copyright and database right [2018].\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231383931\tX:\\Designations\\Natural England\\NE Areas Outstanding Natural Beauty.lyr  X:\\Designations\\Natural England\\NE Country Parks.lyr  X:\\Designations\\Natural England\\NE Designations.lyr  X:\\Designations\\Natural England\\NE Heritage Coast.lyr  X:\\Designations\\Natural England\\NE Local Nature Reserves.lyr  X:\\Designations\\Natural England\\NE National Nature Reserves.lyr  X:\\Designations\\Natural England\\NE National Parks.lyr  X:\\Designations\\Natural England\\NE National Trails.lyr  X:\\Designations\\Natural England\\NE Ramsar.lyr  X:\\Designations\\Natural England\\NE Sites Special Scientific Interest.lyr  X:\\Designations\\Natural England\\NE Special Areas Conservation.lyr  X:\\Designations\\Natural England\\NE Special Protection Areas.lyr\tGIS and Spatial Data Team\tNatural England designate, manage and monitoring a number of protected sites throughout England. This is a spatial dataset detailing the extent and location of these sites. Natural Resources Wales (NRW) has access to this data under an Open Government Licence.\tNatural England\t2020-10-22\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-04-17T12:26:13.000Z\tnobody nobody\t-\tPublic record\n17195\tEXT_DS121926\t2024-05-28T12:15:59.848Z\t1\tUnassessed\tEditable\tEnvironment Agency: Severn Lower 2017 Saltmarsh Extent (3rd Party Data)\t© [Environment Agency] Data may be re-used under the terms of the 3rd Party Open Data licence. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231393236\tX:\\Monitoring\\Marine\\Saltmarsh Areas\\Severn Lower 2017 Saltmarsh Extent.lyr\tMetadata Point of contact - Geospatial Team Internal Custodian - Kathryn Borrowdale, Marine Environmental Assessment \u0026amp; Reporting Team\tWater Framework Directive saltmarsh monitoring. Saltmarsh extents determined in a desk based study using aerial imagery. This data is Open, but owned by the Environment Agency.\tEnvironment Agency (EA)\t2017-08-31\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-03-07T15:58:56.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPrivate record\n17185\tEXT_DS121927\t2024-05-28T12:15:59.542Z\t3\tUnassessed\tEditable\tEnvironment Agency: Severn Lower 2017 Saltmarsh Zonation Points (3rd Party Data)\t© [Environment Agency] Data may be re-used under the terms of the 3rd Party Open Data licence. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231393237\tX:\\Monitoring\\Marine\\Saltmarsh Areas\\Severn Lower 2017 Saltmarsh Zonation Points.lyr\tMetadata contact - Geospatial Team Internal Custodian - Kathryn Borrowdale, Marine Environmental Assessment \u0026amp; Reporting Team\tWater Framework Directive saltmarsh monitoring. Saltmarsh zonation points determined in a desk based study using aerial imagery. This data is Open, but owned by the Environment Agency.\tEnvironment Agency (EA)\t2017-08-31\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-03-07T15:58:55.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPrivate record\n17204\tEXT_DS121928\t2024-05-28T12:16:00.462Z\t1\tUnassessed\tEditable\tEnvironment Agency: Severn Lower 2017 Saltmarsh Zonation Polygon (3rd Party Data)\t© [Environment Agency] Data may be re-used under the terms of the 3rd Party Open Data licence. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231393238\tX:\\Monitoring\\Marine\\Saltmarsh Areas\\Severn Lower 2017 Saltmarsh Zonation Polygons.lyr\tMetadata contact - Geospatial Team Internal Custodian - Kathryn Borrowdale, Marine Environmental Assessment \u0026amp; Reporting Team\tWater Framework Directive saltmarsh monitoring. Saltmarsh zonation polygons are determined in a desk based study using aerial imagery. This data is Open, but owned by the Environment Agency.\tEnvironment Agency (EA)\t2017-08-31\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-03-07T15:58:54.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPrivate record\n17190\tEXT_DS121943\t2024-05-28T12:15:59.688Z\t725\tUnassessed\tEditable\tOceanWise: Marine Themes Vector Maps (3rd Party Data)\tNRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset.  Attribution Statement: © British Crown and OceanWise Ltd, 2013. All rights reserved. License No. EK001-20120402\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231393433\tThe various data layers are stored in the following folder: X:\\Basemapping\\Marine Charts\tGIS and Spatial Data Team\tThis collation of datasets is managed and owned by OceanWise and licenced to NRW for internal use only. Marine Themes Vector comprises of authoritative data from different public sector data agencies, including the UK and other hydrographic offices. The dataset uses different sources of data available for a particular feature and scale range, derived either from the production Electronic Navigational Charts (ENCs) or from original source datasets, where available. Marine Themes Vector is supplied as individual themed layers corresponding to marine reference data or base mapping required for general situation awareness, planning, site selection and investigation and outline engineering design.\tOceanWise\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T12:18:12.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17189\tEXT_DS121944\t2024-05-28T12:15:59.620Z\t549\tUnassessed\tEditable\tOceanWise: Marine Raster Charts (3rd Party Data)\tNRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231393434\tX:\\Basemapping\\Marine Charts\\Marine Raster Data - BNG.lyr  X:\\Basemapping\\Marine Charts\\Marine Raster Data - WGS84.lyr\tGIS and Spatial data Team\tThis collation of datasets is managed and owned by OceanWise and licenced to NRW for internal use only. Raster Charts comprises of the well-known and popular nautical chart series from the UK Hydrographic Office supplied as individual image files for easy loading and use in GIS.\tUnited Kingdom Hydrographic Office (UKHO)-OceanWise\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2026-01-07T16:56:33.000Z\tMonica Jones\t-\tPublic record\n17187\tEXT_DS121945\t2024-05-28T12:15:59.647Z\t999\tUnassessed\tEditable\tOrdnance Survey and Landmark Information Group: Historic Mapping (3rd Party Data)\tNRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Attribution Statement: Historic map data © and database right. Crown copyright and Landmark Information Group Ltd. All rights reserved.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231393435\tX:\\Basemapping\\Ordnance Survey Mapping\\OS MasterMap\\Historic Mapping\\County Series 10560 epoch 1 to 4 X:\\Basemapping\\Ordnance Survey Mapping\\OS MasterMap\\Historic Mapping\\County Series 2500 epoch 1 to 4 X:\\Basemapping\\Ordnance Survey Mapping\\OS MasterMap\\Historic Mapping\\Historic maps indices X:\\Basemapping\\Ordnance Survey Mapping\\OS MasterMap\\Historic Mapping\\National grid 1250 town plans X:\\Basemapping\\Ordnance Survey Mapping\\OS MasterMap\\Historic Mapping\\National grid series 10000 epoch 5 to 7  Historic mapping is also available as a service and on MyMap X:\\Basemapping\\Ordnance Survey Mapping\\Historic Mapping\\OS Historic maps service\\OS Historic maps WMS.lyr\tGIS and Spatial Data Team\tHistorical Map Data is owned and supplied by Landmark Information Group and Ordnance Survey (OS) and supplied to Natural Resource Wales (NRW) via an OS licence.  Landmark Information Group Limited holds the most extensive digital collection of historical Ordnance Survey mapping of Great Britain. This has been taken from Ordnance Survey’s archive of Town Plans, County Series and National Grid mapping covering the period from 1841 to 1996. Historical mapping provides a unique insight into our past and is a fascinating journey through history in itself. Particularly when displayed with contemporary mapping or aerial photography. Historical Map Data is available for different time periods, referred to as epochs.  Epoch 1: the first County Series survey; published dates 1843 to 1893 Epoch 2: the first County Series revision; published dates 1891 to 1912 Epoch 3: the second County Series revision; published dates 1904 to 1939 Epoch 4: the third County Series revision; published dates 1919 to 1939\tLandmark Information Group Ltd-Ordnance Survey (OS)\t2018-11-27\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T12:24:24.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17186\tEXT_DS121956\t2024-05-28T12:15:59.617Z\t690\tUnassessed\tEditable\tPlantlife International: Important Plantlife Areas (3rd Party Data)\tNRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset.  The Plantlife logo, and where appropriate the logo of National IPA Partners and major funders must be included (all those required will be provided with the dataset). Attribution Statement: Copyright © 2018 Plantlife International. All Rights Reserved.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231393536\tX:\\Biological\\Plant Life\\Plantlife International\\Important Plantlife Areas.lyr\tGIS and Spatial Data Team\tPlantlife International collects and holds a large quantity of data on plants and habitats of conservation importance throughout the UK from a network of individuals and organisations. This data collations is owned by Plantlife International and has been licence to Natural Resources Wales (NRW) for use. The Important Plant Area (IPA) programme is intended to inform and underpin existing international, regional and national conservation programmes and legislation. Ultimately Plantlife aim to have Important Plantlife Areas (IPAs) acting as a benchmark for determining whether the strongest protection, under any existing legislation, is being afforded to the most important sites for plants.\tPlantlife\t2021-02-15\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-03-27T09:10:53.000Z\tnobody nobody\t-\tPublic record\n17188\tEXT_DS121959\t2024-05-28T12:15:59.685Z\t595\tUnassessed\tEditable\tPlantlife International: Broad Soil Types (3rd Party data)\t© 2017 Plantlife International. All Rights Reserved. NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly. The Plantlife logo must be included in all publications and one copy of all publications and reports using data supplied by Plantlife International shall be supplied free of charge to Plantlife International.  Attribution Statement: Copyright © 2018 Plantlife International. All Rights Reserved.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231393539\tX:\\Biological\\Plant Life\\Plant Life Soils 2km.lyr\tGIS and Spatial Data Team\tPlantlife International collects and holds a large quantity of data on plants and habitats of conservation importance throughout the UK from a network of individuals and organisations. This data collations is owned by Plantlife International and has been licence to Natural Resources Wales (NRW) for use. Dominant soil types have been determined to ascertain the Important Arable Plant Area  (IAPA) score for each tetrad used in the Welsh Important Arable Plant Area (IAPA) Status dataset.\tPlantlife\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-07-08T08:24:54.000Z\tnobody nobody\t-\tPublic record\n17184\tEXT_DS121960\t2024-05-28T12:15:59.371Z\t1431\tUnassessed\tEditable\tRoyal Commission on the Ancient and Historic Monuments of Wales (RCAHMW): National Monuments Record of Wales (3rd Party Data)\tData may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and owners copyright. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose.. Attribution Statement: © Crown copyright RCAHMW / © Hawlfraint y Goron CBHC\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231393630\tX:\\Designations\\RCAHM\\Royal Commission Ancient Historic Monuments.lyr  X:\\Designations\\RCAHM\\WMS for Coflein National Monuments Record for Wales.lyr\tGIS and Spatial Data Team\tNational Monuments Record of Wales is the Royal Commission on the Ancient and Historic Monuments of Wales\u0027 (RACHMW) archive of built heritage around wales. RACHMW have licenced Natural Resources Wales (NRW) for the use of this data. There are over 110,000 sites including buildings, archaeological, industrial and maritime sites throughout Wales.  NRW has access to both the Coflein National Monuments Records for Wales via a Web Mapping Service (WMS) and a layer file of the Royal Commission Ancient Historic Monuments which includes information on board classes for: - Agriculture and Subsistence - Civil - Commemorative - Commercial - Defence - Domestic - Education - Gardens - Health - Maritime - Religious - Water Supply and Drainage - Unassigned\tRoyal Commission on the Ancient and Historical Monuments of Wales (RACHMW)\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-05-13T10:41:01.859Z\tnobody nobody\t-\tPublic record\n17183\tEXT_DS121965\t2024-05-28T12:15:59.327Z\t824\tUnassessed\tEditable\tUNESCO Geoparks (3rd Party Data)\t© Brecon Beacons National Park and Isle of Anglesey County Council. Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and owners copyright.  It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231393635\tX:\\Designations\\UNESCO\\UNESCO Geoparks.lyr\tGIS and Spatial Data Team\tUNESCO Global Geoparks are single, unified geographical areas where sites and landscapes of international geological significance are managed with a holistic concept of protection, education and sustainable development. Natural Resources Wales (NRW) has access to this dataset through the Breacon Beacons National Park Authority and Isle of Anglesey County Council  (IOACC).\tIsle of Anglesey County Council-Brecon Beacons National Park Authority\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T12:17:40.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17182\tEXT_DS121966\t2024-05-28T12:15:59.324Z\t687\tUnassessed\tEditable\tOffice of National Statistics (ONS): Police Authority Areas (3rd Party Data)\t© Office of National Statistics Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and owners copyright.  It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose.  Attribution Statement: Contains National Statistics data © Crown copyright and database right [2018]. Contains OS data © Crown copyright and database right [2018]\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231393636\tX:\\Designations\\Emergency Services\\Police Authority Areas.lyr  X:\\Basemapping\\Admin Boundaries\\Police Authority Areas.lyr\tGIS and Spatial Data Team\tThis dataset is wholly owned by Office of National Statistics (ONS) and licenced to Natural Resources Wales (NRW) under an Open Government Licence (OGL).\tOffice of National Statistics (ONS)\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-04-17T12:18:00.000Z\tnobody nobody\t-\tPublic record\n17181\tEXT_DS121968\t2024-05-28T12:15:58.964Z\t947\tUnassessed\tEditable\tWelsh Government: Conservation Zones (3rd Party Data)\t© Crown Copyright: Welsh Government. Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose.  Attribution Statement: © Crown copyright: Welsh Government\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231393638\tX:\\Designations\\Welsh Government\\Conservation Zones.lyr\tGIS and Spatial Data Team\tBoundaries of Conservation Areas in Wales, to conform with s.70(5) of the Planning (Listed Buildings and Conservation Areas) Act 1990.  This dataset provides information on the map boundaries only. For the full information, including information on designations, individuals should contact the appropriate Local Authority. This dataset is owned and managed by Welsh Government, and supplied to Natural Resources Wales (NRW) under an Open Government Licence (OGL).\tWelsh Government\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T12:24:03.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17242\tEXT_DS121969\t2024-05-28T12:17:32.753Z\t3\tUnassessed\tEditable\tWelsh Government: Agricultural Census (3rd Party Data)\tNRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231393639\tx:\\Resource Management\\Welsh Government\\Agricultural Census 1969.lyr  x:\\Resource Management\\Welsh Government\\Agricultural Census 1981.lyr  x:\\Resource Management\\Welsh Government\\Agricultural Census 1992.lyr  x:\\Resource Management\\Welsh Government\\Agricultural Census 1997.lyr\tGIS and Spatial Data Team\tThis dataset is supplied to Natural Resources Wales by Welsh Government. This is a statutory sample survey which is carried out annually by the Welsh Government to agricultural holdings in Wales as part of a UK wide exercise.\tWelsh Government\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T12:29:52.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPrivate record\n17244\tEXT_DS121970\t2024-05-28T12:17:32.806Z\t990\tUnassessed\tEditable\tWelsh Government: Environmentally Sensitive Areas (3rd Party Data)\t© Crown Copyright: Welsh Government. NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly. Attribution Statement: © Crown Copyright: Welsh Government. Contains Ordnance Survey data © Crown copyright and database right [2018]\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231393730\tx:\\Resource Management\\Welsh Government\\Environmentally Sensitive Areas Land Cover.lyr  x:\\Resource Management\\Welsh Government\\Environmentally Sensitive Areas.lyr  X:\\Resource Management\\Welsh Government\\Environmentally Sensitive Areas Farms.lyr\tGIS and Spatial Data Team\tThis dataset is owned and managed by Welsh Government and provided to Natural Resources Wales (NRW) under licence. The Environmentally Sensitive Areas were introduced in 1987 to offer incentives to encourage farmers to adopt agricultural practices which would safeguard and enhance parts of the country of particularly high landscape, wildlife or historic value. The scheme has now closed to new applicants.\tWelsh Government\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-07-08T08:24:53.000Z\tnobody nobody\t-\tPublic record\n17226\tEXT_DS121976\t2024-05-28T12:17:04.436Z\t259\tUnassessed\tEditable\tWelsh Government: Glastir Datasets (3rd Party Data)\t© Crown Copyright: Welsh Government NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly. Attribution Statement: © Crown copyright: Welsh Government; © Ordnance Survey 100021874\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231393736\tX:\\Resource Management\\Welsh Government See all those that are marked as Glastir\tGIS and Spatial Data Team\tGlastir is the Welsh Government\u0027s sustainable land management scheme, through which financial support is offered to farmers and land managers. It is funded by the Welsh Government’s Rural Development Programme 2014-20. It pays for the delivery of specific environmental goods and services aimed at: - combating climate change - improving water management - maintaining and enhancing biodiversity. This data collation consists of data associated with Glastir.  Natural Resources Wales (NRW) has access to the following Welsh Government owned Glastir datasets: - Glastir Planted Woodland Fencing - Glastir Planted Woodland - Glastir Woodland Creation - Glastir Water Quality Parcels - Glastir Freshwater Pearls Parcels - Glastir Advanced  - Glastir Entry  - Glastir bracken spraying  - Organic Farm Schemes\tWelsh Government\t2023-08-31\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T12:29:41.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17229\tEXT_DS121982\t2024-05-28T12:17:04.433Z\t390\tUnassessed\tEditable\tWelsh Government: Tir Cynnal and Tir Gofal (3rd Party Data)\t© Crown Copyright: Welsh Government NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly. Attribution Statement: © Crown copyright: Welsh Government © Crown Copyright and database right 2016. Ordnance Survey 100021874\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231393832\tx:\\Resource Management\\Welsh Government\\Tir Cynnal Agreement Areas.lyr  x:\\Resource Management\\Welsh Government\\Tir Cynnal Fields.lyr  x:\\Resource Management\\Welsh Government\\Tir Cynnal S15 2005 2006.lyr  x:\\Resource Management\\Welsh Government\\Tir Cynnal S15 2007 2008.lyr  x:\\Resource Management\\Welsh Government\\Tir Gofal Capital Works Line.lyr  x:\\Resource Management\\Welsh Government\\Tir Gofal Capital Works Points.lyr  x:\\Resource Management\\Welsh Government\\Tir Gofal Capital Works.lyr  x:\\Resource Management\\Welsh Government\\Tir Gofal Districts.lyr  x:\\Resource Management\\Welsh Government\\Tir Gofal Permissive Access Line.lyr  x:\\Resource Management\\Welsh Government\\Tir Gofal Permissive Access Points.lyr  x:\\Resource Management\\Welsh Government\\Tir Gofal Permissive Access.lyr  x:\\Resource Management\\Welsh Government\\Tir Gofal Signed Habitats.lyr  X:\\Resource Management\\Welsh Government\\Tir Gofal Whole Farm.lyr  X:\\Resource Management\\Welsh Government\\Tir Gofal Whole Farm.lyr  X:\\Resource Management\\Welsh Government\\Tir Gofal Whole Farm Features Points.lyr  X:\\Resource Management\\Welsh Government\\Tir Gofal Whole Farm Features Poly.lyr\tGIS and Spatial Data Team\tThis collation of datasets is owned and managed by Welsh Government. Natural Resources Wales (NRW) has access to this data via a licenced agreement. Tir Cynnal and Tir Gofal were welsh agri-environment schemes that have now been replaced by Glastir in 2013. These two schemes were aimed at improving habitat quality, supporting biodiversity, protecting our precious natural landscapes and historic features and adopting improved resource management to minimise water pollution. amongst other agri-environment benefits.\tWelsh Government\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T12:30:27.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17245\tEXT_DS121983\t2024-05-28T12:17:32.898Z\t678\tUnassessed\tEditable\tWelsh Government: Constituency Data (3rd Party Data)\t© Crown Copyright: Welsh Government. Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and copyright of the owners. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231393833\tX:\\Social Economic\\Administrative Boundaries\\Welsh Assembly Constituency Regions.lyr  X:\\Social Economic\\Administrative Boundaries\\Welsh Assembly Members.lyr  X:\\Social Economic\\Administrative Boundaries\\Westminster MP Constituencies.lyr X:\\Resource Management\\NRW Operational Areas\\Senedd Constituencies.lyr\tGIS and Spatial Data Team\tThis data collation is owned and managed by Welsh Government, licenced to Natural Resources Wales for use. These datasets detail the location and constituent regional boundaries across Wales.\tWelsh Government\t\t\tnull\thttps://datamap.gov.wales/layers/geonode:senedd_final_2026\t2026-02-03T15:13:52.000Z\tRachel Morris\t-\tPublic record\n17224\tEXT_DS121984\t2024-05-28T12:17:04.413Z\t913\tUnassessed\tEditable\tWelsh Government: Strategic Regeneration Areas (3rd Party Data)\t© Crown Copyright: Welsh Government. NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly. Attribution Statement: © Crown copyright: Welsh Government © Crown Copyright and database right 2016. Ordnance Survey 100021874\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231393834\tX:\\Social Economic\\Regeneration Areas\tGIS and Spatial Data Team\tThis data collation is owned and managed by Welsh Government and licenced to Natural Resources Wales for use. There are various areas across Wales that have been identified as Strategic Regeneration Areas. Strategic Regenerations Areas site under the Regeneration Framework, which has invested in regeneration schemes. Strategic Regeneration Areas fit in with the Wales Spatial Plan, and the Well-being of Future Generations Targets, which are about the sustainable development, and improving wellbeing and quality of life by integrating, social, economic and environmental objectives.\tWelsh Government\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-07-08T08:24:56.000Z\tnobody nobody\t-\tPublic record\n17240\tEXT_DS121990\t2024-05-28T12:17:05.570Z\t962\tUnassessed\tEditable\tWelsh Government: Technical Advice Note 8 (TAN8) Wind Energy Strategic Search Areas (3rd Party Data)\t© Crown Copyright: Welsh Government. Publically available data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and owners copyright. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose.. You must acknowledge the source of the information in your product or application by including or linking to the following attribution statement: Attribution Statement: © Crown copyright: Welsh Government and database right 2016. Ordnance Survey 100021874.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231393930\tX:\\Resource Management\\Welsh Government\\TAN8 Areas.lyr\tGIS and Spatial Data Team\tThis dataset is owned and managed by Welsh Government and is licenced to Natural Resources Wales (NRW) for use. Technical Advice Notes (TAN8) provides advice on areas including onshore renewable energy technologies, design and energy and how renewable energy should be accounted for as part of development plans, development management and monitoring processes.\tWelsh Government\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-04-17T12:30:13.000Z\tnobody nobody\t-\tPublic record\n17234\tEXT_DS121991\t2024-05-28T12:17:04.487Z\t698\tUnassessed\tEditable\tWelsh Government: Wales Spatial Plans (3rd Party Data)\t© Crown Copyright: Welsh Government Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and copyright of the owners.  It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose.  Attribution Statement: © Crown copyright: Welsh Government\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231393931\tFolder:  X:\\Social Economic\\Wales Spatial Plan\tGIS and Spatial Data Team\tThis is a Welsh Government owned data collation, which Natural Resources Wales (NRW) has access to via a licence agreement. The Planning and Compulsory Purchase Act 2004 placed a duty on the National Assembly for Wales to prepare a spatial plan. The Government of Wales Act 2006 further embeds the Wales Spatial Plan as a policy the Welsh Ministers must now agree and keep under review. For the purposes of the 2004 Act, this Update constitutes the Wales Spatial Plan. This dataset details the extent and location of boundaries for each spatial plan area across Wales.\tWelsh Government\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T12:29:56.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17243\tEXT_DS121993\t2024-05-28T12:17:32.794Z\t982\tUnassessed\tEditable\tWildlife Trust: Reserves (3rd Party Data)\t© Welsh Wildlife Trusts  NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset.  Attribution Statement: © Welsh Wildlife Trusts : Gwent Wildlife Trust, North Wales Wildlife Trust, Radnorshire Wildlife Trust, South and West Wales.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231393933\tx:\\Designations\\Wildlife Trusts\\Brecknock Wildlife Trust Reserves.lyr  x:\\Designations\\Wildlife Trusts\\Gwent Wildlife Trust Reserves.lyr  x:\\Designations\\Wildlife Trusts\\Monmouth Wildife Trust Reserves.lyr  x:\\Designations\\Wildlife Trusts\\North Wales Wildlife Trust Reserves.lyr  x:\\Designations\\Wildlife Trusts\\Radnorshire Wildlife Trust Reserves.lyr  x:\\Designations\\Wildlife Trusts\\South and West Wales WT Reserves.lyr\tGIS and Spatial Data Team\tThis is a collation of spatial datasets owned by the Wildlife Trusts in Wales licenced for use to Natural Resources Wales. This datasets show the location and distribution of reserves across Wales that are owned or managed by each Wildlife Trust.\tWildlife Trusts of South and West Wales-North Wales Wildlife Trust-Radnorshire Wildlife Trust-Gwent Wildlife Trust\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-04-17T10:01:43.000Z\tnobody nobody\t-\tPublic record\n17238\tEXT_DS121996\t2024-05-28T12:17:05.064Z\t512\tUnassessed\tEditable\tWoodland Trust: Woods for People (3rd Party Data)\t© Woodland Trust and Forestry Commission.  Attribution Statement: © Woodland Trust and ©Forestry Commission. © Ordnance survey for the OS derived data\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231393936\tx:\\Social Economic\\Woods for People\\Woods for People Version 11.lyr\tGIS and Spatial Data Team\tThis dataset is owned by the Woodland Trust and Forest Enterprise England, and licenced to Natural Resources Wales for use. The Woods for People project has created a UK-wide provisional inventory of accessible woodland. At present, it does not include woodlands where the only access is on public rights of way. For Scotland, the Land Reform Act gives a right of responsible access to almost all land, but the dataset only includes woods that encourage access.\tWoodland Trust-Forest Enterprise\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T13:06:20.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17230\tEXT_DS122014\t2024-05-28T12:17:04.431Z\t489\tUnassessed\tEditable\tKeep Wales Tidy: Seaside Awards (3rd Party Data)\t© Keep Wales Tidy NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313232303134\tX:\\EU Directives\\Bathing Waters Directive\\Seaside Award.lyr\tHelena Sykes - GIS and Spatial Data Team\tThis spatial dataset show the location fo beaches in Wales that have been awarded with a Seaside Award. The Seaside Award is the nationwide standard for the best beaches across the UK. While Seaside Award beaches can be vastly different, the flag is a symbol of quality which ensures visitors are guaranteed to find a clean, attractive and well managed coastal stretch.\tKeep Wales Tidy\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T12:29:45.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17239\tEXT_DS122088\t2024-05-28T12:17:05.148Z\t463\tUnassessed\tEditable\tEnvironment Agency: All Wales 2017 Saltmarsh Extent (WFD Cycle 3) (3rd Party Data)\t© Environment Agency Data may be re-used under the terms of the 3rd Party Suppliers Open Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and owners copyright. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313232303838\tX:\\Monitoring\\Marine\\Saltmarsh Areas\\All Wales 2017 Saltmarsh Extent (WFD Cycle 3).lyr\tMarine Monitoring Officer\tWater Framework Directive saltmarsh monitoring. Saltmarsh extents determined in a desk based study using aerial imagery. This data is Open, but owned by the Environment Agency.\tEnvironment Agency (EA)\t2017-12-13\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2026-01-12T12:35:29.000Z\tMonica Jones\t-\tPublic record\n17233\tEXT_DS122097\t2024-05-28T12:17:04.469Z\t754\tUnassessed\tEditable\tLocal Environmental Records Centre (LERC) Wales: Invasive Non Native Species (INNS) (3rd Party Data)\t© Cofnod, WWBIC, BIS, SEWBReC NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originators directly.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313232303937\tX:\\Biological\\Local Record Centres\\LRC Invasive non native species points.lyr  X:\\Biological\\Local Record Centres\\LRC Invasive non native species polygon.lyr\tInternal Custodian: Jennie Jones, Specialist Advisor, Non-Native Species Internal Custodian: Barnaby Letheren, Lead Specialist Advisor, Knowledge \u0026amp; Information Management  Contact GIS and Spatial Data Team for more info\tThis spatial data collation is supplied by the Local Environmental Records Centres in Wales who are the data collator and copyright holders. The information Natural Resources Wales (NRW) has access to as part of a licence with the Local Environmental Records Centre in Wales, is only part of the full record. Further details on each observation can be obtained from the data collator. Ownership of the record remains with the original recorder.\tCofnod (North Wales Environmental Information Service)\t2026-02-02\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2026-02-02T14:09:13.000Z\tMichael Goodrich\t-\tPublic record\n17228\tEXT_DS122123\t2024-05-28T12:17:04.424Z\t393\tUnassessed\tEditable\tOceanWise: Nautical Boundaries (3rd Party Data)\tNRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset.  Attribution Statement: © British Crown and OceanWise Ltd, 2013. All rights reserved. License No. EK001-20120402\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313232313233\tx:\\Basemapping\\Admin Boundaries\\Nautical limits.lyr  x:\\Basemapping\\Admin Boundaries\\Marine plan area Wales WGS84.lyr\tGIS and Spatial Data Team\tThis collation of datasets is managed and owned by OceanWise and licenced to NRW for internal use only. This data collation consists of two layers detailing the extent of Welsh waters and jurisdiction boundaries at 3, 6 and 12 nautical miles.\tUnited Kingdom Hydrographic Office (UKHO)\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T12:27:15.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17237\tEXT_DS122152\t2024-05-28T12:17:04.929Z\t2\tUnassessed\tEditable\tHM Land Registry: Spatial Data (3rd Party Data)\tNRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313232313532\tX:\\Ownership\\Land Registry\\Land Registry Polygons.lyr\tGIS and Spatial Data Team\tThis dataset is wholly owned by the Land Registry and has been licenced to Natural Resources Wales (NRW) for use. This dataset contains the extent and location of parcels of land that have been allocated a land registry title number.\tHM Land Registry\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T12:30:20.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPrivate record\n17241\tEXT_DS122161\t2024-05-28T12:17:31.921Z\t1176\tUnassessed\tEditable\tDŵr Cymru Cyf / Welsh Water (DCWW): Asset Management Plans (3rd Party Data)\t© Dŵr Cymru Cyf / Welsh Water. NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313232313631\tx:\\Resource Management\\Water Quality\\AMP2 DCWW Improvements.lyr  x:\\Resource Management\\Water Quality\\AMP3 DCWW Improvements.lyr  x:\\Resource Management\\Water Quality\\AMP3 DCWW sewage works continuous.lyr  x:\\Resource Management\\Water Quality\\AMP3 DCWW sewage works intermittant.lyr  x:\\Resource Management\\Water Quality\\AMP4 DCWW Improvements.lyr  x:\\Resource Management\\Water Quality\\AMP4 Removed Schemes.lyr  x:\\Resource Management\\Water Quality\\AMP5 DCWW Improvements.lyr  x:\\Utilities\\Water\\AMP2 DCWW (1995-2000).lyr  x:\\Utilities\\Water\\AMP3 DCWW (2000-2005).lyr  x:\\Utilities\\Water\\AMP4 DCWW (2005-2010).lyr  x:\\Utilities\\Water\\AMP4 Removed Schemes.lyr  x:\\Utilities\\Water\\AMP5 DCWW (2010-2015).lyr\tGIS and Saptial Data Team\tThis dataset is wholly owned by Dŵr Cymru Cyf / Welsh Water and is licenced to Natural Resources Wales for internal use only. Dŵr Cymru Cyf / Welsh Water is a regulared water and sewerage company.\tDwr Cymru Welsh Water\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2026-02-26T15:22:58.000Z\tMonica Jones\t-\tPublic record\n17236\tEXT_DS122162\t2024-05-28T12:17:04.822Z\t1562\tUnassessed\tEditable\tDŵr Cymru Cyf / Welsh Water (DCWW): Utilities Water Assets and Ownership (3rd Party Data)\t© Dŵr Cymru Cyf / Welsh Water. NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313232313632\tx:\\Utilities\\Water\\DCWW Foul above ground assets.lyr  x:\\Utilities\\Water\\DCWW Groundwater abstraction catchments.lyr  x:\\Utilities\\Water\\DCWW Potable above ground assets.lyr  x:\\Utilities\\Water\\DCWW Potable Line.lyr  x:\\Utilities\\Water\\DCWW Reservoir Catchments.lyr  x:\\Utilities\\Water\\DCWW River Intake Catchments.lyr  x:\\Utilities\\Water\\DCWW Sewer AGA.lyr  x:\\Utilities\\Water\\DCWW Sewer Catchments.lyr  x:\\Utilities\\Water\\DCWW Sewer Chambers.lyr  x:\\Utilities\\Water\\DCWW Sewer Discharge Points.lyr  x:\\Utilities\\Water\\DCWW Sewer Network.lyr  x:\\Utilities\\Water\\DCWW Sewer Structures.lyr  x:\\Utilities\\Water\\DCWW Water Control Valves.lyr  x:\\Utilities\\Water\\DCWW Water Hydrants Washouts.lyr  x:\\Utilities\\Water\\DCWW Water Network Structures.lyr  x:\\Utilities\\Water\\DCWW Water Network.lyr\tGIS and Spatial Data Team\tThis dataset is wholly owned by Dŵr Cymru Cyf / Welsh Water and licenced to Natural Resources Wales (NRW) for internal use. This details the extent and location of various utilities managed or owned by Dŵr Cymru Cyf / Welsh Water.\tDwr Cymru Welsh Water\t2025-12-09\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-12-09T14:31:40.000Z\tGary Eccleston\t-\tPublic record\n17232\tEXT_DS122163\t2024-05-28T12:17:04.412Z\t751\tUnassessed\tEditable\tDŵr Cymru Cyf / Welsh Water: MCERTS Effluent Flow Monitoring Sites (3rd Party Data)\t© Dŵr Cymru Cyf / Welsh Water. NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313232313633\tX:\\Resource Management\\Water Quality\\MCerts DCWW Effluent Flow Monitoring.lyr  x:\\Monitoring\\Sampling Points\\MCerts Effluent Flow Monitoring.lyr   The original source of this data is WISKI\tGIS and Spatial Data Team\tThis dataset is wholly owned by Dŵr Cymru Cyf / Welsh Water and licenced to NRW for internal use. As part of a permit requirements issued by Natural Resources Wales, Dŵr Cymru Cyf / Welsh Water are required to monitoring the Dry Weather Flow or Maximum Daily Volume of discharge as part of their Effluent Flow Monitoring. As part of this Dŵr Cymru Cyf / Welsh Water must comply with MCERTS Flow Monitoring Schemes which records the total daily volume of discharge. This dataset details the locations of these monitoring sites managed by Dŵr Cymru Cyf / Welsh Water.\tDwr Cymru Welsh Water\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-12-01T11:56:35.000Z\tGary Eccleston\t-\tPublic record\n17227\tEXT_DS122164\t2024-05-28T12:17:04.399Z\t22\tUnassessed\tEditable\tGwent Wildlife Trust: Vole Raft Locations (3rd Party Data)\t© Gwent Wildlife Trust NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313232313634\tX:\\Biological\\Gwent Wildlife Trust\\GWT Water Vole Raft Locations.lyr\tInternal Custodian: Rebecca Clews-Roberts, Specialist Advisor: Terrestrial Habitats \u0026amp; Species, Terrestrial Ecosystems \u0026amp; Species Team\tThis dataset is wholly owned by the Gwent Wildlife Trust and licenced to Natural Resources Wales (NRW) for internal use. This dataset details the location of vole rafts collected by the Gwent Wildlife Trust pre 2015.  Water Voles (Arvicola amphibius) are protected in Wales under Schedule 5 of the Wildlife and Countryside Act 1981, Section 42 of the Natural Environment and Rural Communities (NERC) Act making them a \u0027species of principal importance to Wales\u0027, and they are a UK Biodiversity Action Plan (BAP) Priority species. As part of their feed habits, Voles create feeding rafts. These are piles of cut vegetation that will be think enough for a vole to site on in the water. These are most typically found next to areas where suitable vegetation emerges directly from the water.\tGwent Wildlife Trust\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2026-01-12T17:02:23.000Z\tMonica Jones\t-\tPrivate record\n17235\tEXT_DS122165\t2024-05-28T12:17:04.640Z\t744\tUnassessed\tEditable\tWelsh Government: Assisted Areas Objectives (3rd Party Data)\t© Crown Copyright: Welsh Government. NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly. Attirbution Statement: © Crown copyright: Welsh Government  © Ordnance Survey 100021874.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313232313635\tx:\\Resource Management\\Welsh Government\\Objective 1.lyr  x:\\Resource Management\\Welsh Government\\Objective 2 Trans.lyr  x:\\Resource Management\\Welsh Government\\Objective 2.lyr  x:\\Resource Management\\Welsh Government\\Objective 3.lyr  x:\\Resource Management\\Welsh Government\\Objective 5 Tran.lyr\tGIS and Spatial Data Team\tThis dataset is wholly owned by Welsh Government and supplied to NRW under an licence agreement. These dataset feed into the Assisted Areas which are places where government can offer additional financial support to businesses under European Commission state aid rules. Assisted areas are recognised in European state aid rules as being less economically advantaged places that would benefit from additional support for development. As a result, financial support from Government is permitted to undertakings, typically businesses, for new investments in these areas. Being located in an Assisted Area does not confer any right to financial assistance; rather, it allows the public sector to provide certain types of assistance if it wishes. These areas have been split into regional areas where the level of funding allocated is defined by the objective number.\tWelsh Government\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T13:02:03.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17231\tEXT_DS122166\t2024-05-28T12:17:04.453Z\t1660\tUnassessed\tEditable\tDŵr Cymru Cyf / Welsh Water: South Wales Fire Hydrants (3rd Party Data)\t© Dŵr Cymru Cyf / Welsh Water NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313232313636\tx:\\Designations\\Emergency Services\\South Wales Fire Hydrants.lyr\tGIS and Spatial Data Team\tThis dataset has been supplied to Natural Resources Wales via Welsh Government and is owned by Dŵr Cymru Cyf / Welsh Water. This dataset details the location of fire hydrants around South Wales.\tDwr Cymru Welsh Water\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-03-21T10:26:03.920Z\tnobody nobody\t-\tPublic record\n17220\tEXT_DS122167\t2024-05-28T12:17:03.811Z\t717\tUnassessed\tEditable\tLocal Authority: Cycling and Walking Routes (3rd Party Data)\t© Denbighshire County Council, Monmouthshire County Council and Conwy County Borough Council NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313232313637\tx:\\Recreation and Access\\Cycling and walking routes\\Denbigh Conwy Mountain Bike Routes.lyr  x:\\Recreation and Access\\Cycling and walking routes\\Denbigh Cycle Routes.lyr  x:\\Recreation and Access\\Cycling and walking routes\\Monmouth Cycle Routes.lyr\tGIS and Spatial Data Team\tThis data collation is jointly owned by the Denbighshire County Council, Conwy County Borough Council and Monmouthshire County Council and was provided to Natural Resources Wales for use. It details the extent and location of of cycling routes around Denbigh and Monmouth.\tDenbighshire County Council-Monmouthshire County Council-Conwy County Borough Council\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-07-08T08:24:53.000Z\tnobody nobody\t-\tPublic record\n17222\tEXT_DS122193\t2024-05-28T12:17:04.327Z\t303\tUnassessed\tEditable\tWelsh Government: Habitat Land Cover (3rd Party Data)\t© Crown Copyright: Welsh Government NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly.  Attribution Statement: © Crown copyright: Welsh Government © Ordnance Survey 100021874\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313232313933\tX:\\Resource Management\\Welsh Government\\Habitat Land Cover.lyr\tGIS and Spatial Data Team\tThis is a Welsh Government owned dataset licenced to Natural Resources Wales (NRW) for use. This spatial dataset details the extent and location of Habitat Land Cover for Ty Gofal agri-environment schemes.\tWelsh Government\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T13:06:23.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17225\tEXT_DS122194\t2024-05-28T12:17:04.406Z\t2\tUnassessed\tEditable\tForestry Commission Great Britain (FCGB): Recreation Designations (3rd Party Data)\t© Forestry Commission UK NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset. Those seeking such permission should approach the originator directly.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313232313934\tx:\\Recreation and Access\\Designated Areas\\GB Recreation Designations.lyr\tKeith Harri Jones  GIS and Spatial Data Team\tThis dataset is wholly owned by Forestry Commission Great Britain (FCGB) and is licenced to Natural Resources Wales (NRW) for use. This spatial datasets shows the extent and locaiton of designated recreational forestry sites around Great Britain.\t\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2026-01-12T16:48:35.000Z\tMonica Jones\t-\tPrivate record\n17223\tEXT_DS122284\t2024-05-28T12:17:04.289Z\t772\tUnassessed\tEditable\tEnvironment Agency (EA): River Quality Objectives (RQO) Compliance (3rd Party Data)\t© Environment Agency  Data may be re-used under the terms of the 3rd Party Data Sharing Agreement.  Attribution statement: © Environment Agency copyright and/or database right 2015. All rights reserved.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313232323834\tX:\\Monitoring\\River Quality Assessment Sampling (Historic)\\RQO Compliance.lyr\tGIS and Spatial Data Team\tThis dataset is owned by Enivronment Agency (EA). Natural Resources Wales (NRW) has access to this data as part of a Data Sharing Agreement with EA. River Quality Objectives (RQOs) were based on the River Ecosystem (RE) Classification Scheme which was introduced in 1994 to replace the National Water Council\u0027s methodology.\tEnvironment Agency (EA)\t2006-12-31\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T12:27:10.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17221\tEXT_DS122285\t2024-05-28T12:17:04.173Z\t931\tUnassessed\tEditable\tRoyal Yatching Association (RYA): UK Coastal Atlas of Recreational Boating (3rd Party Data)\t© Royal Yachting Association Data for internal use. NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset.  Attribution Statement: © Royal Yachting Association\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313232323835\tX:\\Recreation and Access\\RYA UK Coastal Atlas of Recreational Boating 2\tGIS and Spatial Data Team  Laura Grant was the person who orginally wanted the data. Kate Griffith has requested the 1 year extension to Feb 2021       Licencse renegotiated and signed 12 Feb 2020 to hold for 1 year  until Feb 2021\tThis dataset is wholly owned by the Royal Yachting Association (RYA). The Royal Yachting Association (RYA) UK Coastal Atlas of Recreational Boating is a GIS dataset of recreational boating activity around the UK, comprising spatial data including indicators of intensity of use, general boating areas, offshore routes, as well as the locations of clubs, training centres and marinas\tRoyal Yatching Association (RYA)\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-07-08T08:24:53.000Z\tnobody nobody\t-\tPublic record\n17215\tEXT_DS122392\t2024-05-28T12:17:03.539Z\t1170\tUnassessed\tEditable\tOrdnance Survey: Open Data (3rd Party Data)\t© Ordnance Survey Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and copyright of the owners. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose. Attribution Statement: You must acknowledge the copyright and the source of the data, as follows: Contains OS data © Crown copyright and database right [year] If you use Code-Point Open data, you must also display the following: Contains Royal Mail data © Royal Mail copyright and Database right [year] / Contains National Statistics data © Crown copyright and database right [year]\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313232333932\tx:\\Basemapping\\Ordnance Survey Mapping\\ESRI hosted OS data\\OS Open Background.lyr  x:\\Basemapping\\Ordnance Survey Mapping\\ESRI hosted OS data\\OS Open carto.lyr  x:\\Basemapping\\Ordnance Survey Mapping\\ESRI hosted OS data\\OS Open greyscales.lyr  x:\\Basemapping\\Ordnance Survey Mapping\\ESRI hosted OS data\\OS Open Raster.lyr  x:\\Basemapping\\Ordnance Survey Mapping\\ESRI hosted OS data\\OS VML carto.lyr  x:\\Basemapping\\Ordnance Survey Mapping\\OS Products\\OS Open Greenspace.lyr  X:\\Basemapping\\Ordnance Survey Mapping\\OS Products\\OS Open Rivers.lyr  X:\\Basemapping\\Ordnance Survey Mapping\\OS Products\\OS Open Roads.lyr  x:\\Basemapping\\Addressing\\OS Open Names.lyr  X:\\Basemapping\\Admin Boundaries\\Unitary Authorities Wales.lyr\tGIS and Spatial Data Team\tThis dataset is wholly owned by Ordnance Survey (OS) and licenced for use by Natural Resources Wales (NRW) via an open data licence issued by OS. OS open data products (OS OpenData) are a set of free digital maps of Great Britain, available for anyone to use, for any purpose. The maps include data on roads, rivers and boundaries. This dataset includes layers derived from those available from OS.\tOrdnance Survey (OS)\t\t\tnull\thttps://osdatahub.os.uk/downloads/open\t2025-11-14T13:37:44.000Z\tMonica Jones\t-\tPublic record\n17218\tEXT_DS122402\t2024-05-28T12:17:03.627Z\t699\tUnassessed\tEditable\tDŵr Cymru Cyf / Welsh Water: Reservoir Asset Data (3rd Party Data)\t© Dŵr Cymru Cyf / Welsh Water. NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313232343032\tCronfeydd Database\tMatt O\u0027Brian is the custodian\tThis dataset is owned by Dŵr Cymru Cyf / Welsh Water and licenced to Natural Resources Wales (NRW) for internal use. Welsh Water owns 91 reservoirs varying in size from 2 acres to 1026 acres.\tDwr Cymru Welsh Water\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-07-08T08:24:54.000Z\tnobody nobody\t-\tPublic record\n17219\tEXT_DS122406\t2024-05-28T12:17:03.633Z\t0\tUnassessed\tEditable\tDŵr Cymru Cyf / Welsh Water: Reservoir Level Data Weekly (3rd Party Data)\t© Dŵr Cymru Cyf / Welsh Water NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313232343036\tDMS Location:   https://cyfoethnaturiolcymru.sharepoint.com/:f:/r/teams/waterman/wrmr/ww/Reservoir%20Storage%20Data/Weekly%20DCWW%20data?csf\u003d1\tdata contact - Zhong Zhang\tThis dataset is supplied to Natural Resources Wales (NRW) by Dŵr Cymru Cyf / Welsh Water. Welsh Water owns 91 reservoirs varying in size from 2 acres to 1026 acres.\tDwr Cymru Welsh Water\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T12:13:59.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPrivate record\n17214\tEXT_DS122412\t2024-05-28T12:17:03.535Z\t559\tUnassessed\tEditable\tCanal and River Trust: Water Level and Flow Data held in WISKI 7 Core Hydro and Telemetry (3rd Party Data)\tNRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313232343132\tThis data is held in the Hydro part of WISKI\tAlison Hanson - Team Leader for this area of work  Liam Perrott - technical specialist for hydrometry       Data from 2014 in Water Resources Team DMS location.\tReservoir storage data is recorded by Canal and River Trust. Weekly reading of reservoir storage volume (Million litres) and % storage.\tCanal and River Trust\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T12:13:44.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17212\tEXT_DS122416\t2024-05-28T12:17:03.417Z\t972\tUnassessed\tEditable\tEnvironment Agency (EA): River Level, River Flow, Groundwater Level and Rainfall Data held in WISKI 7 Core Hydro and Telemetry (3rd Party Data)\t© Environment Agency  NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313232343136\tThis data is help within the hydro modules in WISKI\tAlison Hanson - Team Leader for this area of work  Liam Perrott - technical specialist for hydrometry       Data from 2014 in Water Resources Team DMS location.\tHydrometric data collected by the Enivronment Agency (EA) at locations in the vicinity of the England / Wales border.  Data is collected by EA and therefore owned by EA.  Due to proximity to Wales, often located within cross border river catchments, Natural Resources Wales (NRW) also have an interest, and operational use for the data.\tEnvironment Agency (EA)\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T12:05:03.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17217\tEXT_DS122442\t2024-05-28T12:17:03.583Z\t328\tUnassessed\tEditable\tMarine Recorder Snapshot supplied by Joint Nature Conservation Committee (JNCC) (3rd Party Data)\tThis dataset is owned by various third party organisations and is compiled and distributed by JNCC. NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313232343432\tH:\\Science\\MFSG\\MarineRecorder\tBryan Tozer - or Monica Jones Data Services Team\tMarine Recorder is the database application used by Joint Nature Conservation Committee (JNCC) and the organisations, such as Natural Resources Wales (NRW), to store marine benthic sample data such as species, physical attributes and biotopes. JNCC periodically compiles and combines all local Marine Recorder Snapshots into a single UK-wide version and supplies this to NRW, so they can incorporate it into their version of Marine Recorder. JNCC compile the data from various third party providers, including but not limited to various country agencies.\tVarious\t\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-04-17T09:58:00.000Z\tnobody nobody\t-\tPublic record\n17216\tEXT_DS122465\t2024-05-28T12:17:03.561Z\t630\tUnassessed\tEditable\tDŵr Cymru Cyf / Welsh Water: Reservoir Storage Data held in WISKI 7 Core Hydro and Telemetry (3rd Party Data)\t© Dŵr Cymru Cyf / Welsh Water NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313232343635\tData is held in WISKI Hydro Module.\tAlison Hanson - Team Leader for this area of work  Liam Perrott - technical specialist for hydrometry       Data from 2014 in Water Resources Team DMS location.\tReservoir storage data is recorded by Dŵr Cymru Cyf / Welsh Water. Weekly reading of reservoir storage volume (Million litres) and % storage.\tDwr Cymru Welsh Water\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T12:23:42.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17213\tEXT_DS122466\t2024-05-28T12:17:03.533Z\t990\tUnassessed\tEditable\tSevern Trent Water (STW): Reservoir Storage Data held in WISKI 7 Core Hydro and Telemetry (3rd Party Data)\t© Severn Trent Water (STW) NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313232343636\tData is held in WISKI Hydro Module.\tAlison Hanson - Team Leader for this area of work  Liam Perrott - technical specialist for hydrometry       Data from 2014 in Water Resources Team DMS location.\tReservoir storage data is recorded by Severn Trent Water (STW). Weekly reading of reservoir storage volume (Million litres) and % storage.\tSevern Trent Water Ltd\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-07-08T08:24:54.000Z\tnobody nobody\t-\tPublic record\n17211\tEXT_DS122467\t2024-05-28T12:17:03.274Z\t873\tUnassessed\tEditable\tUnited Utilities (UU): Reservoir Storage Data held in WISKI 7 Core Hydro and Telemetry (3rd Party Data)\t© United Utilities  NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate this dataset.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313232343637\tData is held in WISKI Hydro Module.\tAlison Hanson - Team Leader for this area of work  Liam Perrott - technical specialist for hydrometry       Data from 2014 in Water Resources Team DMS location.\tReservoir storage data is recorded by United Utilities. Weekly reading of reservoir storage volume (Million litres) and % storage.\tUnited Utilities\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T12:23:48.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17258\tEXT_DS122471\t2024-05-28T12:18:11.467Z\t306\tUnassessed\tEditable\tLocal Authorities (3rd Party Data)\t© Ordnance Survey Data may be re-used under the terms of the 3rd Party Suppliers Open Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and owners copyright. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313232343731\tX:\\Basemapping\\Admin Boundaries\\Unitary Authorities.lyr\tGIS and Spatial Services Team\tThis data shows the Local (Unitary) Authority boundaries for Wales.\tOrdnance Survey-Ordnance Survey (OS)\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2026-02-26T15:23:51.000Z\tMonica Jones\t-\tPublic record\n17268\tEXT_DS122505\t2024-05-28T12:18:11.759Z\t535\tUnassessed\tEditable\tEnvironment Agency: All Wales 2017 Saltmarsh Zonation Points (WFD Cycle 3) (3rd Party Data)\t© Environment Agency Data may be re-used under the terms of the 3rd Party Suppliers Open Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and owners copyright.  It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended p