\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T10:45:23.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPrivate record\n18695\tNRW_DS123301\t2024-05-28T12:54:22.228Z\t1\tUnassessed\tEditable\tVaccinnium Dominant Open Habitats\t© CNC/NRW Data may only be re-used externally under provision and in line with the terms of a NRW licence following an assessment of the data.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313233333031\tx:\\Incidents\\Forest Health\\Vaccinnium Dominant Open Habitats.lyr\tKeith Harri Jones\t\t\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T10:45:23.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPrivate record\n18689\tNRW_DS123302\t2024-05-28T12:54:22.101Z\t1\tUnassessed\tEditable\tWoodland Types Vaccinnium\t© CNC/NRW Data may only be re-used externally under provision and in line with the terms of a NRW licence following an assessment of the data.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313233333032\tx:\\Incidents\\Forest Health\\Woodland Types Vaccinnium.lyr\tKeith Harri Jones\t\t\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T09:59:10.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPrivate record\n18698\tNRW_DS123303\t2024-05-28T12:54:22.397Z\t670\tValid\tEditable\tKiEco Freshwater Ecology: Diatoms\t© CNC/NRW. Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and NRW\u0027s copyright. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313233333033\tData Held in KiEco.  A CSV copy in DarwinCore can be found here - Z:\\Archive\\Knowledge Data \u0026amp; Information Mgmt\\Data Mgmt\\Data Services Data Publishing Area\\NBN Data\\NRW_DS123303_Diatoms\tInternal Custodian:  Advisor 2 - Data Services Team and Jennifer Owen - Senior Environmental Assessment Officer\tFreshwater diatoms (phytobenthos) are free-living microscopic plants that form a biofilm on submerged substrates such as rock/stone or large plants. They are used as an indicator of water quality because their silica shells are easy to identify under the microscope. This dataset is made up of the relative abundance of different species within the sample from freshwater diatom surveys conducted across Wales by Natural Resources Wales and former Environment Agency Wales. These surveys are conducted as part of on-going monitoring of river water quality for legislative requirements and to meet business drivers.  A geospatial version of this dataset is available to download from DataMapWales. Please see metadata NRW_DS125742 for more information.\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)\t2020-03-09-2025-09-02\tcreation-publication\tnull\thttps://registry.nbnatlas.org/public/show/dp122\t2025-12-01T17:41:00.000Z\tRachel Morris\tGEMINI\tPublic record\n18691\tNRW_DS123304\t2024-05-28T12:54:22.222Z\t6\tUnassessed\tEditable\tHistoric NIRS Incidents (EAW) April 2001 to March 2013\t© CNC/NRW Data may only be re-used externally under provision and in line with the terms of a NRW licence following an assessment of the data.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313233333034\tx:\\Incidents\\National Incident Recording System (NIRS)\\Historic NIRS Incidents (EAW) April 2001 to March 2013.lyr\tJohn Farnhill\t\t\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T10:45:14.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPrivate record\n18703\tNRW_DS123305\t2024-05-28T12:54:22.389Z\t6\tUnassessed\tEditable\tNIRS Incidents\t© CNC/NRW Data may only be re-used externally under provision and in line with the terms of a NRW licence following an assessment of the data.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313233333035\tx:\\Incidents\\National Incident Recording System (NIRS)\\NIRS Incidents.lyr\tJohn Farnhill\t\t\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-07-09T16:23:09.000Z\tRachel Morris\t-\tPrivate record\n18699\tNRW_DS123306\t2024-05-28T12:54:22.410Z\t1\tUnassessed\tEditable\tOil spill booming plans\t© CNC/NRW Data may only be re-used externally under provision and in line with the terms of a NRW licence following an assessment of the data.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313233333036\tx:\\Incidents\\Oil Spills\\Oil spill booming plans.lyr\tAndrew Hill\t\t\t\t\tnull\tnul