NRW Land\\NRW Forest Deeds - Disposals.lyr   Acquisition and Disposal Record Map Scans archive held on G:\\FCData\\Aberystwyth\\EstateManagement\\A and D. Record Map Scans to be moved to Z drive.\tPrimary Metadata contact: Ian Medcalf, GIS Technician 4, NRW Secondary Metadata contact: Arpana Chunilal / Geraint Morgan\tThis dataset illustrates the acquisitions \u0026amp; disposals that have created the NRW Managed Forestry Estate as we know it today. This information is obtained from the Deed Management System which has been designed for the maintenance and reporting of the NRW land holdings.\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)\t2023-06-30\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T12:56:12.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPrivate record\n18706\tNRW_DS123366\t2024-05-28T12:54:49.754Z\t2\tUnassessed\tEditable\tNRW properties\t© CNC/NRW Data may only be re-used externally under provision and in line with the terms of a NRW licence following an assessment of the data.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313233333636\tx:\\Ownership\\NRW Properties\\NRW properties.lyr\tIan Medcalf, Technical Support (4) GIS, Estates, North \u0026amp; Mid Wales Operations\tThe Geospatial Services Team do not currently hold any information for this section. If you are the custodian, please contact the team so we can populate this field.\t\t2020-10-22\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T10:45:10.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPrivate record\n18749\tNRW_DS123367\t2024-05-28T12:55:20.596Z\t688\tUnassessed\tEditable\tAll Wales Hydrological Analysis Catchments\t© CNC/NRW Data may only be re-used externally under provision and in line with the terms of a NRW licence following an assessment of the data.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313233333637\tx:\\Physical\\Hydrological\\Hydro Tools\\allwales_cat.lyr\tBen Anscombe\tThis layer was created to point to rasters used in NRW hydrological analysis tools. They are based upon the flow direction models which were created by the Environment Agency Detailed River Network which subsequently passed to NRW.  The All Wales Hydrological Analysis Catchments is generated for each area above a threshold area from the following related datasets: NRW_DS123368 NRW_DS123369 NRW_DS123370 NRW_DS123371\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-07-08T09:06:50.000Z\tnobody nobody\t-\tPublic record\n18758\tNRW_DS123368\t2024-05-28T12:55:20.709Z\t772\tUnassessed\tEditable\tAll Wales Hydrological Analysis Flow Accumulation Raster\t© CNC/NRW Data may only be re-used externally under provision and in line with the terms of a NRW licence following an assessment of the data.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313233333638\tx:\\Physical\\Hydrological\\Hydro Tools\\allwales_fac.lyr\tBen Anscombe\tThis layer was created to point to rasters used in NRW hydrological analysis tools. They are based upon the flow direction models which were created by the Environment Agency Detailed River Network which subsequently passed to NRW.    The Flow Accumulation Raster is a count for each cell a count of how many other cells flow to it.\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T12:59:10.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n18754\tNRW_DS123369\t2024-05-28T12:55:20.676Z\t351\tUnassessed\tEditable\tAll Wales Hydrological Analysis Flow Direction Raster\t© CNC/NRW Data may only be re-used externally under provision and in line with the terms of a NRW licence following an assessment of the data.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313233333639\tx:\\Physical\\Hydrological\\Hydro Tools\\allwales_fdr.lyr\tBen Anscombe\tThis layer was created to point to rasters used in NRW hydrological analysis tools. They are based upon the flow direction models which were created by the Environment Agency Detailed River Network which subsequently passed to NRW.  For each cell in a raster the All Wales Hydrological Analysis Flow Direction Raster assigns a value indicating which adjacent cell surface water would be expected to flow to.\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T12:59:10.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n18757\tNRW_DS123370\t2024-05-28T12:55:20.710Z\t372\tUnassessed\tEditable\tAll Wales Hydrological Analysis Stream Link\t© CNC/NRW Data may only be re-used externally under provision and in line with the terms of a NRW licence following an assessment of the data.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313233333730\tx:\\Physical\\Hydrological\\Hydro Tools\\allwales_lnk.lyr\tBen Anscombe\tThis layer was created to point to rasters used in NRW hydrological analysis tools. They are based upon the flow direction models which were created by the Environment Agency Detailed River Network which subsequently passed to NRW.  All Wales Hydrological Analysis Stream Link shows the cells representing the All Wales Hydrological Analysis Stream Network (NRW_DS123371) but aggregated together to indicate discrete dendritic areas.\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-07-08T09:06:52.000Z\tnobody nobody\t-\tPublic record\n18763\tNRW_DS123371\t2024-05-28T12:55:20.709Z\t694\tUnassessed\tEditable\tAll Wales Hydrological Analysis Stream Network\t© CNC/NRW Data may only be re-used externally under provision and in line with the terms of a NRW licence following an assessment of the data.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313233333731\tx:\\Physical\\Hydrological\\Hydro Tools\\allwales_str.lyr\tBen Anscombe\tThis layer was created to point to rasters used in NRW hydrological analysis tools. They are based upon the flow direction models which were created by the Environment Agency Detailed River Network which subsequently passed to NRW.  The All Wales Hydrological Analysis Stream Network is based upon a threshold of the flow accumulation raster (NRW_DS123368)\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T12:59:44.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n18748\tNRW_DS123372\t2024-05-28T12:55:20.593Z\t9\tUnassessed\tEditable\tDEM 5m\t© CNC/NRW Data may only be re-used externally under provision and in line with the terms of