2\\EP2 Decrease in Emergence Regime.lyr  x:\\Resource Management\\Climate Vulnerability\\Marine Habitat Vulnerability\\EP2\\EP2 Decrease in Suspended Sediment.lyr  x:\\Resource Management\\Climate Vulnerability\\Marine Habitat Vulnerability\\EP2\\EP2 Decrease in Turbidity.lyr  x:\\Resource Management\\Climate Vulnerability\\Marine Habitat Vulnerability\\EP2\\EP2 Decrease in Water Flow Rate.lyr  x:\\Resource Management\\Climate Vulnerability\\Marine Habitat Vulnerability\\EP2\\EP2 Decrease in Wave Exposure.lyr  x:\\Resource Management\\Climate Vulnerability\\Marine Habitat Vulnerability\\EP2\\EP2 Increase in Emergence Regime.lyr  x:\\Resource Management\\Climate Vulnerability\\Marine Habitat Vulnerability\\EP2\\EP2 Increase in Suspended Sediment.lyr  x:\\Resource Management\\Climate Vulnerability\\Marine Habitat Vulnerability\\EP2\\EP2 Increase in Turbidity.lyr  x:\\Resource Management\\Climate Vulnerability\\Marine Habitat Vulnerability\\EP2\\EP2 Increase in Water Flow Rate.lyr  x:\\Resource Management\\Climate Vulnerability\\Marine Habitat Vulnerability\\EP2\\EP2 Increase in Wave Exposure.lyr  x:\\Resource Management\\Climate Vulnerability\\Marine Habitat Vulnerability\\EP2\\EP2 Overall Biotope Vulnerability V2.lyr  x:\\Resource Management\\Climate Vulnerability\\Marine Habitat Vulnerability\\EP2\\EP2 Overall Biotope Vulnerability.lyr  x:\\Resource Management\\Climate Vulnerability\\Marine Habitat Vulnerability\\EP2\\EP2 Smothering.lyr  x:\\Resource Management\\Climate Vulnerability\\Marine Habitat Vulnerability\\EP2\\EP2 Substratum Loss.lyr  x:\\Resource Management\\Climate Vulnerability\\Marine Habitat Vulnerability\\EP3\\EP3 Abrasion and Physical Disturbance.lyr  x:\\Resource Management\\Climate Vulnerability\\Marine Habitat Vulnerability\\EP3\\EP3 Decrease in Emergence Regime.lyr  x:\\Resource Management\\Climate Vulnerability\\Marine Habitat Vulnerability\\EP3\\EP3 Decrease in Suspended Sediment.lyr  x:\\Resource Management\\Climate Vulnerability\\Marine Habitat Vulnerability\\EP3\\EP3 Decrease in Turbidity.lyr  x:\\Resource Management\\Climate Vulnerability\\Marine Habitat Vulnera\tPaul Brazier\t\t\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T11:14:10.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPrivate record\n18814\tNRW_DS123644\t2024-05-28T12:56:21.917Z\t5\tUnassessed\tEditable\tMarine Licence Disposal Sites\t© CNC/NRW Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and NRW\u0027s copyright. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose. Attribution statement: Contains Natural Resources Wales information © Natural Resources Wales and Database Right. All rights Reserved.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313233363434\tX:\\Licensing and Permitting\\Marine\\Marine Licence disposal sites WGS84.lyr\tJoseph Thomas\tHistoric and current designated sites for disposal of dredge material at sea.\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)\t2025-10-14\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-10-14T08:09:43.000Z\tAndrew Williams\t-\tPrivate record\n18823\tNRW_DS123773\t2024-05-28T12:56:22.175Z\t3\tUnassessed\tEditable\tIntertidal Biotope Map\t© CNC/NRW Data may only be re-used externally under provision and in line with the terms of a NRW licence following an assessment of the data.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313233373733\t\tInternal Custodian: Kirsten Ramsay, Team Leader, Marine \u0026amp; Coastal Ecosystems Team\t\t\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T09:07:28.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPrivate record\n18809\tNRW_DS123857\t2024-05-28T12:56:21.821Z\t783\tValid\tEditable\tGeneral licences - excluded areas where specific licences are required\t© CNC/NRW All rights Reserved. Contains Ordnance Survey Data. Ordnance Survey Licence number AC0000849444. Crown Copyright and Database Right. Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and copyright of the owners. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313233383537\tX:\\Licensing and Permitting\\Areas where bespoke licence required.lyr\tIwan G Hughes, Team Leader, Species and Carbon Permitting, Technical Services and Customer Care\tThis spatial dataset shows the areas which are excluded from General licences 001, 002 and 004 issued on 1st January 2024 by Natural Resources Wales to permit the killing of certain species of wild birds. Individuals wishing to kill wild birds within these areas will need to apply to Natural Resources Wales for a specific licence, using the application form which can be found on the Natural Resources website.\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)\t2024-01-10\tpublication\thttps://datamap.gov.wales/capabilities/layer/568/?ows_service\u003dwms\thttps://datamap.gov.wales/layers/inspire-nrw:NRW_Bespoke_licence_areas\t2025-05-02T14:48:15.000Z\tnobody nobody\tGEMINI\tPublic record\n18807\tNRW_DS123892\t2024-05-28T12:56:21.558Z\t358\tUnassessed\tEditable\tPhase 2 Lowland Peatland Survey of Wales: Species Datasets\t© CNC/NRW  Data may be re-used under provision and in line with the terms of a NRW licence and NRWs guidance on Ecological data exempt from general release.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313233383932\tThis data is now available on the NBN Atlas. This dataset was last updated NBN Gateway (See Resource Locator) on the  17/08/2016 as no more data of this kind is being entered into Recorder 6 this dataset is now classed as static and therefore no longer needs to be updated regularly. This may change if the data gets moved to an NRW centralised system (from legacy CCW).  Update from Kathryn Birch - September 2021 \"2004-2011 species records on NBN Atlas. There is now a lot more species data (2012 to 2021) that needs to go onto NBN Atlas. I haven\u0027t had time to find out how this needs to be done. Probably something to sort out in 2022 when the Peatland survey project ends\".\tInternal Custodian: Kathryn Birch, Specialist Advisor – Terrestrial Habitats \u0026amp; Species, Terrestrial Habitats \u0026amp; Species Team\tThis dataset was part of the Phase 2 Habitats surveys conducted across Wales. It consists of a detailed survey of plant communities in lowland peatland vegetation. The survey was conducted at Phase 2 (plant community) level of herbaceous mire habitats predominantly within the lowland environment of Wales. Key project outputs include site-based assessments of community type, distribution and ecology and evaluative accounts of vegetation and its condition. Strategic outputs include Area of Search/regional/all Wales synthesis and analysis of data to inform site selection, conservation and restoration. This part of the Phase 2 survey includes species datasets collected by Countryside Council for Wales and Natural Resources Wales in-house expert Phase 2 survey team. Peer-based quality assurance is carried out within the team and by CCW\u0027s Peatland Specialist. Regular meetings are held to ensure consistent community and species determination and survey protocol application.\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-03-21T10:35:01.000Z\tnobody nobody\t-\tPublic record\n18810\tNRW_DS123895\t2024-05-28T12:56:21.802Z\t371\tValid\tEditable\tPhase 2 Woodland Survey of Wales: Species Datasets\t© CNC/NRW. NRW does NOT grant permission to third parties to re-use or disseminate the full dataset. A redacted version of the data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and NRW\u0027s copyright. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313233383935\tSpecies data is also stored in Recorder 6 under the Phase 2 Woodland Survey Tag. This data is now available on the NBN Atlas. The species part of the dataset was last updated NBN Gateway (See Resource Locator) on the  17/08/2016 as no more data of this kind is being entered into Recorder 6 this dataset is now classed as static and therefore no longer needs to be updated regularly. This may change if the data gets moved to an NRW centralised system (from legacy system).\tDavid Reed, Specialist Advisor, Terrestrial Habitats - Terrestrial Ecosystems Group\tThis dataset contains species records from detailed Phase 2 survey data from over 800 woodlands of conservation interest in Wales, predominantly Sites of Special Scientific Interest (SSSls) and pSSSI woodlands.   Phase 2 woodland surveys have been carried out periodically since the late 1980s but a concentrated period of survey on SSSI and pSSSI woodland occurred from 1995 and 2000.  Only a redacted version of this data is available under the Open Government Licence and available for public use, see Limitations on Public Access and Use Constraints.\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)\t2020-02-18\tcreation\tnull\thttps://registry.nbnatlas.org/public/show/dp122\t2025-11-25T11:46:33.000Z\tRachel Morris\t-\tPublic record\n18817\tNRW_DS123954\t2024-05-28T12:56:21.745Z\t930\tUnassessed\tEditable\tSands of LIFE (SoLIFE) meteorological data 2017 to 2023 (Morfa Harlech, Merthyr Mawr, Whiteford)\t© CNC/NRW Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and NRW\u0027s copyright. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313233393534\tData is available on DMS here https://cyfoethnaturiolcymru.sharepoint.com/:f:/r/teams/evidence/Marine-Evidence/mcps/Evidence%20%20Data/Wind%20data/Wind%20Data%202017-2023?csf\u003d1\u0026amp;web\u003d1   An NRW Evidence report is in prep (as of May 2023) to describe this dataset, link to be added when available.\tInternal Custodian: Iain Fairley, Specialist Advisor: Marine and Coastal Physical Science, Marine and Coastal Ecosystems\tMeteorological data collected at Morfa Harlech, Merthyr Mawr and Whiteford from February 2017 to February 2023. The data provides wind speed and direction, temperature, rain and pressure at 15 minute intervals.\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)\t2023-02-20\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-12-24T11:23:45.000Z\tMonica Jones\t-\tPublic record\n18806\tNRW_DS123982\t2024-05-28T12:56:21.454Z\t5\tUnassessed\tEditable\tKiEco Freshwater Ecology: Lake Phytoplankton\t© CNC/NRW Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and NRW\u0027s copyright. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose. Attribution statement: Contains Natural Resources Wales information © Natural Resources Wales and Database Right. All rights Reserved.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313233393832\tData Held in KiEco - a PowerBI Report has been created to export this data\tInternal Custodian: Harriet Robinson / Holly Self - Data Services Team.  Internal Custodian: Jennifer Owen, Senior Environmental Assessment Officer, NW Environmental Assessment \u0026amp; Advice Team        Pending finalisation of extract process for NBN / data input into WISKI\tPhytoplankton form the base of many food webs in lakes. This method uses the principle that an increase in nutrients (particularly phosphorus) leads to an increases in phytoplankton biomass and a change in the taxonomic composition, often leading to an increased occurrence of cyanobacteria (blue-green algae.   Only the collection data is held on the KIECO database.\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-03-07T17:24:33.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPrivate record\n18819\tNRW_DS123983\t2024-05-28T12:56:21.928Z\t627\tValid\tEditable\tKiEco Freshwater Ecology: River Macrophytes\t© CNC/NRW Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and NRW\u0027s copyright. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313233393833\tData Held in KiEco - a PowerBI Report has been created to export this data\tAdvisor - Data Services Team.  Graham Rutt  SMEs       Pending finalisation of extract process for NBN / data input into WISKI Data sent to NBN Feb 2020\tMacrophytes (water plants visible to the naked eye) can indicate the impact of pressures such as increased nutrients, flow pressures, channel alterations etc. The species present and their abundance give an indication as to the health of a river. This dataset is made up of species lists and their percentage cover value for each survey conducted across Wales by Natural Resources Wales and former Environment Agency Wales. These surveys are conducted as part of on-going monitoring of river water quality for legislative requirements and to meet business drivers.\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)\t2020-03-09\tpublication\tnull\thttps://registry.nbnatlas.org/public/show/dr2172\t2025-02-04T11:14:08.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n18805\tNRW_DS123984\t2024-05-28T12:56:21.252Z\t3\tUnassessed\tEditable\tKiEco Freshwater Ecology: Incidental Records\t© CNC/NRW Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and NRW\u0027s copyright. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose. Attribution statement: Contains Natural Resources Wales information © Natural Resources Wales and Database Right. All rights Reserved.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313233393834\tData Held in KiEco - a PowerBI Report has been created to export this data\tInternal Custodian: Jennifer Owen, Senior Environmental Assessment Officer, NW Environmental Assessment \u0026amp; Advice Team       Pending finalisation of extract process for NBN / data input into WISKI\tIncidental records are used to record species of importance (may be rare, invasive, of local value) which were not within the confines of the original survey method or were outside the range (spatially) of the original survey.\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-03-07T17:14:26.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPrivate record\n18804\tNRW_DS124099\t2024-05-28T12:56:21.030Z\t2\tUnassessed\tEditable\tRoad verges Designated RVNR\t© CNC/NRW Data may only be re-used externally under provision and in line with the terms of a NRW licence following an assessment of the data.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313234303939\tx:\\Biological\\Road verges Designated RVNR.lyr\tIsobella Griffiths\t\t\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T10:45:11.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPrivate record\n18797\tNRW_DS124101\t2024-05-28T12:56:20.983Z\t189\tUnassessed\tEditable\tForest Research Peat Restoration Climate Suitability (3rd party data)\t© CNC/NRW Data may only be re-used externally under provision and in line with the terms of a NRW licence following an assessment of the data.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313234313031\tx:\\Physical\\Peat\\FR Peat Restoration Climate Suitability.lyr\t\tThe Geospatial Services Team do not currently hold any information for this section. If you are the custodian, please contact the team so we can populate this field.\t\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-10-16T08:35:01.062Z\tRachel Morris\t-\tPublic record\n18800\tNRW_DS124164\t2024-05-28T12:56:21.030Z\t789\tValid\tEditable\tEighteen years of capture-mark-recapture (CMR) data of grey seal pups, Halichoerus grypus, from Pembrokeshire, Wales\t© CNC/NRW, ZSL, WWFS and various third-party recorders NRW owns the copyright of the collation, but the ownership of the records themselves rests with the originators. Data held by NRW may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and NRW\u0027s copyright. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313234313634\tCopies of the 2 spreadsheets, scanned paper files, detailed metadata and copy of the paper submitted (which ws not  accepted for publicatuion in the end) are stored in the DMS https://cyfoethnaturiolcymru.sharepoint.com/teams/evidence/Marine-Evidence/mm/Data Publications  Presentations/Seal Data/Seal Ringing Records Skomer.xlsx?d\u003dw26b1116ca7c44a05a578350158932094    Original paper files were given to presentation to Pembrokeshire Archive on 20/1/23 (by Kate Lock)\tInternal Data Custodian(s): Tom Stringell – electronic data   Metadata Point of Contact:  Tom Stringell       This data accompanies a scientific paper to be published via the Journal of ecology.  Data to be published as part of the paper.  We need to  confirm if the data will be held on the JoE platform or whether we need to put a copy on Lle to link to. All the raw records are third party data but NRW has received permission verbally from a rep of the now obsolete West Wales Field Society Malcolm Cullen.  They have requested the paper data be lodged at the Pembrokeshire Achive and therefore become public information.  detailed metadata (required for the JoE) explains the data futher and is stored in the DMS.\tEighteen years (1954-1972) of capture-mark-recapture data of 245 grey seal pups marked with identification tags in Wales.  The data was obtained from paper files held by NRW and supplied originally West Wales Field Society and includes information on the location and number of animals marked in each year including sex and age estimations.\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)-Zoological Society London (ZSL)\t2019-10-28\tpublication\tnull\thttps://datamap.gov.wales/documents/2611\t2025-11-12T11:52:06.000Z\tRachel Morris\tGEMINI \u0026 MEDIN\tPublic record\n18798\tNRW_DS124197\t2024-05-28T12:56:21.014Z\t4\tUnassessed\tEditable\tEA Environment Management Teams\t© CNC/NRW Data may only be re-used externally under provision and in line with the terms of a NRW licence following an assessment of the data.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313234313937\tx:\\Resource Management\\NRW Operational Areas\\EA Environment Management Teams.lyr\t\tThe Geospatial Services Team do not currently hold any information for this section. If you are the custodian, please contact the team so we can populate this field.\t\t2019-05-23\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T12:59:29.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPrivate record\n18799\tNRW_DS124283\t2024-05-28T12:56:20.997Z\t658\tUnassessed\tEditable\tWater Framework Directive (WFD) Coastal Catchments Cycle 2\t© CNC/NRW All rights Reserved. Contains Ordnance Survey Data. Ordnance Survey Licence number AC0000849444. Crown Copyright and Database Right Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and copyright of the owners. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313234323833\tx:\\EU Directives\\Water Framework Directive\\Cycle2\\WFD Coastal Catchments Cycle 2.lyr\tInternal custodian - Rob Blacklidge - Environment Reporting.\tThe Water Framework Directive (WFD) Coastal Catchments Cycle 2 are a polygon dataset collated and defined for the implementation of the Water Framework Directive. Catchments are defined as an area of land from which all surface run-off flows through a series of streams, rivers and, possibly, lakes to a particular point in the water course such as a river confluence. It is a layer of the undesignated small coastal catchments and is used alongside the Water Framework Directive (WFD) River Waterbody Catchments Cycle 2 dataset to produce outputs showing all the river catchments together.\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)\t2023-04-25\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-12-24T11:20:13.000Z\tMonica Jones\t-\tPublic record\n18802\tNRW_DS124436\t2024-05-28T12:56:20.965Z\t697\tValid\tEditable\tAsh Lichen Alert\t© CNC/NRW and various third-party recorders NRW owns the copyright of the collation, but the ownership of the records themselves rests with the originator. Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and NRW\u0027s copyright. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313234343336\tX:\\Incidents\\Forest Health\\Ash lichens alert.lyr X:\\Incidents\\Forest Health\\Ash lichens alert 1km.lyr\tInternal Custodian: Sam Bosanquet, Specialist Advisor – Terrestrial Ecosystems \u0026amp; Species, Terrestrial Ecosystems \u0026amp; Species Team\tThese data identify 10x10m, 100x100m and 1000x1000m areas where a Threatened Lichen has been recorded on Ash. The dataset is designed to allow land managers to rapidly identify whether they need to consider rare lichens when working with Ash trees, especially if they are considering felling a tree because of Ash Dieback.\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)\t2022-07-29\tpublication\thttps://datamap.gov.wales/capabilities/layergroup/3598/?ows_service\u003dwms\thttps://datamap.gov.wales/layergroups/geonode:nrw_ash_lichen_alerts\t2025-07-18T14:57:38.314Z\tnobody nobody\tGEMINI\tPublic record\n18801\tNRW_DS124618\t2024-05-28T12:56:20.896Z\t2\tUnassessed\tEditable\tNRW Water Quality analytical flow and Quality Control nformation held in LIMS (Laborartory Information Management System)\tTo be added\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313234363138\tLIMS - Swansea Laboratory\tAndrew Wesley, ICT and Data Specialist, Service Delivery\tTo be added when supplied from Data Custodian  Scheduling, collection analysis and reporting of all routine monitoring and pollution response samples.  This includes scheduling and analysis of NRW sample as well as a commercial service for third parties (e.g. Utility companies and Environmental Agencies).  The Results of the Water Quality samples are exported to WISKI (see metadata entry NRW_DS119251)\t\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T10:52:37.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPrivate record\n18803\tNRW_DS124625\t2024-05-28T12:56:20.914Z\t1\tUnassessed\tEditable\tArachnids (spiders \u0026amp; harvestmen) data for Morfa Harlech National Nature Reserve (NNR) 2017-2019\tTO BE UPDATED © CNC/NRW Data may only be re-used externally under provision and in line with the terms of a NRW licence following an assessment of the data.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313234363235\tRecorder 6?\tMike Howe       Waiting for Mike Howe to provide information about the dataset\tMorfa Harlech NNR is a large sand dune system on the west coast of North Wales. In order to improve knowledge of the arachnid fauna of the NNR, four survey visits were made to the reserve in 2017, 2018 and 2019. Arachnids were surveyed from 28 different sample points across the site to gain a broad insight into the fauna. Sampling was largely undertaken using vacuum samplers (G-vac 2-stroke and E-vac Lithium-ion battery powered machines), with hand searching employed in areas with more mobile sand.\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T10:52:30.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPrivate record\n18796\tNRW_DS124626\t2024-05-28T12:56:20.671Z\t1\tUnassessed\tEditable\tNRW North Flood Incident Duty Officer Areas\t© CNC/NRW Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and NRW\u0027s copyright. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose. Attribution statement: Contains Natural Resources Wales information © Natural Resources Wales and Database Right. All rights Reserved.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313234363236\tX:\\Resource Management\\NRW Operational Areas\\NRW North Flood Incident Duty Officer Areas.lyr\tEirian Gilford, Warning \u0026amp; Informing Team Leader, NRW Gwyn Moseley, Warning \u0026amp; Informing Advisor 2, NRW\tAreas covered by the various Flood Incident Duty Officers, with regards to flood incident management and operational response.\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)\t2020-08-14\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-03-07T15:59:01.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPrivate record\n18846\tNRW_DS124627\t2024-05-28T12:56:51.072Z\t0\tUnassessed\tEditable\tNRW North Flood Warning Duty Officer Areas\t© CNC/NRW Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and NRW\u0027s copyright. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose. Attribution statement: Contains Natural Resources Wales information © Natural Resources Wales and Database Right. All rights Reserved.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313234363237\tX:\\Resource Management\\NRW Operational Areas\\NRW North Flood Warning Duty Officer Areas.lyr\tEirian Gilford, Warning \u0026amp; Informing Team Leader, NRW Gwyn Moseley, Warning \u0026amp; Informing Advisor 2, NRW\tAreas covered by the various Flood Warning Duty Officers, with regards to flood monitoring, forecasting and dissemination of alerts/warnings\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)\t2020-08-14\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-03-07T15:59:00.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPrivate record\n18848\tNRW_DS124629\t2024-05-28T12:56:51.071Z\t300\tUnassessed\tEditable\tAculeate Hymenoptera and Diptera assemblages at Dyfi National Nature Reserve – Ynyslas Dunes in 2019\t© CNC/NRW Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and NRW\u0027s copyright. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose. Attribution statement: Contains Natural Resources Wales information © Natural Resources Wales and Database Right. All rights Reserved.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313234363239\tWelsh Invertebrate Database - Recorder 6\tMike Howe       Mike Howe to supply full metadata\tA survey of the aculeate bees \u0026amp; wasps and flies (Diptera) of Ynyslas Dunes was undertaken in 2019 in an attempt to determine the current condition of this site for these taxonomic groups. A total of 57 aculeate species was recorded, 17 of which were to the dunes resulting in a cumulative total of 119 species now known from the site. Only 40 of the 102 previously-recorded aculeates were refound in 2019. 22 of the 38 aculeate species identified as part of the Ynyslas Dunes dune invertebrate assemblage (currently consisting of 141 invertebrate species) were recorded duringthe current survey, and four recognized dune-dependent species were added to the site list. Lasioglossum xanthopus was recorded from a 2nd Welsh locality and Osmia bicolor was recorded new to VC46, both representing significant range expansions\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)\t2019-11-30\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-12-24T11:28:11.000Z\tMonica Jones\t-\tPublic record\n18847\tNRW_DS124635\t2024-05-28T12:56:51.186Z\t683\tUnassessed\tEditable\tAculeate Hymenoptera and Diptera assemblages at Morfa Dyffryn NNR and Morfa Harlech NNR, 2018 and 2019\t© CNC/NRW Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and copyright of the owners. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313234363335\tRecorder 6 - Welsh Invertebrate Database\tDr Mike Howe, Lead specialist advisor; terrestrial habitats and species        Mike Howe to Supply full metadata\tA survey of the aculeate bees \u0026amp; wasps and flies (Diptera) of Morfa Dyffryn and Morfa Harlech dunes was undertaken in 2018 and 2019 in an attempt to determine the current condition of the two sites for these taxonomic groups.    At Morfa Dyffryn, 51 aculeate Hymenoptera species were recorded during the survey including one European IUCN Vulnerable bee Colletes fodiens, two Nationally Rarewasps, one Nationally Rare bee, three Nationally Scarce wasps and two Nationally Scarce bees. 32 aculeate Hymenoptera species of the Welsh sand dune invertebrate assemblage were recorded, but seven previously-recorded species were not found.  Three aculeate Hymenoptera species new to the site list of sand dune assemblage species were recorded, including the Nationally Scarce spider wasp Arachnospila wesmaeli. 110 Diptera (true-flies) species were recorded, including 32 recognised as part of the sand dune invertebrate assemblage. Nine dune-dependent fly species were added to the site list, and nine Nationally Scarce flies were recorded of which two were new to Morfa Dyffryn. The overall totals for dune-dependent aculeate Hymenoptera and Diptera now stand at 39 and 44 species respectively.    At Morfa Harlech, 57 aculeate Hymenoptera species were recorded during the survey including one European IUCN Vulnerable bee Colletes fodiens, one Nationally Rare wasp, one Nationally Rare bee, four Nationally Scarce wasps and three Nationally Scarce bees. 29 aculeate Hymenoptera species of the Welsh sand dune invertebrate assemblage were recorded, but ten previously-recorded species were not found. One Nationally Scarce species recognized as part of the dune  assemblage was recorded new to the site list. 128 Diptera (true-flies) species were recorded (including two species recorded in 2017), including 28 recognised as part of the sand dune invertebrate assemblage. Eight dune-dependent fly species were added to the site list, including Six Nationally Scarce and one “Data Deficient” fly.  The overall totals for dune-dependent aculeate Hymenoptera and Diptera now  stand at 38 and 41 species respectively.\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)\t2019-12-01\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2026-01-09T10:07:26.000Z\tMonica Jones\t-\tPublic record\n18854\tNRW_DS124649\t2024-05-28T12:56:51.285Z\t584\tUnassessed\tEditable\tPen y Cymoedd Windfarm 33 kV Cables\t© CNC/NRW Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and NRW\u0027s copyright. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose. Attribution statement: Contains Natural Resources Wales information © Natural Resources Wales and Database Right. All rights Reserved.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313234363439\tX:\\Utilities\\Renewables\\Pen y Cymoedd Windfarm\\33KV Cables.lyr\tInternal Data Custodian: Dafydd Davies Project Support Officer, Energy Delivery  Metadata Point of Contact: Geospatial Team\tThis dataset shows the Pen y Cymoedd windfarm 33 kV cables. 33kV cables are internal electric cabling come from the wind turbine power systems. They terminate at the sub-station on site. This is the final true data received from the developer (Vattenfall) signifying the end of the construction phase.\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)\t2019-10-29\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T12:00:07.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n18853\tNRW_DS124650\t2024-05-28T12:56:51.273Z\t223\tUnassessed\tEditable\tPen y Cymoedd Windfarm Access Roads\t© CNC/NRW Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and NRW\u0027s copyright. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose. Attribution statement: Contains Natural Resources Wales information © Natural Resources Wales and Database Right. All rights Reserved.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313234363530\tX:\\Utilities\\Renewables\\Pen y Cymoedd Windfarm\\Access Roads.lyr\tInternal Data Custodian: Dafydd Davies Project Support Officer, Energy Deliivery  Metadata Point of Contact: Geospatial Team\tThis dataset shows Pen y Cymoedd Access Roads. The access roads shows forest roads owned and maintained by NRW on the Welsh Government Woodland Estate. This is the final true data received from the developer (Vattenfall) signifying the end of the construction phase.\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)\t2019-10-29\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T11:56:01.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n18839\tNRW_DS124651\t2024-05-28T12:56:50.988Z\t287\tUnassessed\tEditable\tPen y Cymoedd Windfarm Demised Areas\t© CNC/NRW Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and NRW\u0027s copyright. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose. Attribution statement: Contains Natural Resources Wales information © Natural Resources Wales and Database Right. All rights Reserved.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313234363531\tX:\\Utilities\\Renewables\\Pen y Cymoedd Windfarm\\Demised Areas.lyr\tInternal Data Custodian: Dafydd Davies Project Support Officer, Energy Deliivery  Metadata Point of Contact: Geospatial Team\tThis dataset shows Pen y Cymoedd Demised Areas. Demised areas are areas of land ownership that have been transferred by lease over to the leaseholder (Vatenfall), this includes turbine spur roads, substation, turbine bases etc. Vattenfall are therefore fully responsible for the demised areas, this includes maintaining, repairing and granting access to or across these areas. No works can take place in these areas without full consent from Vattenfall. This is the final true data received from the developer (Vattenfall) signifying the end of the construction phase.\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)\t2019-10-29\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-07-08T09:13:58.000Z\tnobody nobody\t-\tPublic record\n18844\tNRW_DS124652\t2024-05-28T12:56:51.185Z\t341\tUnassessed\tEditable\tPen y Cymoedd Windfarm Export Cable\t© CNC/NRW Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and NRW\u0027s copyright. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose. Attribution statement: Contains Natural Resources Wales information © Natural Resources Wales and Database Right. All rights Reserved.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313234363532\tX:\\Utilities\\Renewables\\Pen y Cymoedd Windfarm\\Export Cable.lyr\tInternal Data Custodian: Dafydd Davies Project Support Officer, Energy Deliivery  Metadata Point of Contact: Geospatial Team\tThis dataset shows the Pen y Cymoedd Export Cable (132 kV).  Export cables relate to the 132Kv cable that leaves the Substation once it has been transformed from 33kV. This then runs down to the sub-station in Rhigos where it connects to the National Grid. This is the final true data received from the developer (Vattenfall) signifying the end of the construction phase.\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)\t2019-10-29\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T11:49:19.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n18849\tNRW_DS124653\t2024-05-28T12:56:51.171Z\t298\tUnassessed\tEditable\tPen y Cymoedd Windfarm Low Voltage Cables\t© CNC/NRW Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and NRW\u0027s copyright. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose. Attribution statement: Contains Natural Resources Wales information © Natural Resources Wales and Database Right. All rights Reserved.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313234363533\tX:\\Utilities\\Renewables\\Pen y Cymoedd Windfarm\\Low Voltage Cables.lyr\tInternal Data Custodian: Dafydd Davies Project Support Officer, Energy Deliivery  Metadata Point of Contact: Geospatial Team\tThis dataset shows Pen y Cymoedd Live Cables.  This is the final true data received from the developer (Vattenfall) signifying the end of the construction phase.\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)\t2019-10-29\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T11:55:59.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n18841\tNRW_DS124654\t2024-05-28T12:56:51.048Z\t924\tUnassessed\tEditable\tPen y Cymoedd Windfarm Spur Roads\t© CNC/NRW Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and NRW\u0027s copyright. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose. Attribution statement: Contains Natural Resources Wales information © Natural Resources Wales and Database Right. All rights Reserved.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313234363534\tX:\\Utilities\\Renewables\\Pen y Cymoedd Windfarm\\Spur Roads.lyr\tInternal Data Custodian: Dafydd Davies Project Support Officer, Energy Deliivery  Metadata Point of Contact: Geospatial Team\tThis dataset shows Pen y Cymoedd Spur Roads. Spur roads are all roads that are used to access the wind turbine power systems. These roads tend to divert from the original forest road system and in places they enter the demised areas. This is the final true data received from the developer (Vattenfall) signifying the end of the construction phase.\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)\t2019-10-29\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-07-08T09:13:58.000Z\tnobody nobody\t-\tPublic record\n18840\tNRW_DS124655\t2024-05-28T12:56:51.017Z\t510\tUnassessed\tEditable\tPen y Cymoedd Windfarm Substation\t© CNC/NRW Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and NRW\u0027s copyright. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose. Attribution statement: Contains Natural Resources Wales information © Natural Resources Wales and Database Right. All rights Reserved.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313234363535\tX:\\Utilities\\Renewables\\Pen y Cymoedd Windfarm\\Substation.lyr\tInternal Data Custodian: Dafydd Davies Project Support Officer, Energy Deliivery  Metadata Point of Contact: Geospatial Team\tThis dataset shows Pen y Cymoedd Windfarm Substation Location. The location of the on-site substation. This is where transformers change the 33kV input from the wind turbines to a 132kV rating for use in the National Grid. This the final true data received from the developer (Vattenfall) signifying the end of the construction phase.\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)\t2019-12-29\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T11:55:58.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n18845\tNRW_DS124656\t2024-05-28T12:56:51.186Z\t901\tUnassessed\tEditable\tPen y Cymoedd Windfarm Turbines\t© CNC/NRW Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and NRW\u0027s copyright. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose. Attribution statement: Contains Natural Resources Wales information © Natural Resources Wales and Database Right. All rights Reserved.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313234363536\tX:\\Utilities\\Renewables\\Pen y Cymoedd Windfarm\\Turbines.lyr\tInternal Data Custodian: Dafydd Davies Project Support Officer, Energy Deliivery  Metadata Point of Contact: Geospatial Team\tThis dataset shows Pen y Cymoedd Windfarm (as built) wind turbine locations. This shows all 76 turbines on the Pen y Cymoedd Windfarm. Each turbine is 2MW in power. This is the final true data received from the developer (Vattenfall) signifying the end of the construction phase.\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)\t2019-10-29\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-07-08T09:13:58.000Z\tnobody nobody\t-\tPublic record\n18851\tNRW_DS124658\t2024-05-28T12:56:51.147Z\t340\tUnassessed\tEditable\tPen y Cymoedd Windfarm Permanent Masts\t© CNC/NRW Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and NRW\u0027s copyright. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose. Attribution statement: Contains Natural Resources Wales information © Natural Resources Wales and Database Right. All rights Reserved.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313234363538\tX:\\Utilities\\Renewables\\Pen y Cymoedd Windfarm\\Permanent Masts.lyr\tInternal Data Custodian: Dafydd Davies Project Support Officer, Energy Delivery  Metadata Point of Contact: Geospatial Team\tThis dataset shows Pen y Cymoedd Windfarm (as built) Permanent Mast locations. A measurement tower or met mast is a free standing tower or a removed mast, which carries measuring instruments with meteorological instruments such as thermometers and instruments to measure wind speed. This is the final true data received from the developer (Vattenfall) signifying the end of the construction phase.\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)\t2019-10-29\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T11:56:36.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n18855\tNRW_DS124659\t2024-05-28T12:56:51.307Z\t316\tUnassessed\tEditable\tPen y Cymoedd Windfarm Main Access\t© CNC/NRW Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and NRW\u0027s copyright. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose. Attribution statement: Contains Natural Resources Wales information © Natural Resources Wales and Database Right. All rights Reserved.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313234363539\tX:\\Utilities\\Renewables\\Pen y Cymoedd Windfarm\\Main Access.lyr\tInternal Data Custodian: Dafydd Davies Project Support Officer, Energy Delivery  Metadata Point of Contact: Geospatial Team\tThis dataset shows the Pen y Cymoedd Windfarm Main Access. The Main Access shows the agreed access route used by Vattenfall and their contractors/visitors to get to the Vattenfall control centre (the HWB). The control centre is in the vicinity of the substation.  This is the final true data received from the developer (Vattenfall) signifying the end of the construction phase.\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)\t2019-10-29\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T12:00:45.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n18838\tNRW_DS124661\t2024-05-28T12:56:50.844Z\t277\tUnassessed\tEditable\tPen y Cymoedd Windfarm Site Boundary\t© CNC/NRW Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and NRW\u0027s copyright. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose. Attribution statement: Contains Natural Resources Wales information © Natural Resources Wales and Database Right. All rights Reserved.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313234363631\tX:\\Utilities\\Renewables\\Pen y Cymoedd Windfarm\\Site Boundary.lyr\tInternal Data Custodian: Dafydd Davies Project Support Officer, Energy Delivery  Metadata Point of Contact: Geospatial Team\tThis shapefile shows Pen y Cymoedd Windfarm Construction Site Boundary. The boundary that was granted by the Local Planning Authority and was used as the Construction Design Management (CDM) area. These are the final true shapefiles received from the developer (Vattenfall) signifying the end of the construction phase.\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)\t2019-10-29\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-07-08T09:14:01.000Z\tnobody nobody\t-\tPublic record\n18843\tNRW_DS124663\t2024-05-28T12:56:51.053Z\t1550\tValid\tEditable\tRemaining Landfill Void in Wales\t© CNC/NRW Data may be re-used under provision and in line with the terms of a NRW licence.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313234363633\tOriginal data is held in Documents and collated into CRM (PALS) and provided as an csv export.  Extraction is undertaken annually and placed in Citrix ShareFile.\tJohn Fry Lead Specialist Advisor, Waste Policy\tPermitted landfill operators have a condition in their permits to report the remaining landfill void (capacity) of their sites at the end of the calendar year. This information although used for compliance purposes is also used by the EC, Government, Local Authorities and other interested parties for statutory reporting and waste planning purposes. Data is provided in cubic metres and collated into a national dataset.  There are only around 20 operational landfills in Wales. Operators can claim commercial confidentiality for their data at time of submission. To date, no operator has claimed commercial confidentiality.\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)\t2024-12-06\tpublication\tnull\thttps://datamap.gov.wales/documents/3249\t2025-12-19T12:08:49.251Z\tMonica Jones\tGEMINI\tPublic record\n18852\tNRW_DS124667\t2024-05-28T12:56:51.171Z\t262\tUnassessed\tEditable\tBrechfa Forest West Windfarm - Armoured Crossing Points\t© CNC/NRW Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and NRW\u0027s copyright. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose. Attribution statement: Contains Natural Resources Wales information © Natural Resources Wales and Database Right. All rights Reserved.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313234363637\tX:\\Utilities\\Renewables\\Brechfa Forest West Windfarm\\Armoured Crossing Points.lyr\tInternal Data Custodian: Dafydd Davies Project Support Officer, Energy Delivery  Metadata Point of Contact: Geospatial Team\tThis shapefile shows Brechfa Forest West windfarm Armoured Crossing Points. These are the final true shapefiles received from the developer (Innogy) signifying the end of the construction phase.\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)\t2019-12-31\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-07-08T09:13:59.000Z\tnobody nobody\t-\tPublic record\n18850\tNRW_DS124668\t2024-05-28T12:56:51.186Z\t294\tUnassessed\tEditable\tBrechfa Forest West Windfarm - Blade Pad\t© CNC/NRW Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and NRW\u0027s copyright. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose. Attribution statement: Contains Natural Resources Wales information © Natural Resources Wales and Database Right. All rights Reserved.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313234363638\tX:\\Utilities\\Renewables\\Brechfa Forest West Windfarm\\Blade Pad.lyr\tInternal Data Custodian: Dafydd Davies Project Support Officer, Energy Delivery  Metadata Point of Contact: Geospatial Team\tThis shapefile shows Brechfa Forest West windfarm Blade Pad. These are the final true shapefiles received from the developer (Innogy) signifying the end of the construction phase.\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)\t2019-12-31\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-07-08T09:13:57.000Z\tnobody nobody\t-\tPublic record\n18837\tNRW_DS124669\t2024-05-28T12:56:50.842Z\t867\tUnassessed\tEditable\tBrechfa Forest West Windfarm - Bridges\t© CNC/NRW Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and NRW\u0027s copyright. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose. Attribution statement: Contains Natural Resources Wales information © Natural Resources Wales and Database Right. All rights Reserved.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313234363639\tX:\\Utilities\\Renewables\\Brechfa Forest West Windfarm\\Bridges.lyr\tInternal Data Custodian: Dafydd Davies Project Support Officer, Energy Delivery  Metadata Point of Contact: Geospatial Team\tThis shapefile shows Brechfa Forest West windfarm Bridges. These are the final true shapefiles received from the developer (Innogy) signifying the end of the construction phase.\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)\t2019-12-31\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-07-08T09:13:57.000Z\tnobody nobody\t-\tPublic record\n18836\tNRW_DS124670\t2024-05-28T12:56:50.647Z\t327\tUnassessed\tEditable\tBrechfa Forest West Windfarm - Armoured Crossing Point Markers\t© CNC/NRW Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and NRW\u0027s copyright. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose. Attribution statement: Contains Natural Resources Wales information © Natural Resources Wales and Database Right. All rights Reserved.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313234363730\tX:\\Utilities\\Renewables\\Brechfa Forest West Windfarm\\Armoured Crossing Point Markers.lyr\tInternal Data Custodian: Dafydd Davies Project Support Officer, Energy Delivery  Metadata Point of Contact: Geospatial Team\tThis shapefile shows Brechfa Forest West windfarm Armoured Crossing Point Markers. These are the final true shapefiles received from the developer (Innogy) signifying the end of the construction phase.\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)\t2019-12-31\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-07-08T09:13:58.000Z\tnobody nobody\t-\tPublic record\n18842\tNRW_DS124671\t2024-05-28T12:56:51.072Z\t389\tUnassessed\tEditable\tBrechfa Forest West Windfarm - Crane Pad\t© CNC/NRW Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and NRW\u0027s copyright. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose. Attribution statement: Contains Natural Resources Wales information © Natural Resources Wales and Database Right. All rights Reserved.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313234363731\tX:\\Utilities\\Renewables\\Brechfa Forest West Windfarm\\Crane Pad.lyr\tInternal Data Custodian: Dafydd Davies Project Support Officer, Energy Delivery  Metadata Point of Contact: Geospatial Team\tThis shapefile shows Brechfa Forest West windfarm Crane Pad. These are the final true shapefiles received from the developer (Innogy) signifying the end of the construction phase.\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)\t2019-12-31\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-07-08T09:13:59.000Z\tnobody nobody\t-\tPublic record\n18831\tNRW_DS124672\t2024-05-28T12:56:50.296Z\t337\tUnassessed\tEditable\tBrechfa Forest West Windfarm - Culverts\t© CNC/NRW Data may be re-used under the terms of the Open Government Licence providing it is done so, acknowledging both the source and NRW\u0027s copyright. It is the recipient\u0027s responsibility to ensure the data is fit for the intended purpose. Attribution statement: Contains Natural Resources Wales information © Natural Resources Wales and Database Right. All rights Reserved.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313234363732\tX:\\Utilities\\Renewabl