r\\Freshwater Fish Cleddau Sites.lyr       x:\\Biological\\Species sourced by NRW\\Freshwater\\Freshwater Fish Lamprey West.lyr      x:\\Biological\\Species sourced by NRW\\Freshwater\\Freshwater Fish Teifi Sites.lyr          x:\\Biological\\Species sourced by NRW\\Freshwater\\Freshwater Fish Tywi Sites.lyr        x:\\Biological\\Species sourced by NRW\\Freshwater\\Freshwater Fish West Cleddau Sites.lyr\tTristan Hatton-Ellis, Lead Specialist Advisor, Freshwater Habitats and Species, Marine \u0026amp; Freshwater Ecosystems Group\t\t\t2015-11-18\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T10:30:46.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPrivate record\n18627\tNRW_DS123225\t2024-05-28T12:53:17.226Z\t0\tUnassessed\tEditable\tMalltraeth cockle survey\t\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313233323235\t\t\t\tx:\\Biological\\Species sourced by NRW\\Marine\\WG_Malltraeth_cockle_survey\\All Stations WGS84.lyr  x:\\Biological\\Species sourced by NRW\\Marine\\WG_Malltraeth_cockle_survey\\District Low Water Marks.lyr  x:\\Biological\\Species sourced by NRW\\Marine\\WG_Malltraeth_cockle_survey\\Most Accurate District Coastline.lyr\t\t\t\t2015-11-18\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T12:36:39.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPrivate record\n18636\tNRW_DS123226\t2024-05-28T12:53:17.621Z\t1\tUnassessed\tEditable\tGreat crested newt habitat suitability\t\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313233323236\t\t\t\tx:\\Biological\\Species sourced by NRW\\Terrestrial\\Amphibians\\Great crested newt habitat suitability (EQSS).lyr  x:\\Biological\\Species sourced by NRW\\Terrestrial\\Amphibians\\Great crested newt habitat suitability.lyr\tJonathan Rothwell\t\t\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T10:38:43.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPrivate record\n18619\tNRW_DS123227\t2024-05-28T12:53:16.737Z\t5\tUnassessed\tEditable\tNatterjack font\t\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313233323237\t\t\t\tx:\\Biological\\Species sourced by NRW\\Terrestrial\\Amphibians\\Natter_Jack_font_point.lyr\tLiz Halliwell\t\t\t2015-06-01\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T10:22:45.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPrivate record\n18624\tNRW_DS123228\t2024-05-28T12:53:16.953Z\t2\tUnassessed\tEditable\tInvertebrates South\t\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313233323238\t\t\t\tx:\\Biological\\Species sourced by NRW\\Terrestrial\\Invertebrates\\Invertebrates South points.lyr  x:\\Biological\\Species sourced by NRW\\Terrestrial\\Invertebrates\\Invertebrates South rectangle.lyr\tJonathan Rothwell\t\t\t2015-11-18\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T10:22:44.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPrivate record\n18621\tNRW_DS123234\t2024-05-28T12:53:16.582Z\t12\tValid\tEditable\tDrinking Water Protected Areas Lakes and River catchments 2021\t\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313233323334\tAny waterbodies in Wales that are used to provide drinking water are designated as drinking water protected areas (DrWPAs). The designation aims to protect the water and prevent any deterioration in quality that could increase the required treatment of water to meet Drinking Water Standards. Drinking Water Protected Areas are required to be identified under the Water Environment (Water Framework Directive) (England and Wales) Regulations 2017.\tThe designation may be based around any abstractions  that meets the qualifying criteria.\t\tx:\\Designations\\NRW Non-Statutory\\NRW Drinking Water Protected Areas Lakes.lyr  x:\\Designations\\NRW Non-Statutory\\NRW Drinking Water Protected Areas River Catchments.lyr\tSuzanne Lawn, Specialist Advisor WQ\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)\t\t2027-03-31\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-03-07T15:58:55.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPrivate record\n18623\tNRW_DS123236\t2024-05-28T12:53:16.953Z\t1\tUnassessed\tEditable\tNRW Valleys Regional Park\t\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313233323336\t\t\t\tx:\\Designations\\NRW Non-Statutory\\NRW Valleys Regional Park.lyr\tPeter Cloke\t\t\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T10:30:27.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPrivate record\n18622\tNRW_DS123237\t2024-05-28T12:53:16.851Z\t5\tUnassessed\tEditable\tDrinking Water Safeguard Zones 2020\t\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313233323337\tAny waterbodies in Wales that are used to provide drinking water are designated as drinking water protected areas (DrWPAs). The designation aims to protect the water and prevent any deterioration in quality that could increase the required treatment of water to meet Drinking Water Standards. Drinking Water Protected Areas are required to be identified under the Water Environment (Water Framework Directive) (England and Wales) Regulations 2017. Within these drinking water protected areas we work with water companies to identify raw water sources that are ‘at risk’ of deterioration which would result in the need for additional treatment. These areas are degsinated as Safeguard Zones where additional measures can be used to address any factors that may reduce the water quality. The SgZ have been identified based on DCWW monitoring and risk assessments and are not limited to the DWPA but based on the wider Water Company identified catchment areas.  A catchment is the term used to describe the area of land where water drains or collects. After rain, water flows over the land, through soil and rock, into streams and eventually the main river. The boundary of a catchment follows natural slopes, hills or mountains within a landscape and determines if water flows into one river or another or subsequently into a reservoir.\tThe boundaries in the dataset are reviewed annually and are subject to change. Contact water.source@dwrcymru.com for updated copy of dataset.\t\tX:\\Designations\\NRW Non-Statutory\\Drinking Water Safeguard Zones 2020.lyr\tSuzanne Lawn Suzanne.Lawn@cyfoethnaturiolcymru.gov.uk\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)-Dwr Cymru Welsh Water\t\t2025-03-31\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-03-07T15:52:24.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPrivate record\n18625\tNRW_DS123239\t2024-05-28T12:53:16.961Z\t3\tUnassessed\tEditable\tNon EC Bathing Waters Classification\t\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313233323339\t\tExtracted from WISKI - KwiQM\tThe same information is also available for EC sites\tX:\\EU Directives\\Bathing Waters Directive\\Non EC Bathing Waters Classification.lyr   Original data is held in WISKI - KwiQM (see metadata entry116227)\tHelena Sykes?\t\t\t2021-11-24\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T10:30:15.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPrivate record\n18626\tNRW_DS123240\t2024-05-28T12:53:17.062Z\t1\tUnassessed\tEditable\tNon EC Bathing Waters Historic Compliance 1988 to 2014\t\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313233323430\t\t\tInformation is also available for EC sites (see NRW_DS100375)\tX:\\EU Directives\\Bathing Waters Directive\\Non EC Bathing Waters Historic Compliance 1988 to 2014.lyr\t\t\t\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T12:36:10.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPrivate record\n18620\tNRW_DS123241\t2024-05-28T12:53:16.554Z\t5\tUnassessed\tEditable\tDangerous Substances Directive\t\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313233323431\t\t\t\tx:\\EU Directives\\Dangerous Substances Directive\\Dangerous Substances Directive.lyr\t\t\t\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T10:30:19.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPrivate record\n18616\tNRW_DS123242\t2024-05-28T12:53:16.427Z\t3\tUnassessed\tEditable\tFisheries Stretches\t\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313233323432\t\t\t\tx:\\EU Directives\\Freshwater Fish Directive\\Fisheries Stretches.lyr\t\t\t\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T10:45:11.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPrivate record\n18618\tNRW_DS123243\t2024-05-28T12:53:16.358Z\t7\tUnassessed\tEditable\tFreshwater Fish Sample Points\t\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313233323433\t\t\t\tx:\\EU Directives\\Freshwater Fish Directive\\Freshwater Fish Sample Points.lyr\t\t\t\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T10:45:11.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPrivate record\n18617\tNRW_DS123244\t2024-05-28T12:53:16.297Z\t1\tUnassessed\tEditable\tNitrates\t\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313233323434\t\t\t\tx:\\EU Directives\\Surface Water Abstraction Directive\\Nitrates.lyr\t\t\t\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T12:32:31.000Z\tAstun Technol