taken if a site visit is required.   This data should only be available for staff who administer the database (currently ICC) and relevant information will be provided to individuals seeking to make site visits.   The Grid Reference for each site is provided to the Geospatial Team for upload to GIS, no other data is provided. This data is also restricted and should not be shared externally.\tInformation is provided by staff who encounter a hostile situation whilst carrying out duties for NRW. This information is then used to determine whether site visits should be made.   Please note, the data should be reviewed annually, however this doesn\u0027t currently happen.  This data should not be shared externally, please see access and use restrictions for further information.\t\tX:\\Incidents\\Hostile sites.lyr  L Drive - Please contact the custodian or ICC Team for access\tSean Moore, Team Leader, Incident Communications Centre, Incident and Emergencies, Flood and Operational Risk Management  Please note that metadata should also be left for internal view only.\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)\tNot Licenced for Re-use\t2025-11-13\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-11-14T09:38:11.403Z\tMonica Jones\t-\tPrivate record\n18646\tNRW_DS123297\t2024-05-28T12:53:50.137Z\t1\tUnassessed\tEditable\tAvian flu seabird colony\t\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313233323937\t\t\t\tx:\\Incidents\\Avian flu contingency\\Avian flu seabird colony text.lyr  x:\\Incidents\\Avian flu contingency\\Avian flu seabird colonys.lyr\t\t\t\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T12:36:59.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPrivate record\n18704\tNRW_DS123298\t2024-05-28T12:54:22.493Z\t0\tUnassessed\tEditable\tAvian flu winter species\t\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313233323938\t\t\t\tx:\\Incidents\\Avian flu contingency\\Avian flu winter species.lyr\t\t\t\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T12:43:34.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPrivate record\n18696\tNRW_DS123299\t2024-05-28T12:54:22.393Z\t11\tUnassessed\tEditable\tAsh DieBack\t\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313233323939\t\t\t\tx:\\Incidents\\Forest Health\\Ash DieBack Monitoring Squares.lyr  x:\\Incidents\\Forest Health\\Ash Dieback Working Target Sites.lyr\tKeith Harri Jones\t\t\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-12-12T14:52:05.000Z\tMonica Jones\t-\tPrivate record\n18705\tNRW_DS123300\t2024-05-28T12:54:22.452Z\t5\tUnassessed\tEditable\tChalara Working Target Sites\t\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313233333030\t\t\t\tx:\\Incidents\\Forest Health\\Chalara Working Target Sites.lyr\tSam Milner\t\t\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T10:45:23.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPrivate record\n18695\tNRW_DS123301\t2024-05-28T12:54:22.228Z\t1\tUnassessed\tEditable\tVaccinnium Dominant Open Habitats\t\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313233333031\t\t\t\tx:\\Incidents\\Forest Health\\Vaccinnium Dominant Open Habitats.lyr\tKeith Harri Jones\t\t\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T10:45:23.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPrivate record\n18689\tNRW_DS123302\t2024-05-28T12:54:22.101Z\t1\tUnassessed\tEditable\tWoodland Types Vaccinnium\t\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313233333032\t\t\t\tx:\\Incidents\\Forest Health\\Woodland Types Vaccinnium.lyr\tKeith Harri Jones\t\t\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T09:59:10.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPrivate record\n18698\tNRW_DS123303\t2024-05-28T12:54:22.397Z\t594\tValid\tEditable\tKiEco Freshwater Ecology: Diatoms\tKiECO Ecoleg Dŵr Croyw Diatomau\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313233333033\tFreshwater diatoms (phytobenthos) are free-living microscopic plants that form a biofilm on submerged substrates such as rock/stone or large plants. They are used as an indicator of water quality because their silica shells are easy to identify under the microscope. This dataset is made up of the relative abundance of different species within the sample from freshwater diatom surveys conducted across Wales by Natural Resources Wales and former Environment Agency Wales. These surveys are conducted as part of on-going monitoring of river water quality for legislative requirements and to meet business drivers.  A geospatial version of this dataset is available to download from DataMapWales. Please see metadata NRW_DS125742 for more information.\tA strict methodology is applied when sampling for freshwater diatoms. There is a core network of sites which are monitored on a three-yearly rolling programme. These sites may be added to for investigative work, or on an ad hoc basis. Sampling areas are located with a larger survey area and must be representative of the overall survey area. A stone scrape method is the most commonly used method for sampling freshwater diatoms. However, where necessary alternative methods are used, for example in areas with no suitable substrate. Natural Resources Wales collect and analyse in excess of 350 diatom samples from rivers and lakes every year. Once samples are collected they are sent to the laboratory for analysis.\t\tData Held in KiEco.  A CSV copy in DarwinCore can be found here - Z:\\Archive\\Knowledge Data \u0026amp; Information Mgmt\\Data Mgmt\\Data Services Data Publishing Area\\NBN Data\\NRW_DS123303_Diatoms\tInternal Custodian:  Advisor 2 - Data Services Team and Jennifer Owen - Senior Environmental Assessment Officer\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)\tOpen Government Licence\t2020-03-09-2025-09-02\tcreation-publication\tnull\thttps://registry.nbnatlas.org/public/show/dp122\t2025-12-01T17:41:00.000Z\tRachel Morris\tGEMINI\tPublic record\n18691\tNRW_DS123304\t2024-05-28T12:54:22.222Z\t6\tUnassessed\tEditable\tHistoric NIRS Incidents (EAW) April 2001 to March 2013\t\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313233333034\t\t\t\tx:\\Incidents\\National Incident Recording System (NIRS)\\Historic NIRS Incidents (EAW) April 2001 to March 2013.lyr\tJohn Farnhill\t\t\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T10:45:14.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPrivate record\n18703\tNRW_DS123305\t2024-05-28T12:54:22.389Z\t6\tUnassessed\tEditable\tNIRS Incidents\t\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313233333035\t\t\t\tx:\\Incidents\\National Incident Recording System (NIRS)\\NIRS Incidents.lyr\tJohn Farnhill\t\t\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-07-09T16:23:09.000Z\tRachel Morris\t-\tPrivate record\n18699\tNRW_DS123306\t2024-05-28T12:54:22.410Z\t1\tUnassessed\tEditable\tOil spill booming plans\t\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313233333036\t\t\t\tx:\\Incidents\\Oil Spills\\Oil spill booming plans.lyr\tAndrew Hill\t\t\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T10:45:14.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPrivate record\n18701\tNRW_DS123307\t2024-05-28T12:54:22.411Z\t1\tUnassessed\tEditable\tOil spill dispersant advice\t\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313233333037\t\t\t\tx:\\Incidents\\Oil Spills\\Oil spill dispersant advice.lyr\tAndrew Hill\t\t\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T10:45:13.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPrivate record\n18692\tNRW_DS123308\t2024-05-28T12:54:22.216Z\t1\tUnassessed\tEditable\tOil spill dispersant\t\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313233333038\t\t\t\tx:\\Incidents\\Oil Spills\\Oil spill dispersant.lyr\tAndrew Hill\t\t\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T10:45:12.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPrivate record\n18702\tNRW_DS123309\t2024-05-28T12:54:22.363Z\t1\tUnassessed\tEditable\tWIRS\t\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313233333039\tSee  metadata entry 117602 This GIS layer is likely to be an extract from the WIRS database\t\t\tx:\\Incidents\\Wales Incident Recording System (WIRS)\\WIRS.lyr\tSean Moore\t\t\t2023-11-15\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T10:45:12.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPrivate record\n18686\tNRW_DS123310\t2024-05-28T12:54:21.985Z\t584\tValid\tEditable\tMetal Mines\tMwyngloddiau Metel\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313233333130\tMetal Mines records locations of disused metal mines in Wales with each being represented by centre point of the site. The dataset is collected to display the locations of metal mines which can be used in conjunction with other datasets to provide a better understanding of the area. They have also been attributed with a \"Failing Water Body\" status (Amber or Red). This identifies mines which are understood to be contributing to failures to achieve good ecological or chemical status in water bodies with High (red) or low (amber) confidence. This attribute was applied in 2020 and only to sites within water bodies identified as failing in the 2018 Water Framework Directive (WFD) Cycle 2 classification.\tThe Metal Mines dataset is sourced from legacy data and reports on metal mines in Wales, originally to support the 2002 Metal Mines Strategy for Wales. Changes have been made to the dataset to remove duplicates and to correct inaccurate grid references for certain mine locations.  The Failing Water Bodies attribute is sourced from the 2020 Failing Water Bodies Report. With amendments to remove duplicates and correct errors.\t\tx:\\Industrial\\Mines\\Metal Mines.lyr\tDave Johnston,\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)\tOpen Government Licence\t2025-07-09\tpublication\thttps://datamap.gov.wales/capabilities/layer/7651/?ows_service\u003dwms\thttps://datamap.gov.wales/layers/geonode:nrw_metal_mines\t2025-12-01T17:41:37.250Z\tRachel Morris\tGEMINI\tPublic record\n18697\tNRW_DS123311\t2024-05-28T12:54:22.268Z\t2\tUnassessed\tEditable\tMine Water Discharges\t\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313233333131\t\t\t\tx:\\Industrial\\Mines\\Mine Water Discharges.lyr\tTrystan James\t\t\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T10:02:21.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPrivate record\n18693\tNRW_DS123312\t2024-05-28T12:54:22.107Z\t5\tUnassessed\tEditable\tMining Impact Non Coal\t\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313233333132\t\t\t\tx:\\Industrial\\Mines\\Mining Impact NonCoal.lyr\tTrystan James, Team Leader, Geoscience, Geoscience/Knowledge Strategy \u0026amp; Planning\t\t\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T10:45:19.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPrivate record\n18700\tNRW_DS123313\t2024-05-28T12:54:22.296Z\t1\tUnassessed\tEditable\tPPC Air Emissions Points\t\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313233333133\t\t\t\tx:\\Industrial\\Pollution and Waste\\PPC Air Emissions Points.lyr\tJulie Boswell\t\t\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T10:02:20.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPrivate record\n18688\tNRW_DS123314\t2024-05-28T12:54:22.104Z\t1\tUnassessed\tEditable\tPPC Installation Boundary\t\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313233333134\t\t\t\tx:\\Industrial\\Pollution and Waste\\PPC Installation Boundary.lyr\tJulie Boswell\t\t\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T10:02:18.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPrivate record\n18685\tNRW_DS123315\t2024-05-28T12:54:21.584Z\t1\tUnassessed\tEditable\tPPC Sewer Emission Points\t\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313233333135\t\t\t\tx:\\Industrial\\Pollution and Waste\\PPC Sewer Emission Points.lyr\tJulie Boswell\t\t\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T10:30:15.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPrivate record\n18690\tNRW_DS123316\t2024-05-28T12:54:22.092Z\t1\tUnassessed\tEditable\tPPC Water Emission Points\t\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313233333136\t\t\t\tx:\\Industrial\\Pollution and Waste\\PPC Water Emission Points.lyr\tJulie Boswell\t\t\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T10:45:08.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPrivate record\n18694\tNRW_DS123317\t2024-05-28T12:54:22.228Z\t2\tUnassessed\tEditable\tRadioactive Sites Non Nuclear\t\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313233333137\t\t\t\tx:\\Industrial\\Pollution and Waste\\Radioactive Sites Non Nuclear.lyr\t\t\t\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T10:45:08.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPrivate record\n18687\tNRW_DS123318\t2024-05-28T12:54:22.128Z\t972\tValid\tEditable\tWater Quality Exemptions\tEsemptiad Ansawdd Dŵr\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313233333138\tThe Environmental Permitting Regulations contains exemptions from needing an environmental permit for certain water discharges and groundwater activities. Exemptions cover the discharge of treated domestic sewage to either surface or groundwater, managing vegetation near/on inland water, substances to ground for scientific purposes and discharges from open loop heating and cooling systems.    These exemptions must be registered with Natural Resources Wales. The Water Quality Exemptions dataset contains the locations for these registered exemptions in Wales.-Mae\u0027r Rheoliadau Trwyddedu Amgylcheddol yn cynnwys esemptiadau rhag bod angen trwydded amgylcheddol ar gyfer rhai gollyngiadau dŵr a gweithgareddau dŵr daear. Mae esemptiadau yn cynnwys gollwng carthion domestig wedi’u trin naill ai i ddŵr wyneb neu ddŵr daear, rheoli llystyfiant ger/ar ddŵr mewndirol, sylweddau i’r ddaear at ddibenion gwyddonol a gollyngiadau o systemau gwresogi ac oeri dolen agored.  Rhaid i\u0027r esemptiadau hyn fod wedi\u0027u cofrestru â Cyfoeth Naturiol Cymru. Mae\u0027r set ddata Eithriadau Ansawdd Dŵr yn cynnwys lleoliadau\u0027r esemptiadau cofrestredig hyn yng Nghymru.  Rhybudd ynghylch Gwybodaeth  Mae rhai cyfeiriadau grid o fewn y set ddata yn anghywir ac wedi\u0027u plotio y tu allan i Gymru – mae\u0027r rhain wrthi\u0027n cael eu cywiro.  Cydnabyddiaeth  Yn cynnwys gwybodaeth Cyfoeth Naturiol Cymru © Cyfoeth Naturiol Cymru a Hawl Cronfa Ddata. Cedwir pob hawl.\tSome grid references within the data set are incorrect and are plotted outside Wales – these are in the process of being corrected.\t\tX:\\Licensing and Permitting\\Water Abstractions \u0026amp; Discharges\\Water quality exemptions.lyr\tInternal Data Custodian(s): Water Quality Policy Team, Natural Resources Wales waterqualitypolicyteam@cyfoethnaturiolcymru.gov.uk\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)\tNRW Conditional\t2026-01-08\tpublication\thttps://datamap.gov.wales/capabilities/layer/2359/?ows_service\u003dwms\thttps://datamap.gov.wales/layers/geonode:nrw_water_quality_exemptions\t2026-01-12T14:41:22.084Z\tRachel Morris\tGEMINI\tPublic record\n18682\tNRW_DS123319\t2024-05-28T12:54:21.538Z\t3\tUnassessed\tEditable\tFelling Licence Applications Pre 1 April 1998\t\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313233333139\t\t\t\tx:\\Licensing and Permitting\\Felling Licences\\Felling Licence Applications Pre 1 April 1998.lyr\t\t\t\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T10:38:07.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPrivate record\n18683\tNRW_DS123324\t2024-05-28T12:54:21.545Z\t0\tUnassessed\tEditable\tProtected Sp