0Z\t0\tUnassessed\tEditable\tNRW Acquisitions \u0026amp; Disposals\t\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313233333635\tThis dataset illustrates the acquisitions \u0026amp; disposals that have created the NRW Managed Forestry Estate as we know it today. This information is obtained from the Deed Management System which has been designed for the maintenance and reporting of the NRW land holdings.\tEstates, Forest Planning, Mapping and Geodata and ESRI (UK) Ltd have developed the Deed Management Extension. It has been designed to: enable the Mapping and Geographic Information Units to interrogate and maintain the NRW land holdings records, provide land ownership data to Estates staff with GIS, produce update polygons to maintain legal boundary information in NRWs \u0027Forester Web\u0027 GIS system. The Deed Management System application is packaged as Web based GIS system powered by ESRI. Spatial information (polygons covering acquisitions and NRW accesses, NRW servitudes). Since the creation of NRW in 2013, NRW have maintained the data in the Forester GIS.\t\tX:\\Ownership\\NRW Land\\NRW Forest Deeds - Acquisitions.lyr  X:\\Ownership\\NRW Land\\NRW Forest Deeds - Disposals.lyr   Acquisition and Disposal Record Map Scans archive held on G:\\FCData\\Aberystwyth\\EstateManagement\\A and D. Record Map Scans to be moved to Z drive.\tPrimary Metadata contact: Ian Medcalf, GIS Technician 4, NRW Secondary Metadata contact: Arpana Chunilal / Geraint Morgan\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)\t\t2023-06-30\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T12:56:12.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPrivate record\n18706\tNRW_DS123366\t2024-05-28T12:54:49.754Z\t2\tUnassessed\tEditable\tNRW properties\t\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313233333636\tThe Geospatial Services Team do not currently hold any information for this section. If you are the custodian, please contact the team so we can populate this field.\tThe Geospatial Services Team do not currently hold any information for this section. If you are the custodian, please contact the team so we can populate this field.\t\tx:\\Ownership\\NRW Properties\\NRW properties.lyr\tIan Medcalf, Technical Support (4) GIS, Estates, North \u0026amp; Mid Wales Operations\t\t\t2020-10-22\tpublication\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T10:45:10.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPrivate record\n18749\tNRW_DS123367\t2024-05-28T12:55:20.596Z\t608\tUnassessed\tEditable\tAll Wales Hydrological Analysis Catchments\t\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313233333637\tThis layer was created to point to rasters used in NRW hydrological analysis tools. They are based upon the flow direction models which were created by the Environment Agency Detailed River Network which subsequently passed to NRW.  The All Wales Hydrological Analysis Catchments is generated for each area above a threshold area from the following related datasets: NRW_DS123368 NRW_DS123369 NRW_DS123370 NRW_DS123371\tCreated as a precursor to the Ordnance Survey Mastermap Water Network. There is a lot of subjectivity in terms to the thresholds used to generate these by-products from the flow direction raster.. It depends on intended use, spatial extent and scale. Changing these variables will alter the number and size of the resulting streams and catchments\t\tx:\\Physical\\Hydrological\\Hydro Tools\\allwales_cat.lyr\tBen Anscombe\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)\t\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-07-08T09:06:50.000Z\tnobody nobody\t-\tPublic record\n18758\tNRW_DS123368\t2024-05-28T12:55:20.709Z\t691\tUnassessed\tEditable\tAll Wales Hydrological Analysis Flow Accumulation Raster\t\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313233333638\tThis layer was created to point to rasters used in NRW hydrological analysis tools. They are based upon the flow direction models which were created by the Environment Agency Detailed River Network which subsequently passed to NRW.    The Flow Accumulation Raster is a count for each cell a count of how many other cells flow to it.\tCreated as a precursor to the Ordnance Survey Mastermap Water Network. There is a lot of subjectivity in terms to the thresholds used to generate these by-products from the flow direction raster. It depends on intended use, spatial extent and scale. Changing these variables will alter the number and size of the resulting streams and catchments\t\tx:\\Physical\\Hydrological\\Hydro Tools\\allwales_fac.lyr\tBen Anscombe\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)\t\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T12:59:10.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n18754\tNRW_DS123369\t2024-05-28T12:55:20.676Z\t308\tUnassessed\tEditable\tAll Wales Hydrological Analysis Flow Direction Raster\t\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313233333639\tThis layer was created to point to rasters used in NRW hydrological analysis tools. They are based upon the flow direction models which were created by the Environment Agency Detailed River Network which subsequently passed to NRW.  For each cell in a raster the All Wales Hydrological Analysis Flow Direction Raster assigns a value indicating which adjacent cell surface water would be expected to flow to.\tCreated as a precursor to the Ordnance Survey Mastermap Water Network. There is a lot of subjectivity in terms to the thresholds used to generate these by-products from the flow direction raster.. It depends on intended use, spatial extent and scale. Changing these variables will alter the number and size of the resulting streams and catchments\t\tx:\\Physical\\Hydrological\\Hydro Tools\\allwales_fdr.lyr\tBen Anscombe\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)\t\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T12:59:10.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n18757\tNRW_DS123370\t2024-05-28T12:55:20.710Z\t326\tUnassessed\tEditable\tAll Wales Hydrological Analysis Stream Link\t\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313233333730\tThis layer was created to point to rasters used in NRW hydrological analysis tools. They are based upon the flow direction models which were created by the Environment Agency Detailed River Network which subsequently passed to NRW.  All Wales Hydrological Analysis Stream Link shows the cells representing the All Wales Hydrological Analysis Stream Network (NRW_DS123371) but aggregated together to indicate discrete dendritic areas.\tCreated as a precursor to the Ordnance Survey Mastermap Water Network. There is a lot of subjectivity in terms to the thresholds used to generate these by-products from the flow direction raster.. It depends on intended use, spatial extent and scale. Changing these variables will alter the number and size of the resulting streams and catchments\t\tx:\\Physical\\Hydrological\\Hydro Tools\\allwales_lnk.lyr\tBen Anscombe\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)\t\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-07-08T09:06:52.000Z\tnobody nobody\t-\tPublic record\n18763\tNRW_DS123371\t2024-05-28T12:55:20.709Z\t620\tUnassessed\tEditable\tAll Wales Hydrological Analysis Stream Network\t\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313233333731\tThis layer was created to point to rasters used in NRW hydrological analysis tools. They are based upon the flow direction models which were created by the Environment Agency Detailed River Network which subsequently passed to NRW.  The All Wales Hydrological Analysis Stream Network is based upon a threshold of the flow accumulation raster (NRW_DS123368)\tCreated as a precursor to the Ordnance Survey Mastermap Water Network. There is a lot of subjectivity in terms to the thresholds used to generate these by-products from the flow direction raster.. It depends on intended use, spatial extent and scale. Changing these variables will alter the number and size of the resulting streams and catchments\t\tx:\\Physical\\Hydrological\\Hydro Tools\\allwales_str.lyr\tBen Anscombe\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)\t\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T12:59:44.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n18748\tNRW_DS123372\t2024-05-28T12:55:20.593Z\t6\tUnassessed\tEditable\tDEM 5m\t\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313233333732\tThe Geospatial Services Team do not currently hold any information for this section. If you are the custodian, please contact the team so we can populate this field.  This is the same data that is held at X:\\Basemapping\\Height\\APGB_5m_DEM.lyr (see URI EXT_DS121661) Speak to Ben Anscombe for further information\tThe Geospatial Services Team do not currently hold any information for this section. If you are the custodian, please contact the team so we can populate this field.\t\tx:\\Physical\\Hydrological\\Hydro Tools\\dem_5m.lyr\tGeospatial Services Team, Knowledge Information Management Group\t\t\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T10:52:38.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPrivate record\n18752\tNRW_DS123373\t2024-05-28T12:55:20.653Z\t12\tUnassessed\tEditable\tTerrain 5m\t\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313233333733\tThis dataset forms part of the Hydrological Tools Datasets  The Geospatial Services Team do not currently hold any further information for this section. If you are the custodian, please contact the team so we can populate this field.\tThe Geospatial Services Team do not currently hold any information for this section. If you are the custodian, please contact the team so we can populate this field.\t\tx:\\Physical\\Hydrological\\Hydro Tools\\Terrain_5m_Terrain.lyr\tGeospatial Team, Knowledge Information Management\t\t\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T10:52:43.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPrivate record\n18762\tNRW_DS123374\t2024-05-28T12:55:20.703Z\t5\tUnassessed\tEditable\tFR Peat Restoration Current Suitability\t\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313233333734\tThe Geospatial Services Team do not currently hold any information for this section. If you are the custodian, please contact the team so we can populate this field.\tThe Geospatial Services Team do not currently hold any information for this section. If you are the custodian, please contact the team so we can populate this field.\t\tx:\\Physical\\Peat\\FR Peat Restoration Current Suitability.lyr\t\t\t\t\t\tnull\tnull\t2025-02-04T10:52:41.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPrivate record\n18765\tNRW_DS123375\t2024-05-28T12:55: